{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:58.532474Z","id":"71ea2f58c4375b918954359520f536cd6395bf0d911a9adb2285c58b3d1fdda8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"job_tx rolls back on every error and answers the refusal as the closure gave it; jobs::tests::a_refusal_after_a_write_rolls_the_write_back (a job_steps insert, then JobError::Conflict, leaves no row; a Moved refusal after an UPDATE leaves the row as it was) failed before the change and passes. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 652f225fcffa)","supersedes":"6958dd4bfc3aca046a4b50e9360d3f54a55332fddb9864b04751f3939c65d269","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:58.639790Z","id":"31a052366ed8bc3cb648a69fc21f2ca1db6ae37bcf0b08c98cd32296f48212b2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"JobState enum (ToSql/FromSql, serde lowercase) replaces STATES and the String fields; jobs::may_move is the one table, obeyed by patch_job, set_job_thread, remove_job_thread, ask_job_question, commit_step and the close of a job's question; spec §8.1 gains the table. jobs::tests::done_and_cancelled_jobs_refuse_every_write, a_patch_never_moves_a_job_to_queued_waiting_or_done, only_a_running_job_that_asks_moves_to_waiting and a_job_resumed_while_its_question_is_open_waits each failed against the old moves and pass. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 652f225fcffa)","supersedes":"95e2323382e4c31c27355b3a5b54e7e41e07cb1dbab8a415d94cfc1d01fe534b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:58.757806Z","id":"3b4720d39d943ac21894b80965d711cbd4165bbd1228ed96729d41b775bd23fa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Migration 46 in place: job_questions.question_id UNIQUE REFERENCES questions(id), outcome CHECKed to answered/declined/withdrawn with answers_json present exactly for an answer; JobQuestion.answer is JobAnswer {Pending, Answered, Declined, Withdrawn}; ask_job_question answers invalid_question for an unknown question or another job's. jobs::tests::a_question_belongs_to_one_job_and_must_exist failed before and passes. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 652f225fcffa)","supersedes":"aea075980cdfbab1c00d5fc35eb0ddd9a1c1a696726dbcdffa1dd9348abb92f9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:58.816521Z","id":"111d9796eebed244be7938c3dfc9fca6803a5bf5aeed762412247762bb7117b5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"close_question stores every ending close (answered, declined, withdrawn) through close_job_question_tx and moves the job by may_move; ask_job_question refuses a hook question (invalid_question). jobs::tests::a_withdrawn_question_moves_the_job_back_with_its_outcome and a_job_asks_only_the_ask_tools_questions failed before and pass. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 652f225fcffa)","supersedes":"0e88da634a1f5e615f65e729d62cc6c8b3ec70bcd97f51ed9d78c906492ae48f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:58.874547Z","id":"4d07d5363287d463e6e18170f53a92f831881230358085410949e8898af0b85a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"ask_job_question refuses a final job (job_moved), reads the question's status in its transaction, stores a closed question's outcome at once and keeps the job's state, and moves only a running job to waiting. jobs::tests::a_question_closed_before_it_is_recorded_is_stored_at_once failed before and passes; done_and_cancelled_jobs_refuse_every_write covers the done job. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 652f225fcffa)","supersedes":"ccd00e63f86c024a4c7b0646e4fab9faaf160e431152be05e63896dc5b1bac22","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:59.215273Z","id":"647d6925f94799eb8b77412bffa5f6ddc8780b0732cf12c99af11f5c18b59ed7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"The write connection's update hook records every written jobs rowid (crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs, beside inbox_items and approval_requests); with_tx reads them before the commit and Store::set_job_listener's listener hears each changed job once after it, never on a rollback. Event::Job itself is Task 21's: its router installs the listener and publishes. jobs::tests::every_committed_job_change_is_heard_once_whatever_made_it (create, patch, ask, then an answer through close_question heard at its new rev, and a rolled-back write unheard) failed without the hook branch and passes. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 652f225fcffa)","supersedes":"d4ba1c8694af7acab90ac10f5af20b1a421a626c7ec2740940401990dbcd4221","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:59.498730Z","id":"9bfd1963400c27a4a2d24df59e76041d5de5aa3ebecbed8ff94079019e4c5a24","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Migration 46 in place: every job-table foreign key, agent_read_consents.reader/source and draft_renders.draft_id ON DELETE CASCADE, with indexes on the child columns; artifact_going_tx (soft delete, purge, zero-version delete, both draft deletes) cancels open jobs with error artifact_deleted and rev + 1, thread_going_tx and artifact_threads_going_tx (thread delete, purge) forget the thread with rev + 1. jobs::tests::a_deleted_artifact_cancels_its_open_jobs_and_a_purge_takes_them, deleting_a_thread_a_job_answers_moves_the_job and deleting_a_draft_or_an_empty_artifact_takes_its_jobs_and_consents failed (FOREIGN KEY constraint failed, or the job left queued) and pass. forks.rs:635 is a test's own DELETE, not a delete path. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 652f225fcffa)","supersedes":"77cd6afa09c12ad26da008eea1ba7cef6612fb3703e61c4a668aced72eee9326","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:59.715124Z","id":"aa7e44a9416db488e5286172a2301abef4039f384231e017271415dc57f043bd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Migration 46 in place and spec §8.1: CHECK (stopped IN (0, 1)), CHECK (clean IN (0, 1)), CHECK (rev >= 1) and json_valid on every _json column (NULL passes where allowed). jobs::tests::the_schema_refuses_values_no_job_can_have failed before and passes. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 652f225fcffa)","supersedes":"06a22f77d3cf6102127e86c7b0edd4dbf5bbaf362b7a47af446b1b4da305c59f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:59.892100Z","id":"64b30d8c8848b7a9923a26c32035334dfd9eefb254a2b645d24007216b6fc58d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"jobs_tables_disagree compares each jobs table's and each of its indexes' sqlite_master SQL, normalised by normalised_sql (comments and spacing), with the in-memory copy, refusing a missing or extra index. migrations::tests::a_database_whose_jobs_tables_disagree_is_refused gains job_threads without its cascades and jobs_open dropped (both failed before, pass), and sql_is_compared_without_its_comments_and_spacing tests the normaliser. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 652f225fcffa)","supersedes":"93e744c464aad06a2570d9aad4ea76dcc70a0ca3e577cc983a85d7ad55b3efd2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:59.964306Z","id":"a750112f6d12a22d29bc78e73a1a127476ccc120bf00b895496c0f152b524f85","body":{"detail":"artifact_going_tx (jobs.rs:987-1024) and patch_job to cancelled (or failed, stopped) move the job but leave its unclosed job_questions question open: the person still sees and may answer a question no worker will read. The close is then stored nowhere (close_job_question_tx returns None for a final job). Withdrawing the job's open questions when it becomes final, in the same transaction (close_question's Close::Withdraw logic factored to run inside a caller's transaction), would end both together.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":987},"end":{"line":1024},"content_hash":"e220c0b4094b41b60e1b35a801dc66c1e69428dab2d99074b977606edc6752d5"},"summary":"Cancelling a job leaves the question it waits on open in the person's inbox","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:59.964533Z","id":"b5d2b6fa2bc784fc54b6c1b62bc9075235c75f6e23c5e0f75af8470325682359","body":{"detail":"Their foreign keys cascade only on a hard delete (a purge, a draft's delete). The soft delete, which is how artifacts are deleted, leaves them until a purge, unlike db_read_grants, net_grants and sample_grants, whose triggers on deleted_at remove them (migrations 41, 43, 44). Nothing reads a consent of a deleted artifact today; a trigger here would also have to be built in adoption's in-memory copy (migrations.rs jobs_tables_disagree), which has no artifacts table.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1329},"end":{"line":1342},"content_hash":"99e101a6350f979603aa5112ae4c5ec49f8a169951c678222e665b71cfab2af0"},"summary":"agent_read_consents and draft_renders rows outlive a soft-deleted artifact","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:36.955189Z","id":"4d77b6109624896e2005540996a3ae89755b8c672e4c18b94bc679c718232dc0","body":{"detail":"Failure: a running job asks question Q of session S (Store::ask_job_question moves it to waiting), then S ends: the reaper (Store::reap_sessions, system:ttl), the person (end_session_by_person) or the agent (end_session). every session end calls withdraw_session_questions (sessions.rs:1675), whose bulk UPDATE (WITHDRAW_SESSION, questions.rs:421) sets Q to withdrawn without close_question, so close_job_question_tx (jobs.rs:940) never runs: job_questions.outcome stays NULL, the job stays waiting, and every later PATCH to running lands in waiting again (may_move with waits = true, jobs.rs:121). Nothing can close Q any more (close_question answers question_closed). This breaks spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §7.4 (waiting: 'a withdrawal stores its outcome and moves the job to running') and §8.1, and the claim of resolve 111d9796 that every ending close is stored.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":518},"end":{"line":536},"content_hash":"d0a4029caadaa4ff18d323d2b748676cd16154f94bbe2f8985f80611273b7402"},"suggested_fix":"In withdraw_session_questions, after WITHDRAW_SESSION, call self.close_job_question_tx(tx, &k.id, &JobAnswer::Withdrawn) for each withdrawn key (its job moves back to running, its outcome stored, its Event::Job heard through the update hook). Test in jobs.rs: running job asks a question of session s, st.end_session(DAEMON, s), the job is running at rev + 1 with JobAnswer::Withdrawn. Check every other bulk UPDATE of questions.status the same way (WITHDRAW_HOOKS only touches source = 'hook', which ask_job_question refuses).","summary":"A session's end withdraws a job's ask question without storing its outcome, so the job waits forever","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:36.955668Z","id":"81029f45e07486eaffe2f5fdb42c1e18b93885dbecb504e7df0102b7586ee559","body":{"detail":"A final job (cancelled or done) never reads an outcome again, so a question left open is one the person can answer for nothing, and its close is then stored nowhere (close_job_question_tx returns None for a final job). The final moves are three: patch_job to cancelled (jobs.rs:698), artifact_going_tx (jobs.rs:987) and commit_step with done (jobs.rs:859; may_move lets a waiting job's last step end it). stopped and failed are not final: Keep going and Retry move them back to running, which lands in waiting while the question is open, so the person's later answer is still used; withdrawing there would lose it. With the fix, no committed row holds a final job with a job_questions row whose outcome is NULL.","kind":"comment","references":"a750112f6d12a22d29bc78e73a1a127476ccc120bf00b895496c0f152b524f85","suggested_fix":"Factor close_question's Close::Withdraw arm (questions.rs CLOSE, record_question with a new Reason such as job_ended, inbox::question_changed) into withdraw_question_in(tx, ctx, qid, reason). Give jobs.rs one helper, ending(tx, job_id) called whenever moving() or may_move yields a state that is_final, that withdraws each SELECT question_id FROM job_questions WHERE job_id = ?1 AND outcome IS NULL through it and sets outcome = 'withdrawn'. patch_job and commit_step use AuditCtx::DAEMON (or gain a ctx), artifact_going_tx its caller's. Tests: cancel a waiting job, its question is withdrawn and its inbox item read; delete its artifact, the same; a done step on a waiting job, the same.","summary":"Yes: every move of a job to a final state should withdraw its unclosed questions in the same transaction; stopped, failed and paused should not","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:36.955936Z","id":"625ab7965401353e3eb52a878e5912851da3e7aa756a950ad7cd101d9eb83cde","body":{"detail":"A soft-deleted artifact is never purged in normal use: delete_corrupt_deleted_rows (artifacts.rs:633) removes only corrupt rows, and there is no undelete, so these rows stay for good, not until a purge. Store::agent_read_consents (jobs.rs:893) lists them with no deleted_at filter, so GET /api/agent-read-consents will show consents naming deleted artifacts. A trigger on artifacts, as migrations 41, 43 and 44 do, cannot be built by adoption's in-memory copy (jobs_tables_disagree executes migration 46 on a database with no artifacts table) and is not compared by it (it reads only tables and indexes). artifact_going_tx already runs inside every delete of an artifact, the soft delete included.","kind":"comment","references":"b5d2b6fa2bc784fc54b6c1b62bc9075235c75f6e23c5e0f75af8470325682359","suggested_fix":"In artifact_going_tx, after cancelling the jobs: DELETE FROM agent_read_consents WHERE reader = ?1 OR source = ?1; DELETE FROM draft_renders WHERE draft_id = ?1. Migration 46 is unchanged. Test: put consents both ways and a render for an artifact, delete_artifact it, agent_read_consents() and draft_renders are empty.","summary":"Remove them at the soft delete, in artifact_going_tx, rather than with a trigger","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:36.956141Z","id":"2c9b54e8f6cc95ba69b9f773b6e4402794564058e5181ebfe832767623df82be","body":{"detail":"jobs_tables_disagree selects sqlite_master rows WHERE tbl_name = ?1 AND type IN ('table', 'index'). A trigger on jobs, job_steps or any other jobs table (an extra one in an earlier database, or one migration 46 later gains and an earlier database lacks) is neither required nor refused, though it changes what writes do. No text of migration 46 has had a trigger so far (git log -p of tests/fixtures/old-migrations/flutter-app-652f225fcffa.sql), so no database is mis-adopted today. The normaliser itself is sound: SQLite keeps the CREATE text verbatim on every version, so an identical schema is never refused, and only spacing next to parentheses and commas, runs of spaces and -- comments are dropped, which cannot merge two tokens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1631},"end":{"line":1636},"content_hash":"1b1bf31d09d8ca14c10140ed104c554ed015c601fe52be0b74976a31813cdb23"},"suggested_fix":"type IN ('table', 'index', 'trigger'), with a case in a_database_whose_jobs_tables_disagree_is_refused that adds a trigger on jobs.","summary":"Adoption's comparison of the jobs tables reads only tables and indexes, so a trigger on them is not seen","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:36.956224Z","id":"7fd10650304ae9bb467d2ceef3f71368911d9fdc14a20eeb196b87f999a1a66f","body":{"detail":"threads_going bumps rev and updated_at of every job with a job_threads row for the thread, final ones included, so a done or cancelled job changes after it ended and its listener hears an Event::Job for it. JobError::Moved's contract (jobs.rs:373) and spec §8.1's table say a final job is changed by no write. Harmless to the worker (it drops rows of jobs it has not loaded) but it breaks the invariant the rest of jobs.rs keeps.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1046},"end":{"line":1061},"content_hash":"1c3b8677de9f3941a2ae34db91b65db08f9c1a1c62e9f88f47cd3a63403a5304"},"suggested_fix":"Add AND state NOT IN ('cancelled', 'done') to the UPDATE; the DELETE of job_threads still takes every row. Test: a done job answering a thread keeps its rev when the thread is deleted.","summary":"A thread's delete moves the rev of cancelled and done jobs, which no write is to change","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:13:09.667588Z","id":"22de7cb210fc9bced02868fc9c3d257491e0d93739afa11eaf65f67c4132274c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed: every close of a question goes through Store::close_in (questions.rs), which calls close_job_question_tx; a session's end and the daemon's start withdraw each question by withdraw_question_in, and the bulk UPDATEs WITHDRAW_SESSION and WITHDRAW_HOOKS are gone. jobs::tests::a_sessions_end_withdraws_its_question_and_moves_the_job_back (end_session and reap_sessions: the job is running at rev + 1 with JobAnswer::Withdrawn) failed before (left: (Waiting, 3), right: (Running, 4)) and passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test, 733 passed, 0 failed.","supersedes":"4d77b6109624896e2005540996a3ae89755b8c672e4c18b94bc679c718232dc0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:13:09.955658Z","id":"a8ced3baa59767d1926815fdf89230164a424cbae759bdf16041e0c4d4004891","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed: patch_job to cancelled, commit_step with done and artifact_going_tx call Store::ending (jobs.rs), which withdraws each job_questions question with outcome NULL by withdraw_question_in (reason job_end, system:daemon) in the same transaction; close_job_question_tx stores the outcome for a final job without moving it. jobs::tests::a_jobs_final_move_withdraws_its_open_questions (each final move empties the owner's open questions, stores Withdrawn, leaves the final row as the move made it; stopped, failed and paused keep the question open) failed before (left: 1, right: 0) and passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test, 733 passed, 0 failed.","supersedes":"a750112f6d12a22d29bc78e73a1a127476ccc120bf00b895496c0f152b524f85","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:13:19.872045Z","id":"9f9bd32798f129c8b1ca2211faa504e3217f86e49c90de3d93888c04b36e35c4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed as reply 625ab796 says: artifact_going_tx (jobs.rs), which every delete of an artifact runs, the soft delete included, deletes agent_read_consents naming the artifact as reader or source and its draft_renders; migration 46 is unchanged. jobs::tests::a_soft_deleted_artifact_takes_its_consents_and_renders (delete_artifact leaves only the consent and render not naming it) failed before and passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test, 733 passed, 0 failed.","supersedes":"b5d2b6fa2bc784fc54b6c1b62bc9075235c75f6e23c5e0f75af8470325682359","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:13:20.146222Z","id":"d8f8f6e42e58ca9b47d54f8ef425c9f06ea3aa328100a2d1a8581b3fc314db29","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed: jobs_tables_disagree (migrations.rs) reads type IN ('table', 'index', 'trigger') and compares each by name, kind and normalised SQL, none missing and none more. The new case in migrations::tests::a_database_whose_jobs_tables_disagree_is_refused (a trigger jobs_touched on jobs) was not refused before and is now, by name, leaving the home as it was: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test, 733 passed, 0 failed.","supersedes":"2c9b54e8f6cc95ba69b9f773b6e4402794564058e5181ebfe832767623df82be","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:13:20.423273Z","id":"b51aa4dab19fcef0c65c43be644d60652b961297d15c4ed8c807409a2cbb1478","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed: threads_going (jobs.rs) bumps rev and updated_at only of jobs not in cancelled or done; the job_threads rows go for every job. jobs::tests::deleting_a_thread_leaves_done_and_cancelled_jobs_as_they_were (the done and cancelled rows unchanged, only the open job heard at rev + 1) failed before (rev 5 against 4) and passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test, 733 passed, 0 failed.","supersedes":"7fd10650304ae9bb467d2ceef3f71368911d9fdc14a20eeb196b87f999a1a66f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:21:49.412681Z","id":"e5598513f049e41a8f1642f32ff285bb74c1f7207cd0bb321a5d926493b6e530","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed in 652f225fcffa: backup::before_migrate_reporting calls its report just before the copy, and Store::open_with passes it the BackingUp report instead of restating the rule. Evidence: backup::tests::backing_up_is_reported_only_for_a_copy_and_before_it_is_made (did not compile before the fix) and tests::opening_a_home_reports_each_migration_and_a_current_one_none pass; bazelisk test --keep_going //crates/clax-embed:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-store:all //scripts:no_unsafe //scripts:no_unsafe_test //scripts:crate_layers at 0a8d4312d97d: 19 tests pass.","supersedes":"bba3aeec4f4a1d03cea7bf1d7b32d439a14a6de69fb3c0cec3d8180481a26cb2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:10:12.309813Z","id":"94b81ad4563a53e265047f3957e248db934b36ea87eb2adc112d46dad6cf8cac","body":{"detail":"Failure: the app is killed after FsContent::write_version renamed the staging directory to versions/<n> (crates/clax-core/src/content/fs.rs place) and before the step's transaction commits. SQLite rolls the transaction back, so no version, no step and no job change remain, but versions/<n> stays on disk with no row. On the next launch the worker commits the same key again; publish_step_cut reaches record_version_locked, whose content write fails in FsContent::check_new with 'version <n> of <id> is already present' (CoreError::Io), so the step answers 500 until `clax doctor` lists and the directory is removed. The tests (jobs::tests::a_step_cut_before_commit_leaves_no_version_and_resumes_once) cut inside the transaction, where the failure path removes the content; they do not cover a real kill.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1313},"end":{"line":1390},"content_hash":"f63c720a7a93f5e536b63227ddc8572b1da55c6826c7ded6e69eac7db1e914bb"},"suggested_fix":"Under the content lock, when the artifact's current_version is n-1 and versions/<n> exists unrecorded, remove it before writing (only this process writes the home while the core holds core.lock), or compare its manifest with the step's and adopt it.","summary":"A process killed between a publish step's content write and its commit leaves a stray version directory that refuses the resumed step","tags":["review","kill-resume","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:10:12.309981Z","id":"550e9e35194ba5105bb547a2b819e8af07bdd8e1b57e1a2bf68d36e983749604","body":{"detail":"PublishStep.draft (DraftRef) is parsed by POST /api/jobs/{id}/steps/{key} (crates/clax-server/src/routes/jobs.rs parse_step) and ignored by commit_publish_step; StepError::NotRenderedClean is never returned. Spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §8.2 refuses a draft's step unless draft_renders holds a clean render of its digest, which needs POST /api/drafts/{id}/renders and clax_core::digest::files_digest.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1137},"end":{"line":1140},"content_hash":"57cf6c7a63b0211553be687046f8eac98352bac1208f4db39660d4503d4cf5a5"},"summary":"A publish step's draft is accepted and not checked: the render gate is not applied yet","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:19:56.892914Z","id":"4ff66d9a49355bb1ff2d67c41f363719e80ea225a8f13fa779d37cca5c0741bd","body":{"detail":"Scope, beyond the root: the stray refuses every later publish of that artifact (a manual one too), not only the resumed step. For a new app the resume succeeds under a fresh ID (publish_step_cut generates one per attempt) and leaves a zero-version row and its versions/1 behind. On the git store the stray is not refused but adopted as a push: see the concern on crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs:724-747.\n\nNot sound: (1) writing to a staging path named by the step key and renaming it into place at the commit. A rename cannot be atomic with SQLite's COMMIT: renaming after the commit leaves, on a kill, a recorded version with no files (served broken), and renaming before it is today's gap. On git the 'rename' is the ref update, with the same window. (2) Adopting a stray whose bytes equal the step's. Equal bytes do not say who wrote them, and on git the push adoption runs before the write is attempted.\n\nSound: write the step's identity with the version's content and let only that step replace it. VersionMeta gains step: Option<String> (job ID and key). Git writes it as a Clax-Step trailer on the version commit (version_commit already writes trailers, lib.rs:332). FsContent writes a sidecar versions/<n>.step before place() renames staging to versions/<n>, and remove_version removes the directory, then the sidecar. A new ContentStore::unrecorded_step(id, n) -> Option<String> reads the mark. In record_version_locked (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:1413), under the content lock and after the row check finds current_version == expected: when n is present and its mark equals this write's step, remove_version(n) and write again. `made` stays true, so the failure path's removal keeps its invariant that this call made n. pushed_commits leaves a commit carrying Clax-Step to its step.\n\nWhy it is sound: only the same (job, key) matches the mark. A key commits once (replay). In one process the owner claim and the content lock serialize the writers, core.lock (crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs opening) keeps out a second core, and an older daemon's writes never carry a mark. Records dc11e4cd and 4f959f4e explain why removing an unmarked unrecorded n is unsafe with several writers; the mark removes that ambiguity.\n\nTest: a jobs.rs unit test that writes version n's content through the content store with the step's mark, as a kill leaves it, then commits the step: one version, not replayed, and a second commit replayed. The same test runs over MemGitContent.","kind":"comment","references":"94b81ad4563a53e265047f3957e248db934b36ea87eb2adc112d46dad6cf8cac","summary":"A fix sound for both content stores: mark each version write with its step, and let only that step replace an unrecorded version carrying its mark","tags":["review","kill-resume","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:19:56.893152Z","id":"d2630639c8575fa2f3d1968b5f4a3cb642ef9cb7e4cd03e2f48571ec068a8c5e","body":{"detail":"Two commits of one key on a change (base b, existing artifact) can overlap. Examples: a worker retrying after the call timed out at status 0 (commit f1c07f346b12) while the first call still runs in the core, or a new owner's resume racing the old owner's in-flight write (record 091f185d). Both calls pass replay() before either commits. The first commits version b+1 and the step. The second, under the content lock, fails record_version_locked's base check (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:1437-1441 or its in-transaction twin) before `then` runs, so cutting is None and this arm answers StepError::VersionMoved { current: b+1 }. It should replay the step the first call recorded. A worker that re-plans on version_moved publishes the change a second time. A new app does not have this problem: its second call's insert_step finds the key (Cut::Replayed) and rolls back.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1376},"end":{"line":1388},"content_hash":"b5078a0acf9c5854db5e56c4c022aa8b95b1ef7618a002bae3ac0d957e3e0953"},"suggested_fix":"In publish_step_cut, on any error with cutting None, call self.replay(id, key) again and answer the recorded step when the key has landed; only otherwise map Conflict to VersionMoved. Test: hold the first call inside the content store (the Gated store in crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs tests), commit the same key from a second call once the first is past replay(), and assert that the second call is replayed with the first call's version.","summary":"A publish step's key committed by a concurrent call answers version_moved, not replayed, on an existing artifact","tags":["review","kill-resume","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:19:56.893526Z","id":"0afd804b7b12827525b1a22ef59e3e79024eb43ab39803f0d1c3ccf28827829d","body":{"detail":"commit_reply_step requires s.session_id to name a live session. The core's reaper ends a local session unseen for Store::SESSION_IDLE_SECS (300 s) whose process is unknown (crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs:1205-1250; crates/clax-server/src/core.rs:15). That ending also releases the session's feedback. So when the app is killed after a change's publish step and relaunched more than five minutes later, the reply step names an ended session and is refused 400 unknown_session on every retry. Spec §18 Review Focus 1 expects one version and one reply after resume. Spec §7.4's resume table (`running`, a `publish:<b>` step, a change -> Reply) does not say which session a resumed reply is made from.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1410},"end":{"line":1419},"content_hash":"4667d35a6d83e15fe1cd3caa0d8aa11376104db69f2804973438f93cda287755"},"suggested_fix":"Either keep a session alive while an open job names it (the reaper's stale query skips sessions an open job names, which needs the job to record its session), or have the resumed worker open a new session and the reply step take it, with the feedback it answers retargeted; the choice changes spec §7.4 and §8.1.","summary":"A change resumed after its agent session was reaped cannot commit its reply step: 400 unknown_session on every retry","tags":["review","kill-resume","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:19:56.894055Z","id":"fa6ff1137cd6a61e30a3e4f4c6b9cd1dfea88b19e2973a51c9b5b44437a28e20","body":{"detail":"Task 23 (plan lines 1286-1306) changes crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs so that commit_publish_step refuses NotRenderedClean unless draft_renders holds a clean row for draft.digest and the request's files hash to that digest (clax_core::digest::files_digest). It adds POST /api/drafts/{id}/renders and not_rendered_clean to docs/contract.md, with the tests a_draft_publish_needs_a_clean_render_of_its_digest and a_publish_without_a_draft_has_no_render_gate. Until Task 23 lands, docs/contract.md's Jobs section correctly leaves not_rendered_clean out.","kind":"comment","references":"550e9e35194ba5105bb547a2b819e8af07bdd8e1b57e1a2bf68d36e983749604","summary":"Confirmed: Task 23 of docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md applies the gate here","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:00:10.983082Z","id":"e8d9e52c92c609e4b599f3d2d2268bde500c1bff69ee77b580f9cc91adf7c69f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed: a publish step marks its version content with its step (VersionMeta.step, clax_store::jobs::step_mark; versions/<n>.step on the home's files, a Clax-Step trailer in git) and record_version_locked removes and rewrites an unrecorded n carrying the writing step's own mark (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs, the unrecorded_step check). Test passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-content-git:integration (steps::a_killed_step_resumes_once_on_files, steps::a_stray_no_step_marked_is_not_replaced_on_files, steps::a_stray_another_step_marked_is_not_replaced_on_files); before the fix the resume failed with 'version 2 of <id> is already present'.","supersedes":"94b81ad4563a53e265047f3957e248db934b36ea87eb2adc112d46dad6cf8cac","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:00:12.441101Z","id":"7c5ace7a0cb4f1a1a5e455a9726a8be375b054f3642cedcccf69bac68cb6ad0d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed: publish_step_cut calls replay(id, key) again on any error with no cut before mapping Conflict to VersionMoved. Test passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test (jobs::tests::a_key_committed_by_an_overlapping_call_is_replayed_not_moved, two overlapping commits of one key over the Gated content store); before the fix the second call answered VersionMoved { current: 2 }.","supersedes":"d2630639c8575fa2f3d1968b5f4a3cb642ef9cb7e4cd03e2f48571ec068a8c5e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:00:14.319757Z","id":"bb5440b869c9d97bedf5fd772d365da73dad40790e1b73647c470040ed577347","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0afd804b7b12827525b1a22ef59e3e79024eb43ab39803f0d1c3ccf28827829d","summary":"Decided by the owner (2026-10-19): keep a session alive while an open job names it; the reaper skips sessions an open (non-final) job references. Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md §8.1 says so.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:00:14.320221Z","id":"c9871e654ab95a258326463bb6c737709e9b81e506c3b95bc5ddaeeea679ac17","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed as decided: reap_sessions and its in-transaction re-check (end_in with a cutoff) skip every session that published a version one of an open job's steps recorded (OPEN_JOB_SESSIONS, crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs); a question's asker is not kept, so its end still withdraws the question (jobs::tests::a_sessions_end_withdraws_its_question_and_moves_the_job_back). Test passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test (jobs::tests::a_session_an_open_job_names_outlives_the_reaper_until_the_job_ends, a relaunch after SESSION_IDLE_SECS + 60 s on a ManualClock; the reply step commits); before the fix the session was reaped.","supersedes":"0afd804b7b12827525b1a22ef59e3e79024eb43ab39803f0d1c3ccf28827829d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:00:15.875301Z","id":"0d42049f19e76569faed7e5b877f59ef32ff028c519000e481078ad801c5d251","body":{"detail":"record_version_locked replaces an unrecorded version n only when its mark (ContentStore::unrecorded_step) equals the writing publish's own step mark. A process killed after a publish step wrote n, followed by the job's cancellation (or any end without that step), leaves n marked by a step that never commits again: on the home's files every later write of n is refused (FsContent::check_new, 500 until clax doctor lists and the directory is removed), and on git pushed_commits skips the tagged Clax-Step commit, so write_version is refused as present. Removing n is also safe when the mark names a step whose job is final (it can never commit, and the content lock and core.lock exclude another writer), which would let any publish replace it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1443},"end":{"line":1452},"content_hash":"8f8dad2d9f84fd5cba360de26a68875e61f2ba7ec5d5303bf8a7f0ab8553dc26"},"summary":"An unrecorded version marked by a step that can no longer commit (its job cancelled or done) blocks every later publish of the artifact","tags":["kill-resume","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:07:20.174967Z","id":"e4a3a8b71779d75e4dfaabb99d23973d267ffe614b2c71584e404f746c536818","body":{"detail":"bazelisk test //crates/clax-embed:old_homes: the_installed_flutter_app_home_backs_up_and_is_adopted and the_perf_home_opens_through_the_core pass. The first asserts 'backing up' as the first phase, one backups/clax-43-*.db at user_version 43 holding the old rows, user_version JOBS_MIGRATION (46) = MIGRATIONS.len(), every row of every table unchanged (EXCEPT against a pristine load of the dump), both artifacts listed by GET /api/artifacts with their versions and threads, and a second open that backs up and migrates nothing. The second grows the same home to 302 artifacts, 2,402 threads and 7,204 comments at schema 43 first. With the fixture's user_version changed to 44 both fail on the store's refusal ('lacks the table jobs'). The fixture's schema came from a cp and sqlite3 .backup copy of the container home; it holds artifacts' columns in the order draft_of, hidden, person (an earlier adoption's), which the 652f225fcffa replay does not give. Its rows were written by clax at 652f225fcffa on a scratch home, none of the owner's. Still open: the phone's home, which no test or copy has opened.","kind":"comment","references":"a12d81ff2ea90885dd2f7ef01f3158e2439a188a76c31a575578ce567fedc53a","summary":"The embedded core's open of a schema-43 home is now tested: crates/clax-embed/tests/old_homes.rs (0a8d4312d97d) opens crates/clax-embed/tests/fixtures/homes/flutter-app-43.sql, whose schema is the macOS app's own clax-home, through Embed and checks the backup, the adoption to 46 and every row","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:08:37.180877Z","id":"2cb3adf8dcb5089f0185e849c1c36170024dd7ff5c48b153c4081c7a5a8e9b25","body":{"detail":"In record_version_locked (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:1443-1452), under the content lock and with the artifact at expected, read unrecorded_step(id, n) for every write, Write and Adopt alike, and decide in the store. A mark equal to this step's own: remove n and write again (as now). A mark naming a step that can never commit (no such job, the job cancelled or done, or the key already committed): remove n, whoever writes, since no writer can ever claim it and the content lock and core.lock exclude any other. Any other mark (a live step that has not committed): leave it, and the write is refused as now. The second branch fixes this record whichever way the job ended: a cancel, a final step, a delete, a kill during the ending, or a job row a reset removed. Doing it in the ending instead (ending() removing the strays its steps marked) runs in the final move's transaction without the content lock, and misses an ending a kill interrupts. In git this needs the two records just above it on crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs:757-768: a stray with commits above it is a push, not a stray to remove (remove_version would refuse, or would discard a push from main); and an unforgeable mark, so a dead-mark removal can never delete a pushed commit that forged one. clax doctor should list a marked stray with its job and whether it is live. Test: kill after a step's content write, cancel the job, then publish over the API, on files and on git.","kind":"comment","references":"0d42049f19e76569faed7e5b877f59ef32ff028c519000e481078ad801c5d251","summary":"Proposed fix: clear a dead mark lazily at the one place that writes n, rather than in the job's ending","tags":["kill-resume","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:08:37.181082Z","id":"3fb6069523e34ca8a379686142fc8c281cc6e79775eac07a80bb06af5e240e3b","body":{"detail":"Failure: in the app, a job asks a question (PUT /api/jobs/{id}/questions/{qid}, job waiting); the app is killed; the app is relaunched more than five minutes later, before the person answers. reap_sessions ends the asking session (local, pid dead, unseen for SESSION_IDLE_SECS), its end withdraws the question, and the job moves to running, so the person never sees the question again. By the §7.4 table (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md:891-942), next() then answers the ask call with the outcome withdrawn. Nothing asks again unless the model chooses to, so the spec's own sentence at line 1176 ('which asks again') does not follow from §7.4. The owner's decision bb5440b8 on crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs is that the reaper skips sessions an open job references. A waiting job references its question's asker (job_questions to questions.session_id), and OPEN_JOB_SESSIONS keeps only sessions that published a version a step recorded. Fix: add to OPEN_JOB_SESSIONS 'UNION SELECT q.session_id FROM job_questions jq JOIN jobs j ON j.id = jq.job_id JOIN questions q ON q.id = jq.question_id WHERE j.state NOT IN (cancelled, done) AND jq.outcome IS NULL', correct spec line 1176, and add a test beside jobs::tests::a_session_an_open_job_names_outlives_the_reaper_until_the_job_ends in which the question survives the relaunch and an answer moves the job to running. The same gap holds for a running job with no publish step yet, whose step names a session_id the reaper ends: the step is then refused unknown_session (publishing_session), which is harmless only if the worker registers a fresh session on relaunch. The spec should say which.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":213},"end":{"line":223},"content_hash":"266a75e68c4216955272ae00cb4cbd5791a7c1cbee3f38ffdaa5ff94e0d271d9"},"summary":"A waiting job's question is withdrawn when the app is relaunched more than SESSION_IDLE_SECS after a kill, because OPEN_JOB_SESSIONS leaves out the question's asker","tags":["reaper","jobs","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:08:37.181188Z","id":"b6a134904b9f8c0cd826a3dab5338c0bdbda4fa1d64bd6edc7cfc899bd64ba6e","body":{"detail":"publish_step_cut makes aid = ArtifactId::generate() whenever artifact_id is None. A process killed after create_artifact_then_async wrote version 1's content, and before the transaction, leaves that content (a versions/1 directory on the home's files, a whole repository with v1 tagged in git) under an ID no row names. The resume generates another ID, and the step commits once with no stray to block it. The orphan is never removed, and the mark check in record_version_locked never sees it. Fix: derive the new app's ID from the step (store it on the job row before the content write, or derive it from step_mark), so the resume finds its own marked version 1 and replaces it as it does for an existing artifact. Or have clax doctor and the startup sweep remove marked content under an ID no row names.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1348},"end":{"line":1348},"content_hash":"9691f69bb8ac3dc0cffb85efcb7522a0828b960a6b93592c8d63658a0f567d6b"},"summary":"A new app's publish step generates a fresh artifact ID per call, so a killed first attempt's content is orphaned rather than replaced","tags":["kill-resume","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:13:44.507453Z","id":"cf898ce84a4b8541cb3c81a4b862f9e3a51c75044a3dd142f0e9a0e0d6b9cc8f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed in 652f225fcffa and 652f225fcffa: OPEN_JOB_SESSIONS (crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs) also names the asker of each unclosed question of an open job and the session of each publish step that began and has not committed (job_step_marks.session_id); spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §7.4 and §8.1 no longer say the job asks again, and state which session each resumed step names so a relaunched worker is never refused unknown_session. Tests jobs::tests::a_waiting_jobs_question_outlives_the_reaper_until_it_closes (ManualClock past SESSION_IDLE_SECS + 60 s: the question stays open, its answer moves the job to running) and jobs::tests::a_begun_publish_steps_session_outlives_the_reaper_until_it_commits fail before the fix (the asker, the session, reaped) and pass after. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all //crates/clax-content-git:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-core:all: all PASSED; //crates/clax-server:integration__1 --test_arg=api_jobs:: --runs_per_test=10: 10 of 10 passed (16 tests each).","supersedes":"3fb6069523e34ca8a379686142fc8c281cc6e79775eac07a80bb06af5e240e3b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:13:44.789406Z","id":"6bd5f0a052b485cd3590a2dd6baf54b5de42dc5cf9d81e53c5a2d1242c208b48","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed in 652f225fcffa: a new app's ID is minted with the step's mark and kept in job_step_marks, so every attempt writes the same artifact; create_artifact_then_async replaces a zero-version row of that ID. Tests steps::a_killed_new_apps_step_resumes_as_one_artifact_on_files and _in_git (the resume writes the killed attempt's ID and replaces its version 1) fail before (another ID) and pass; jobs::tests::a_new_apps_step_resumed_over_its_killed_attempts_row_makes_one_artifact covers the zero-version row a kill leaves. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all //crates/clax-content-git:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-core:all: all PASSED; //crates/clax-server:integration__1 --test_arg=api_jobs:: --runs_per_test=10: 10 of 10 passed (16 tests each).","supersedes":"b6a134904b9f8c0cd826a3dab5338c0bdbda4fa1d64bd6edc7cfc899bd64ba6e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:13:44.845310Z","id":"8e84b6f2d229971465c1301acf198cfd4e06fc2968c8a145f53364faaaa81e49","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed in 652f225fcffa as reply 2cb3adf8 proposed: record_version_locked asks the store about an unrecorded n's mark on every write: its own is replaced, a dead one (no job, job cancelled or done, key committed) is removed whoever writes and its row forgotten, a live one refuses the write. clax doctor lists marked strays with job, key and liveness (Store::marked_strays). Tests steps::a_cancelled_steps_stray_is_removed_by_the_next_write_{on_files,in_git} and a_done_jobs_stray_..._{on_files,in_git} fail before ('version 2 ... is already present') and pass; a_live_steps_stray_refuses_another_write_{on_files,in_git} pass. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all //crates/clax-content-git:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-core:all: all PASSED; //crates/clax-server:integration__1 --test_arg=api_jobs:: --runs_per_test=10: 10 of 10 passed (16 tests each).","supersedes":"0d42049f19e76569faed7e5b877f59ef32ff028c519000e481078ad801c5d251","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:40:49.160194Z","id":"12475f7b271acc4604b2b57d69373862a682d462abc7231cb06eb3db709e2dec","body":{"detail":"Commits 652f225fcffa to 652f225fcffa's parent made migration 46 without job_step_marks; 652f225fcffa to 652f225fcffa's parent added it as 47; 652f225fcffa folded it into 46. A home a build between 652f225fcffa and 652f225fcffa opened is at 46 in this numbering, with the jobs tables and without job_step_marks. adopt_earlier_flutter_app returns early for this numbering's homes, and migrate_steps (crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:789) returns at once when user_version equals the last migration, so jobs_tables_disagree never sees it: the store opens it, and the first query of job_step_marks (crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs, sessions.rs OPEN_JOB_SESSIONS) fails with 'no such table'. A home at 47 (652f225fcffa onwards) is refused as SchemaNewer. Only agents' dev homes can hold either shape (installed homes are at 43), and AGENTS.md has a branch's dev homes reset, not upgraded. The adoption refusal of the same shape at an earlier numbering is tested by migrations::tests::a_database_whose_jobs_tables_disagree_is_refused (the job_step_marks case).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1415},"end":{"line":1427},"content_hash":"6e555db55e362b5f1eb493f4b4968ef75aff8c02dcbc155e598e8421d29cbb92"},"suggested_fix":"Reset such a dev home (move its clax.db aside). If it should be refused instead, compare the jobs tables on every open of a home whose version is JOBS_MIGRATION or above, at the cost of an in-memory database per open.","summary":"A home of this numbering at 46 without job_step_marks opens without error and fails at its first publish step","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:48:34.779038Z","id":"5baa6f6b29c8b47ddefaef2b42d9d29b16308f9defe34c2b6deb788ca75266cf","body":{"detail":"The nonce is secret only until a step's stray is readable: a stray v<n> is main's head (crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs unrecorded_step), so anyone who can fetch the repository reads its Clax-Step trailer. The MarkOf::Own branch here removes the stray and the resumed attempt rewrites v<n> under the same nonce (begin_publish_step, crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs:1475-1524, reuses a held nonce when artifact and version agree). Sequence: (1) step publish:1 of job j writes stray v2 with nonce N and is killed; (2) a collaborator fetches main and reads N; (3) the resume removes the stray (MarkOf::Own) and is killed before its write, leaving main at v1 and the row (N, j, publish:1, aid, 2); (4) the collaborator pushes P on v1 whose message carries the trailer 'Clax-Step: [\"j\",\"publish:1\",\"N\"]'; (5) a reconcile tags P v2 (tag_pushed runs before the version's transaction, artifacts.rs:1541) and is killed before the row; (6) the next reconcile lists P as marked, is_step_mark finds N held for (aid, 2), and pops it (crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs:139-148); (7) the step's next resume finds P's mark Own and remove_version moves main back past P. The same holds for a dead row whose stray was removed by Own before its job ended (MarkOf::Dead removes P at the next write). It needs two kills in narrow windows and a collaborator with push rights, so it is not a merge blocker, but it is a push removed by a forged mark, which the content module's Ordering (crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs) says cannot happen.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1452},"end":{"line":1472},"content_hash":"80245ae5a9757dc40210fb435e7f456dfb111664d21828e87c850cbf69bc0bf0"},"suggested_fix":"Retire a nonce once content carrying it is removed: in the Own branch, after remove_version succeeds, give the step a fresh nonce (update job_step_marks and the request's step mark) before writing. Remove first, then rotate: rotating first and being killed before the remove would leave the stray Foreign. Add a steps.rs case that tags a copied-mark push at the step's version after its stray was removed and checks it is recorded as a push.","summary":"A step's nonce stays valid after the content that exposed it is removed, so a copied mark on a pushed commit can be taken for the step's stray and removed","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:48:34.779278Z","id":"e51f822314239cb4281879c6b6a028d2be8e0541dbde9baece7bd3573347f9c3","body":{"detail":"Failure: step publish:1 (base 1) writes stray v2 under nonce N0 and is killed; an attempt of the same key with another base (say 0, or another artifact_id) re-mints: the ON CONFLICT (job_id, key) update replaces N0 with N1 for (aid, 1), and record_version_locked answers Conflict before it looks at v2 (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:1447-1451); the next attempt with base 1 mints N2 for (aid, 2). The stray's N0 is no longer held, so mark_of answers Foreign: the step and every other writer of v2 are refused as present, Store::marked_strays leaves it out (it lists held rows only), and in git clax doctor's stray_version_dirs does not see it either. Begin runs before the if_version check, so a single bad attempt is enough. The app sends one base per key today, so this needs a client that changes a step's base or artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1475},"end":{"line":1524},"content_hash":"03adbca9c3ba3f049228a173e84879815a55123ea77899b14f2c8bd11ab79044"},"suggested_fix":"Re-mint only after the held (artifact, version) carries no unrecorded content with the held mark: when it does, remove that content under the content lock first (it is the step's own and the step no longer writes there), or refuse the attempt with version_moved before minting. Alternatively mint after the if_version check.","summary":"begin_publish_step re-mints a step's nonce when an attempt names another base or artifact, which leaves the step's unrecorded stray Foreign and refuses every later write of that version","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:48:34.781363Z","id":"4b3802db55ec5f9ba6abe3726e11fbfe70a4299273dc5da7b119ef73dca245df","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"12475f7b271acc4604b2b57d69373862a682d462abc7231cb06eb3db709e2dec","summary":"Reviewed with the fold in 652f225fcffa: acceptable as recorded. Only builds from 652f225fcffa to 652f225fcffa's parent (all 2026-10-20, unmerged) write a 46 without job_step_marks, and AGENTS.md has a branch's dev homes migrated by its earlier builds reset, not upgraded. Every adoption path of the installed and earlier numberings reaches 46 with job_step_marks and every row: migrations::tests::the_frozen_app_migrations_are_this_numberings (fixture flutter-app-652f225fcffa.sql equals MIGRATIONS[45]), a_database_with_the_jobs_tables_at_another_version_is_adopted, a_database_whose_jobs_tables_disagree_is_refused (the job_step_marks case) and the old_homes test pass: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all //crates/clax-embed:old_homes, all PASSED.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:48:28.409814Z","id":"d8c142faf4c68f5a4229fab383e85e820b3ca7dc0429a77cb153a9e2379474f7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"A step's own stray is removed and then the step's nonce renewed (Store::clear_stray_locked, renew_step_mark), and the write carries the store's current mark (held_step_mark). Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-content-git:integration --test_arg=a_mark_copied_from_a_removed_stray_is_a_push failed before the change (the step committed v2 over the push) and passes after; the whole integration target passes at 652f225fcffa.","supersedes":"5baa6f6b29c8b47ddefaef2b42d9d29b16308f9defe34c2b6deb788ca75266cf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:48:28.554737Z","id":"0cb00a76f528731ef5665bc87611a6de31d42a34237e8abea8bbfee3b02c228a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Before begin_publish_step re-mints, Store::remove_moved_stray removes, under the held artifact's content lock, an unrecorded version still carrying the step's held mark (MarkOf::Own). Evidence: steps::a_step_on_another_base_removes_its_stray_on_files and _in_git (crates/clax-content-git/tests/steps.rs) failed before (the stray stayed) and pass after: bazelisk test //crates/clax-content-git:integration PASSED.","supersedes":"e51f822314239cb4281879c6b6a028d2be8e0541dbde9baece7bd3573347f9c3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:48:35.575082Z","id":"bbd0c773353cc18150e6bc302313a14eca19a39c811d15fc2662afcf5ceb7f04","body":{"detail":"When a push that was not a fast forward moves main off a step's unrecorded version v<n> onto a commit P on v<n-1>, P can take n only once the stray's tag is gone. Store::clear_stray_locked (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs) removes it at the next write of n (the step's resume, or anyone's write once the step is dead), but record_pushes_locked alone does not clear it, so a reconcile triggered by a push fails in tag_pushed with present until such a write. Needs a host that allows non-fast-forward pushes (the core's own server denies them by default: deny_non_fast_forwards).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":139},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"c35862a55d72184f01d1309e8a785df7e370ad4fbd452dd74e916c31a58943ae"},"suggested_fix":"Call clear_stray_locked(id, current + 1, None) at the start of record_pushes_locked for a dead step's stray.","summary":"A reconcile with no write after it never records a push beside a stray step version","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:09:09.166956Z","id":"262407ec9da14fdc206bdf40401c363cfd861af89c8b241e52c3f1378776d46f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"The render gate is applied: publish_step_cut refuses a step whose draft has no clean draft_renders row for its digest, or whose version's files (the request's and those carried from base, clax_core::digest::manifest_digest) do not have that digest, with StepError::NotRenderedClean (409 not_rendered_clean); POST /api/drafts/{id}/renders records renders. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__1 --test_arg=api_jobs PASSED, including api_jobs::a_draft_publish_needs_a_clean_render_of_its_digest and a_publish_without_a_draft_has_no_render_gate; //crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test and //apps/clax_app:bundle_files_digest_test PASSED with the same vector.","supersedes":"550e9e35194ba5105bb547a2b819e8af07bdd8e1b57e1a2bf68d36e983749604","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:09:09.398270Z","id":"aae0642789c6d62e06b6ac3d5bf8348c93c6e585ed7856e79d6138fb857e6b31","body":{"detail":"record_render stores any well-formed digest for any draft, so a client holding the token and not the owner's agents (the route refuses those) can record a clean render of files it never rendered. The gate then holds only as far as the app reports truthfully. Comparing the digest with the draft's current version (clax_core::digest::manifest_digest of its files) would tie a render to content the core holds, but a draft is published version by version while the app renders, so the digest may name a version the draft has since moved past.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":430},"end":{"line":446},"content_hash":"f9bc71b76fcbab8e6c00b3dda25d7be4b6e40a733d2e06630875f8abde374335"},"suggested_fix":"Accept a render only when some version of the draft has that digest (versions.files_json), and answer 409 otherwise.","summary":"A recorded render is the app's word: the core does not check that the digest is of the draft's files","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:09:09.398798Z","id":"4a954d6b450716d342932ff6986191ea078303f4109185884cc3c9051ff466ef","body":{"detail":"Spec §9 makes a stopped make job of every plans.json entry that no pending make claims. plans.json keeps the plan of every app built since, finished ones included (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/plan.dart PlanStore), so that would put a Keep going row in the queue for every finished build. The import makes one only while a feature is todo or doing.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":450},"end":{"line":452},"content_hash":"d764f559a2fae8f0174c4b236ea86cb57d1344812d64405f866cdd0fab37635c"},"summary":"A plan with no feature left to build makes no job","tags":["revisit:the owner wants every kept plan in the queue, or a finished build's plan is needed in the core","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:09:09.398869Z","id":"dd1e145a3cf72ff18c3819c288ad8fbe4e5ce35dd3bb97b139d69cee6889d472","body":{"detail":"lib/queue/codec.dart does not exist yet (the worker isolate passes JobInput, PlanState and Carry across as objects, apps/clax_app/lib/queue/.qual), so the shapes the import writes, input {request, base, threads}, plan {plan_rest, data}, carry {stops, can_keep_going, data}, are its own choice, documented in docs/contract.md ('The app's JSON state, imported once'). The codec must read these, or the import must change with it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"b162978fd2d581be383463e9e6eb0f07d2de2f13ebf25e5afc4ca921da52d00f"},"suggested_fix":"Write the codec against these shapes, with a test decoding the rows of crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs's each_file_becomes_its_rows_once.","summary":"The import fixes the JSON of a job's input, plan and carry before the queue's codec reads it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T23:52:58.918347Z","id":"4a1c81dc19cc5b173802076b78d07a8d5eb50bc07bce4407a7dfd0b1f1ed1f18","body":{"detail":"Failure: a change-ledger.json whose records have an empty db (no document writes). The app sets docs_done only when it wrote documents (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart:681-684, lib/agent/loop.dart), and keeps a finished change's record until 64 newer ones push it out, so most records have docs_done false. ledger() makes a job done only when docs_done and the reply landed (imports.rs:584-595), so each such record becomes a queued change job, most with a publish:<base> step committed, which the worker isolate's queue then takes up (its next step is the reply). Seen on a read-only copy of the Mac app's support directory and clax-home (11 ledger records on one app, all docs_done false): the import made 11 queued change jobs, 10 with publish steps (publish:1, 2, 3, 10-16) and 6 with no thread, plus 2 stopped make jobs, with no artifact, for two provisional plans (new:<time>) of the same request 'A vim inspired text editor' that had features left.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":556},"end":{"line":614},"content_hash":"c071ca3bd097e792a4f6d17b9284502c64fedac97bd704860a3a41e6d4398e1b"},"suggested_fix":"Treat an empty db as documents done (docs_done || db is empty), and a record whose version and reply landed as done. A record whose version base + 1 was not made by it is a change that may never have landed; whether it should run again is the owner's call. Decide whether provisional plans (new:<time> keys) with no app should become stopped makes.","summary":"A ledger record of a change that wrote no documents is imported as a queued change job, so every past change the ledger still holds would run again","tags":["task:29","import","core","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T00:27:58.945618Z","id":"9fd36173bd98e32d83d1fbb7ecc994bfb5eddaafc77f8fa550ee8b3c536dac5c","body":{"detail":"Spec §9 makes a stopped make job of every plans.json entry that no pending make claims. plans.json keeps the plan of every app built since, finished ones included (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/plan.dart PlanStore), so that would put a Keep going row in the queue for every finished build. The import makes one only while a feature is todo or doing.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":472},"end":{"line":474},"content_hash":"d764f559a2fae8f0174c4b236ea86cb57d1344812d64405f866cdd0fab37635c"},"summary":"A plan with no feature left to build makes no job","supersedes":"4a954d6b450716d342932ff6986191ea078303f4109185884cc3c9051ff466ef","tags":["revisit:the owner wants every kept plan in the queue, or a finished build's plan is needed in the core","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T00:27:59.003724Z","id":"9e3264daea4500a5cc3bd4d9e043c437501b227d76e2bfb45a92c455d475e46c","body":{"detail":"The app moves a make's plan to the app's ID once the make made it (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart newApp, plans.move) and clears pending-make.json after (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart, the finally of the make), so a pending make whose request has only an app's plan ended after making its app, and importing it would make that app a second time. The same inputs come from a second make of an earlier app's exact request that was cut off before its first plan_set (or a single-call make, which keeps no plan): that make is left out too, named in the summary's left_out. Not taken: keeping every such make queued (a made one makes a duplicate app), or telling them apart by time (pending-make.json keeps no time).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":494},"end":{"line":514},"content_hash":"54dc184a022c804ee548f0f05b6fa264b3bb92bc9019b6ad911a5b5a23a69de0"},"summary":"A pending make is left out as made whenever an app's plan names its request and no provisional plan claims the make","tags":["revisit:a make retried with an earlier app's request is found missing after the import","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T00:27:59.003789Z","id":"0c194fcb63b4ecddf29ac0b160b0799f461154cb8f7b1fa928c087aeb9b35638","body":{"detail":"The app's recovery starts the build of every plan not under a provisional key that is buildable (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart _recoverBuilds, and _buildable at worker.dart:705-706: not stopped, features to build, spentUsd under buildCapUsd). The import makes every plan with a todo or doing feature a stopped make job and does not read the plan's stopped field, so after the import a build the app would have resumed by itself waits for Keep going, and looks the same as one the person stopped. The choice is the owner's: queued for a buildable plan (the app's behaviour), or stopped for all (the person resumes each).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":479},"end":{"line":492},"content_hash":"f3da61b6f158b7f8a9c29abffc14f53ef48365ed39bbe13d5980dd93e6b54a59"},"summary":"A plan under an app with features to build imports as a stopped make, though the app's own recovery builds it","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T00:27:59.003839Z","id":"b9805f50dc4a570f37bc059c986d9aa752d5fa8416717c0c26eae6c130d4b3e7","body":{"detail":"The app's recovery forgets every unfinished.json entry whose thread is not among the open threads, the thread resolved or its app deleted (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart _pruneUnfinished), so such a change is never kept going. The import makes a stopped change job of it all the same, offering Keep going on a change whose threads are closed or gone. Leaving such an entry out breaks apps/clax_app/test/core/json_import_real_test.dart as it stands: its fixture's unfinished change (apps/clax_app/test/fixtures/json-state/unfinished.json) names thread 01JA8Z3K6Q0V7N2M4P5R6S7T8W, which the test never creates, and the test expects a stopped change on Habits and two left_out entries. The fix lands together with that test giving the entry an open thread, or expecting it left out.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":579},"end":{"line":594},"content_hash":"e772edc7e704307b2ada03da2912479d187ab7bfa3e3d4f529ca6be1ef1f3306"},"suggested_fix":"Before change_threads, leave the entry out unless one of its threads is open on its artifact (threads.status = 'open'), naming it in left_out; change json_import_real_test.dart to create the fixture's thread, or to expect the change left out.","summary":"An unfinished change none of whose threads is open imports as a stopped change job, though the app forgets it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T00:27:59.046714Z","id":"dae8517d3c68a075ef7eb117dc8fd364668fa99bc85f4c5a33591d48398a7ae6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed: a ledger record whose version landed is done when docs_done or its db is empty (as apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart _settleDocs reads it) and every address still open has an agent reply at or after the version; a record whose addresses are all resolved or gone has no reply left. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test passes (758 passed, 3 ignored), among them imports::tests::a_ledger_change_with_nothing_left_to_apply_is_done (base 1 no db -> done [publish:1, reply]; base 2 db unwritten -> queued [publish:2]; base 3 thread resolved -> done; base 4 reply owed -> queued [publish:4]; base 8 never landed -> queued, no steps), which fails with the fix reverted to rec.docs_done alone and with replied() refusing a closed address; //apps/clax_app:core_json_import_real_test passes.","supersedes":"4a1c81dc19cc5b173802076b78d07a8d5eb50bc07bce4407a7dfd0b1f1ed1f18","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T00:48:41.603188Z","id":"4a7e054f2f68bbad51478e97f065596cc92465701d06d3d816821079618da26c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed: the import leaves out an unfinished.json change unless one of its threads is open on its artifact, naming it in left_out, as AgentWorker._pruneUnfinished forgets it. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test passes (759 passed, 3 ignored), among them imports::tests::an_unfinished_change_with_no_thread_open_makes_no_job (a resolved thread and a gone thread left out; a change with one of two threads open stays stopped), which fails with the check disabled; //apps/clax_app:core_json_import_real_test passes, expecting the fixture's unfinished change (its thread not in the core) left out with three left_out entries, and fails with the check disabled (Expected length 3, has length 2).","supersedes":"b9805f50dc4a570f37bc059c986d9aa752d5fa8416717c0c26eae6c130d4b3e7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:15:44.978870Z","id":"72024249511b7f6fd15b884bafba2591d72780b72cdc319605f8193ccb9eb5a2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d49ac731c5f255c580ef21652d8e574aa629c99bba4ed98b7e3aa38dd9d66bfd","summary":"The loser's error is no longer a 500: record_version_locked maps a content write's AlreadyExists, while the artifact is still at expected, to CoreError::Invalid version_present, which clax-http answers 409 (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs version_present; crates/clax-http/src/error.rs). It is still not Conflict with current, since the winner has not recorded the version yet; a client that rereads and retries gets Conflict or succeeds.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:18.131813Z","id":"ec9ae232c212514a566830fec4df3cb14343a464f1372bdb27c87ba16e041831","body":{"detail":"Failure: thread T has viewer comment C, sent to everyone while session S (the owner's agent) and session A (a connected person's agent) both watch; S takes C (row (C,S) delivered, S becomes owner through take_in, which keeps A's row because A is another person's); S releases T (Store::handoff with to = None, feedback.rs:1013-1027), which untargets A's undelivered row to an untargeted row U for C; then the owner sends T to S again (Store::send_to with SendTarget::Agent(S), or `@S` through Store::send_to_named). send_in runs `UPDATE feedback SET target_session_id = S ... WHERE target_session_id IS NULL AND delivered_at IS NULL` (feedback.rs:261-265), which sets U's target to S while (C,S) already exists: SQLite refuses it under the unique index feedback_comment_target (migrations.rs:97) and the whole send fails with a database error. send_to_named has the same UPDATE at feedback.rs:917-921. Every other path that hands untargeted rows to a session first deletes the untargeted rows whose comment the session already has a row for: take_in (threads.rs:373-378), Store::handoff to a session (feedback.rs:1074-1079) and Store::retarget_untargeted (feedback.rs:1655-1666). These two UPDATEs also leave notified_at and push_failed_at as they were, which those paths clear.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":258},"end":{"line":266},"content_hash":"147124b07d691eadbd883fa9d45005db802123215c5655dfe6c51ab13b0015f6"},"suggested_fix":"Before each UPDATE, run the same DELETE the other paths use (`DELETE FROM feedback WHERE thread_id = ?1 AND delivered_at IS NULL AND target_session_id IS NULL AND comment_id IN (SELECT comment_id FROM feedback WHERE thread_id = ?1 AND target_session_id = ?2)`), clear notified_at and push_failed_at in the UPDATE, and factor the three-statement hand-over into one helper used by send_in, send_to_named, handoff, take_in and retarget_untargeted. Add a test for the sequence above.","summary":"A send naming an agent retargets untargeted rows without dropping duplicates first, so it can trip the unique (comment_id, target_session_id) index and fail","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:18.132040Z","id":"517b3e30ac5e9a733de52cb2ffb8a28d8a88703243af459aef029f54cde89f28","body":{"detail":"take_feedback_readable (feedback.rs:1190) and take_notices (feedback.rs:1704) refuse a view older than the store's visibility generation inside their write transaction (stale_view, feedback.rs:421-423), so an approval revoked after the view was built never lets a withheld body through. acknowledge_where uses `vis` to decide whether an undelivered row's body was seen (feedback.rs:1589-1602) and then marks it delivered by piggyback and records feedback.delivered, but never asks whether `vis` is stale. Its callers build the view in a separate read just before (clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs:772, routes/threads.rs:1095 and 1539: Visibility::for_session, then store.acknowledge), so an approval revoked between the two marks a row delivered whose body the agent's person no longer lets through. A delivered row is never held or resent (spec §9.4, 'what was delivered stays delivered'), so the row is lost to the placeholder and to any later approval.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1573},"end":{"line":1603},"content_hash":"2b340a95b6cb5353f3c2c5372c9fd0bdb2753b4383d702f1baba8341c9741fac"},"suggested_fix":"Check stale_view(self, vis) at the start of acknowledge_where's transaction and, when stale, return a stale marker (as Taken::stale does) so the caller rebuilds the view and acknowledges again; or rebuild the view inside the transaction with Visibility::for_reader_in.","summary":"acknowledge marks rows delivered under a view it never checks against the visibility generation, unlike take_feedback and take_notices","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:18.132175Z","id":"da9843eba8b3f5d3ebfd1c1182383317dfdb9101758afc636b75be8dfe0a76aa","body":{"detail":"request_state_in (approvals.rs:155-175) answers `declined` for any declined request of the approver there, of any age, for the thread or the whole artifact. declines_in (feedback.rs:2169-2203), which feeds a thread's delivery state, ends a decline once an approval of that author covering the thread was made or revoked after it (`a.created_at > decided_at OR a.revoked_at > decided_at`). So after a decline, a later approval and its revocation, the agent's thread view (clax-http/src/views/thread.rs:1146-1170, `withheld.approval`) and its placeholders (feedback.rs:688-694 uses only `requested`, but the view uses `declined`) say `declined` while the thread's delivery state, read by the owner and the person, no longer does. The two readings of one hold disagree, and the agent is told its person declined content its person last approved.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"c7248feee5c71a8cbc3b6b4cee4c654628aad3cd26e0c1fb1eeb654c655c9a29"},"suggested_fix":"Apply the same 'no approval made or revoked since' rule in REQUEST_STATE (an EXISTS against approvals per declined row, as DECLINES does), or have request_state_in call declines_in's logic, so both readings share one definition of a decline in force.","summary":"REQUEST_STATE reads a decline as standing forever, while the delivery state ends it at a later approval or revocation","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:18.132279Z","id":"f2ce08a5b0c74a558ba6a1001e944866d3e0aff589a9be0602e563082ce5a76a","body":{"detail":"The doc comment (approvals.rs:1927-1928) says 'Once the approver holds fewer than [`MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS`], the overflow marker is cleared.' The code (approvals.rs:2001-2012) never counts open requests: it keeps every place for which held_without_request (approvals.rs:968-1007) still holds, so an approver well under the limit keeps the banner while any counted place is still held without a request, and an approver still at the limit loses it once those places are answered. The banner's lifetime is a known open thread (b8689b37); this record is only about the contract text.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1920},"end":{"line":1933},"content_hash":"ade18f3cc28118a3c6cc46156e5914af2af3c2d8a26c9d6bc4c6b8664fdeca8c"},"suggested_fix":"Reword the doc to say what the code does: after every decision, each place the overflow marker holds is dropped once its content is no longer held without a request (held_without_request), and the marker goes when none is left.","summary":"decide_request's doc says the overflow marker clears once the approver holds fewer than MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS; the code drops each place only when its content is no longer held without a request","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:18.132434Z","id":"8332718f9ffd0e03ff684a160447439939c4238a9bf4d0319c320eb3cf3ede88","body":{"detail":"narrowing() returns None when the person's rights are within the access the client asked for (people.rs:456-458); request_grant (people.rs:1115) and approve_grant (people.rs:1297-1301) then store narrow_json NULL, and grant_caller_in (people.rs:2541-2550) gives the grant the person's current rights. A client that asked for, say, read access while its person held only read keeps no record of that ask: when the owner later raises the person to the collaborator preset, the machine's agents gain write access it never asked for. The asked access survives only in the grant.request audit record (people.rs:627). Whether a grant should follow its person's rights upward is a product decision; the store currently cannot keep the ask either way.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":454},"end":{"line":458},"content_hash":"913a42f078e2d657c9aa36665eee58191ea253819621bde3a4a1cca32a66af23"},"suggested_fix":"Store the asked access whenever it is narrower than full rights (narrow_json = access unless access is Rights::full()), so effective rights stay person ∩ asked as the person's rights change; or record that following the person upward is intended in the grant section of the multi-person spec.","summary":"A grant whose client asked for at least its person's rights stores no narrowing, so it widens with every later raise of the person's rights beyond what it asked","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:18.132569Z","id":"f707bd244b6ca7359470e5895ed33fc52a0e6e241592bebd294541137f2d7168","body":{"detail":"The continuation token, accept_t's replay check, the issue window and the 'already answered' check run in one with_tx (people.rs:1547-1598); the approval is made afterwards by Store::approve_touched in a second transaction (people.rs:1602-1608), whose approve_in checks only that the person is connected (approvals.rs:543-556), not that the grant is still approved. A revoke_grant or disconnect_grant committed between the two leaves an approval of the owner everywhere recorded as the person (created_via connect) through a grant that had already ended. The window is small, but this is the one approval made without a browser (waiver 9de6ef35), so its checks and its write belong in one transaction.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1545},"end":{"line":1610},"content_hash":"9daccd6836bd98430336a830052976546ba1246d69be0578b83fef5d9456c11e"},"suggested_fix":"Make the approval inside the first transaction: expose approve_in (or a pub(crate) wrapper taking a Transaction) and call it after the checks, returning the Approval and Touched from the same with_tx.","summary":"approve_owner_on_connect checks the grant in one transaction and makes the approval in another","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.329513Z","id":"f3deee1549760876d0e5033484bb0804cfc4d8f270b273c15c20e40fca17337d","body":{"detail":"Store::assemble records every inbox_items and approval_requests row change through conn.update_hook and drops the list only in conn.rollback_hook. SQLite invokes the rollback hook only when a whole transaction rolls back (https://sqlite.org/c3ref/commit_hook.html), not on ROLLBACK TO a savepoint, and the update hook has already fired for rows a later-failing multi-row statement undoes (https://sqlite.org/c3ref/update_hook.html). No write under Store::with_tx uses a savepoint today (only backfill.rs:541, which runs before the hooks are installed), so nothing breaks now; but the first write that wraps an inbox insert in a savepoint and rolls it back, while its transaction commits, hands the inbox listener a seq that does not exist. Because inbox_items.seq is a plain INTEGER PRIMARY KEY (migrations.rs:919-920), the next insert in the same transaction reuses that seq, so the listener hears it twice as made.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":304},"end":{"line":328},"content_hash":"8d5328b25a37682e7c5e5b38263f0ace46e6273d4dc0138b397cf29ef9a6a5d9"},"suggested_fix":"Either document on Store::with_tx that jobs must not roll back to a savepoint after writing inbox_items or approval_requests, or make the listener inputs robust: dedupe inbox changes by seq when taking them in with_tx (as request_changes already does by rowid) and have the listener's readers skip seqs that are not found.","summary":"The inbox and approval-request change lists are cleared only by the rollback hook, which a savepoint rollback or a failed statement does not fire","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.329690Z","id":"ffd232e74ce1887d93c07e16c4cdb36ab4ef78963a32982f29359db1bf8d50f4","body":{"detail":"repair() inserts each live session's owner elevation with INSERT OR IGNORE INTO session_elevations, then creates session_elevations_key (UNIQUE on session_id, COALESCE(granter, '')) later, in REPAIR_INDEXES (migrations.rs:1457). When the table was just made by REPAIR_TABLES or came from a copy of migration 24 without that index, OR IGNORE has nothing to ignore against: an owner row already present for the session is duplicated, and the CREATE UNIQUE INDEX that follows fails, so migration 37 aborts and the store cannot open. Whether any database holds both elevate_json and a pre-index session_elevations row is not known; the ordering makes the repair depend on it.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1555},"end":{"line":1569},"content_hash":"487fc66b9c0330dbad7d6d8ba10cbd4f8babbb0d2cfa748f0d6f1ee7057e3708"},"suggested_fix":"Create session_elevations_key (CREATE UNIQUE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS) right after REPAIR_TABLES and before the elevate_json move, or guard the insert with WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM session_elevations WHERE session_id = ?1 AND granter IS NULL).","summary":"Migration 37's repair moves sessions.elevate_json into session_elevations with INSERT OR IGNORE before it creates the unique index that OR IGNORE relies on","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.329806Z","id":"260fe64542ac9839ccb8d720599fb577ec9f0d1bdabde2819b8e4940891476f2","body":{"detail":"The doc block above legacy_viewer_cookies opens with 'Mints the install ID once: 128 random bits in lowercase hex…', which describes install_id (migrations.rs:1607), then goes on to describe the legacy cookies. rustdoc and editors show the install-ID text on the wrong function, and install_id is undocumented.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1586},"end":{"line":1608},"content_hash":"58340413419b701cf7c1e51846d980fe3ae18a6c79b36ddbc45681e2bfd4482d"},"suggested_fix":"Move the first two sentences ('Mints the install ID once … does not date the install.') to a doc comment on install_id, leaving legacy_viewer_cookies' doc to start at 'Keeps every existing viewer's cookie'.","summary":"install_id's doc comment is attached to legacy_viewer_cookies, and install_id has none","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.329878Z","id":"cbc488f75583cf92188b7cc4b1129cf3c9caaf1c2548b624dd1a0f4b165d93fe","body":{"detail":"hosted_setup_via checks hosted_needs_setup() (a read), then calls set_owner_name(name, true) (viewers.rs:700-713, its own with_tx), and only then runs the transaction whose INSERT OR IGNORE INTO hosted_setup decides who set up. Interleaving: request A and request B both read needs_setup = true; A renames the owner 'Ada' and commits setup; B renames the owner 'Bob', then its INSERT OR IGNORE changes no row and it returns NotFound. The site is set up by A, but the owner row is now named 'Bob' and no audit record says so. The same holds for a setup whose later step fails (record_audit, the approval revokes): the owner keeps the new name with setup still open. Both setup callers can race: the setup-secret route and github_sign_in's owner path (github.rs:197-206), which may also retry with the login as the name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":417},"end":{"line":458},"content_hash":"49b34a278e4109554a1abfbcc0fb487d21eb48d9c91cf7afbe7ee415bc4e6e19"},"suggested_fix":"Do the name check and the UPDATE of the owner's display_name inside the setup transaction, after the INSERT OR IGNORE INTO hosted_setup succeeds (owner_viewer(true) can still run first, as it only makes or claims the row); add a test that a second setup with another name leaves the first name in place.","summary":"hosted_setup_via renames the owner in its own transaction before the setup transaction, so a setup that loses the race (or fails later) still renames the owner","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.329951Z","id":"29bc565de9f2f998b8d4f4fda83d6b60435a2f437f4dbf45d1a742487be578f7","body":{"detail":"fold() rewrites sessions/artifacts/versions/assets person columns, invites, grants, comments, mentions, threads, viewer_seen, viewer_threads, private docs and cookies, then DELETEs the viewer row. Tables added since by migrations without a foreign key on viewer_id (browser_sessions and signin_links, migrations.rs:772-790, whose comment says there is no foreign key 'as the owner row's ID is rewritten by a claim'; github_identities; artifact_shares.viewer_id and created_by, migrations.rs:950-970; legal_agreements, legal.rs) are not touched, so their rows would point at a deleted row ID or a retired public ID. Today claim_for_owner (viewers.rs:735-795, the only caller) is reached only from the local shell token route (crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs:62) for a minted_local, non-person viewer, so these tables are empty for the rows it folds; the invariant is implicit and the next table keyed by viewer row will be missed the same way.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":337},"end":{"line":415},"content_hash":"ff4e7538a6958b2ee7ed1c5e1d00ebba1327239d759605db3ba3c3a5d40370e9"},"suggested_fix":"Either move the hosted tables in fold() (UPDATE ... SET viewer_id = into.id, and created_by public IDs), or assert in claim_for_owner that the folded row has no rows in them, with a test that lists every table holding a viewer_id column (from sqlite_master) against what fold() handles.","summary":"fold() moves a hand-kept list of viewer-row tables and misses every hosted-era one (browser_sessions, signin_links, github_identities, artifact_shares, legal_agreements, hosted_setup)","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.330005Z","id":"c6b2c70b37f45e9f9cebb159eb42cc4767b2513f50c0a8df07a1a2cec528a774","body":{"detail":"share_artifact (shares.rs:331-346) returns already_owner only when a github_identities row already links the login to the owner. A share made to the owner's login before the owner's account was linked waits with viewer_id NULL; github_sign_in's owner path then calls link(tx, now, user, &owner.id) (github.rs:131-141, 210-224), and bind_github_shares binds the waiting share to the owner's row. The sharing dialog (artifact_shares, SHARE_SELECT) then lists the owner as a person the artifact is shared with, which share_artifact never allows; rights are unaffected (rights_of_row returns full rights for the owner, people.rs:406-415).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":192},"end":{"line":231},"content_hash":"d900f1093954fe8f09fbe2d41cddf15b8614c0a19ebe048ced1d2a2ec59cf73d"},"suggested_fix":"In bind_github_shares, when viewer_id is the owner's row, delete the waiting shares instead of binding them (recording artifact.update of the share as unshare_artifact does), and cover it with a test that shares to a login, links it to the owner, and expects no share left.","summary":"A share waiting for a GitHub login binds to the owner's row when the owner later signs in with that login, though share_artifact refuses sharing with the owner","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.330109Z","id":"3bc9d44f895ae70a36c4ee1e5d43e933f0c8026eb8eb1a6c01a75b4aa1d7c6f8","body":{"detail":"Failure: a local daemon linked to a remote (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs) mirrors remote thread R as local thread T; the owner deletes T (DELETE /api/artifacts/<id>/threads/<T>, crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:1726); then anyone comments on R there. delete_thread_rows (threads.rs:1736-1775) deletes comments, feedback, version_threads, live_pending, mentions, viewer_threads, batch_threads, thread_moves and page_authors, but not linked_threads, linked_comments, linked_outbox, comment_keys or live_picks. On the next read, crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs mirror() finds the linked_threads row (linked_thread_by_remote, unlinked_at NULL), calls Store::mirror_comment (linked.rs:607, thread_in -> NotFound) or reaches st.get_thread(&tid)?.ok_or(NotFound) (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs:1538). The error becomes Stop::Unreachable through From<ApiError> (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs:238), read() returns before set_sync_cursor, so every later cycle re-reads R and fails the same way: the link shows unreachable and no other thread syncs. mirror_thread (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:544-553) likewise returns the dead local ID for that remote thread. The outbox side copes (send() acks rows of a gone thread, crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs:855-862); the inbound side does not, and no test in crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs deletes a linked thread.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":1736},"end":{"line":1775},"content_hash":"a07b1ac69c4bca19383547e644613884500a8fe1f86b2c8fca5c547326734520"},"suggested_fix":"Decide what a local delete of a linked thread means and make both sides agree. Either mark the link instead of deleting it (UPDATE linked_threads SET unlinked_at = now WHERE thread_id = ?1, in delete_thread_rows; mirror() already skips unlinked rows) and delete its linked_comments, linked_outbox and comment_keys rows, or have mirror()/mirror_comment treat a linked row whose thread is gone as unlinked rather than an error. Add an api_linked test: mirror, delete locally, comment remotely, sync, and check the link still syncs other threads.","summary":"Deleting a mirrored (linked) thread leaves its linked_threads row, so the next sync that sees the remote thread fails with NotFound and stops the link's sync for good","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.330205Z","id":"3604d6f60cfbf480efcf3de48cec233a0b91dd48b27c7200669019b848271926","body":{"detail":"commit_refile updates live_pending, live_picks, version_threads, watches, inbox_items (inbox::thread_moved), questions and sessions.delivered_artifact_id for a moved thread (site.rs:684-714), but approval_requests rows carry artifact_id and thread_id (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1306-1320) and are looked up by both: REQUEST_STATE (crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs:145-152) and the open-request lookup (approvals.rs:1090-1096) filter on artifact_id = the thread's page. After a merge, un-merge, owner move or join moves a thread, its open or declined request is no longer found at the new page: a declined author can be asked about again, and a second open request is made for the same thread. Deleting the old page then withdraws the moved thread's request with reason artifact_deleted (withdraw_artifact_in, approvals.rs:1449-1466, called from Store::delete_artifact_async). linked_threads.artifact_id and linked_outbox.artifact_id are not carried either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":674},"end":{"line":714},"content_hash":"d202c89427ccb6f97258fb96296f697f9f40c757ca0f6c842fa5a46bf0a7c8a6"},"suggested_fix":"In the p.from != to.artifact_id branch of commit_refile, also run UPDATE approval_requests SET artifact_id = ?2 WHERE thread_id = ?1 (and the same for linked_threads/linked_outbox if live pages can be linked), and do the same in the join path in crates/clax-store/src/joined.rs; add a store test that moves a thread with a declined request and checks request_state at the new page.","summary":"Moving a thread to another page (commit_refile) carries its questions, inbox items and pending address but not its approval_requests, which stay keyed on the old page's artifact_id","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.330308Z","id":"04160d91ba261c333a0ad4ffedb33bf2f980d141e0f5184027a717a523bb9464","body":{"detail":"Store::ensure_live_page_linking_async (crates/clax-store/src/live.rs:494-534) inserts the page's artifacts row at current_version 0 and, through materialize/scope_row (live.rs:197-215, 264-300), a watches row for each live session whose scope covers it, in one transaction; version 1 is written in a later one. A crash or a failed snapshot write between them leaves a zero-version page with watches rows. zero_version_artifacts lists it, and delete_zero_version_artifacts_async (artifacts.rs:571-610) deletes its assets, versions, docs, leases and live_pages rows, then the artifacts row; watches.artifact_id REFERENCES artifacts(id) (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:50-54) and foreign keys are on (crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:274), so the DELETE fails with a FOREIGN KEY error, the transaction rolls back, and doctor's fix step (crates/clax-commands/src/commands/doctor.rs:461-462) returns that error every run. live_merged_pages and page_authors (kind asset) rows of the artifact are not removed either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":571},"end":{"line":610},"content_hash":"bc07a3cbde6781e0777781bdc619c252cdf18447364fa51e3367bcc46dbf7aea"},"suggested_fix":"Add watches (and live_merged_pages, and page_authors of its assets) to the tables delete_zero_version_artifacts_async clears, gated by the same zero-version subquery; add a test that makes a live page with a scope watch and no version, then runs delete_zero_version_artifacts.","summary":"delete_zero_version_artifacts deletes no watches, so a live page left at version 0 with a scope watch makes the artifacts DELETE fail its foreign key and `clax doctor --fix` errors","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.330390Z","id":"2ad79590adb495d372f3c59723d4aa2d25346590a327813cb56d04a8930e47f3","body":{"detail":"create_artifact_async calls check_quota (artifacts.rs:1027) and then inserts the row in a separate with_tx (artifacts.rs:1028-1036); fork_artifact_async does the same (crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs:98, insert at forks.rs:175). check_quota (crates/clax-store/src/github.rs:312-342) counts the person's live artifacts with with_read. Two creates by a capped member at count max_artifacts - 1 both see room and both insert, ending above MemberCaps::max_artifacts; N parallel publishes over the API can overshoot by up to N - 1. The cap exists to bound a hosted member's use of a shared service, so it is the case that sees concurrent callers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1019},"end":{"line":1036},"content_hash":"744ff823de91a235e46099a73773f90062ca529ab2db679589eaa41b6ff91fab"},"suggested_fix":"Run the count inside the insert's transaction (a check_quota_in(tx, person) used by both create_artifact_async and fork_artifact_async before their INSERT), so the count and the insert are serialised by SQLite's write lock.","summary":"A member's artifact cap is checked in its own read, outside the transaction that inserts the artifact, so concurrent creates or forks exceed it","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.330444Z","id":"55d8463c9bfe0ac7f1bade1f51cd6a25f354d63b3e5d818df8e4e2946a33de9d","body":{"detail":"add_asset_async checks get_artifact (assets.rs:176), writes the bytes with put_asset (assets.rs:189), then inserts the row (assets.rs:190-191) without re-checking deleted_at and without lock_content, which delete_artifact_async holds across its mark and its content removal (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:368-454). If the delete runs between the check and put_asset, the content store's removal has already happened and put_asset recreates the bytes; the INSERT then succeeds for the soft-deleted artifact. get_asset (assets.rs:219-229) does not filter deleted artifacts, and the /_blob route (crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs:159-194) checks only SeesLive, so those bytes stay public until `clax doctor --fix` runs delete_assets_of_deleted_artifacts. The same holds whenever the content removal in delete_artifact_async fails, which it only logs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":176},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"4c590a1d9650e4099e6f7bfc98ffa4160437b8c20151ec96bb7249cf304b429d"},"suggested_fix":"Take lock_content(id) around the check, put_asset and insert (as create_thread_inner does for clips, crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs:838-849), and re-check liveness in the insert's transaction (artifact_live); have get_asset, or the /_blob route, answer NotFound for an asset whose artifact is deleted.","summary":"An asset upload checks the artifact is live outside its transaction and without the content lock, so an upload racing a delete stores a row and bytes for a deleted artifact that /_blob then serves","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.330529Z","id":"e52804edf2a474d42e4400b7da6a76ebc01e6a3e7a2160242a51ec385a9bcbf1","body":{"detail":"close_question (crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs:1001-1002) calls super::inbox::question_changed on every close, including Close::Withdraw, so the item's inbox_fts text is rewritten with answered_text(q) and QUESTION_TOUCH runs; crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:1232 says that touch is 'Always written, so the listener hears that the source changed'. withdraw_session_questions (lines 529-533) calls it only for in_terminal rows, and withdraw_hook_questions_on_start (lines 1097-1108) never calls it. So when a session ends or the daemon restarts, the open questions it withdraws leave their inbox items untouched: no inbox change is signalled for them, and their search text still reads as an open question. The two paths and close_question now disagree on what a withdrawal does to the inbox.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":518},"end":{"line":536},"content_hash":"d0a4029caadaa4ff18d323d2b748676cd16154f94bbe2f8985f80611273b7402"},"suggested_fix":"In withdraw_session_questions and withdraw_hook_questions_on_start, call super::inbox::question_changed(tx, &q, false, now) for every withdrawn question (it already marks in-terminal items read itself), and add a test that an ended session's open ask question's inbox item is touched.","summary":"Session-end and daemon-start withdrawals skip inbox::question_changed for questions not in the terminal, unlike every other close","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.330607Z","id":"c453957c1c869106adfbec22ce5620e54a5cfa63c4181114d65cd8c6caa2964f","body":{"detail":"The query is 'SELECT id FROM questions WHERE thread_id = ?1 AND status = 'open' ORDER BY id'. Migration 38 (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1152) adds questions.thread_id with no index, and the existing indexes (questions_by_status, questions_by_session, questions_by_artifact, questions_by_tool_use, questions_*_by_person) do not lead with thread_id, so SQLite scans questions (or walks every open row through questions_by_status). Closed questions are kept forever, so the table only grows. The caller, crates/clax-http/src/views/question.rs:118-119 (announce_thread), runs on every resolve, reopen or delete of any thread. The SQL is inline rather than a pub(crate) const, so crates/clax-store/src/plans.rs question_queries() cannot check it. crates/clax-store/src/site.rs:707 ('UPDATE questions SET artifact_id = ?2 WHERE thread_id = ?1') has the same full scan.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":805},"end":{"line":813},"content_hash":"e5e4d0738ff98d61c2d1f1ba4f88a964ea7f8e39e6337e218d99f08c9e5f1823"},"suggested_fix":"Add a migration with a partial index such as 'CREATE INDEX questions_by_thread ON questions(thread_id, id) WHERE thread_id IS NOT NULL', move the query into a const, and add it and the site.rs update to plans.rs question_queries().","summary":"open_questions_in_thread scans the whole questions table: questions.thread_id has no index and the query is not in the plan checks","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.330700Z","id":"a2967b618a2d4b830469a252f3348d3ccdac0818d576bd10e6cc431afdd8c7c0","body":{"detail":"scan_linked loads links with links_of_remote (a separate read, line 749) and then, in with_tx, inserts linked_threads rows with unlinked_at NULL and linked_outbox rows for each link (lines 773-805); mirror_thread (lines 530-598) is handed a RemoteLink by crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs (cycle reads links before drain/read) and inserts a linked_threads row without checking the link still exists. unlink_remote (lines 467-482) is an owner action on another task; if it commits between the read and the write, the new rows survive with unlinked_at NULL although the link is gone. linked_views (line 1106) then reports them as not unlinked. If the owner later links the artifact to the same remote again (possibly a different remote_artifact_id), scan_linked's comment query (lines 808-814) filters only by remote_id and artifact_id, so those stale rows are picked up again and their comments are sent with the old remote_thread_id against the new link.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":748},"end":{"line":873},"content_hash":"6b386ff7257d77ec92a0cd7279902040f89789f4666dc4ff379b08d30bc4134b"},"suggested_fix":"Inside each transaction, re-read the link (SELECT from remote_links WHERE artifact_id AND remote_id, matching remote_artifact_id) and skip it when it is gone or changed; or have scan_linked's comment and status queries join remote_links on remote_artifact_id so stale rows are never resent.","summary":"scan_linked and mirror_thread read the link outside their write transaction and never re-check remote_links inside it, so a concurrent unlink leaves live-looking linked_threads rows","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.330771Z","id":"b8ab72608f6012889aabb83bc1419dd84ee1f8a93e0a3b3b525b4e0d625e5dcd","body":{"detail":"The hosted route checks the key with Store::comment_key in one store call (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:745) and, in a later call, creates the thread and only then records the key with record_comment_key's own with_tx (routes/threads.rs:894-895; the comment path at 1153 does the same). Two requests carrying the same Idempotency-Key that both pass the check create two threads; INSERT OR IGNORE keeps only the first key, so the second request's thread is an unkeyed duplicate. A failure or cancelled future between the thread's transaction and the key's (on a Worker every job is awaited inline) leaves a thread with no key, and the linked sync's resend under the same key (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs drain) then makes a second public thread. Questions avoid this: create_question_keyed (crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs:689-760) checks and records question_keys inside the creating transaction.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1385},"end":{"line":1416},"content_hash":"b8ab43d4cba6ee0bb3ef860a9fd66e2e33a6da678b22bcb8eba28cab63d7a1ac"},"suggested_fix":"Give create_thread/add_comment a keyed variant, as create_question_keyed does: look up comment_keys, create, and insert the key in one transaction, returning the existing thread/comment when the key is already recorded.","summary":"A keyed comment or thread is recorded in comment_keys in a separate transaction from the write it keys, so concurrent or interrupted resends can make it twice","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.330860Z","id":"c6aabc94859c56db6d88ba500a29052ef4757603eb6248947cdf49d0d364b2be","body":{"detail":"The doc comment (lines 1047-1049) says each page watch removed records its own event, and the main loop does so (lines 1107-1126 record artifact_watch_record(AuditKind::WatchStop, ...)). The loop over 'others' (scope-made watches on pages of a site split off the scope's) deletes rows at lines 1147-1150 and pushes them to `removed` but records nothing, so the audit log shows a page watch that started (watch.start, cause scope) and never stopped.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1131},"end":{"line":1153},"content_hash":"4ba8f4f14367f161fca7432c7d1d682391fff60febeb73caa87e1826c9a6de9c"},"suggested_fix":"Use 'DELETE ... RETURNING replies_armed' there as at lines 1107-1114 and record artifact_watch_record(AuditKind::WatchStop, ..., \"scope\") for each removed row; extend scope_watch_changes_record_starts_updates_and_stops with a split-site case.","summary":"live_unwatch deletes scope-made watches on other sites' pages without recording watch.stop","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:59:34.330912Z","id":"80a4f01bb15e055072d5ba9e0c67e9d91c2ef154177b08a5e78167d7ef08a9f7","body":{"detail":"Store::publish_key (remotes.rs:585) is a plain read and Store::record_publish_key (remotes.rs:599) a separate INSERT OR IGNORE transaction. crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:410-424 (create) and :767-800 (publish) call replayed() -> publish_key, then create_artifact_async / publish_version_async (their own transactions, with awaits on the content store between), then record_publish_key. Two consequences: (1) a retry sent while the first request is still in flight (the client timed out, the server did not) misses the key, so a create makes a second artifact, and a publish without if_version a second version; the loser's INSERT OR IGNORE then drops its key silently. (2) a crash or error between the version's commit and record_publish_key leaves the version with no key, so the retry the key exists for publishes again. The module doc (remotes.rs:24-27) promises that a push sent again is answered the version it made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":583},"end":{"line":608},"content_hash":"93a217a932c976e81355f5df0b6a90fe05e4706902c37d9bdee42b62ebd97c58"},"suggested_fix":"Record the key in the same transaction that inserts the version (pass it into create_artifact_async / publish_version_async and INSERT it next to the version row, failing on a conflicting row), and, under the artifact's content lock or a per-(grant, key) lock, re-check publish_key before doing work so a concurrent duplicate waits and then replays.","summary":"An Idempotency-Key is looked up, and later recorded, outside the transaction that makes the version, so a retry can publish twice","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:04.741298Z","id":"b5d2f61c2174fd3f3a12f77332273eb520ea8fdcde7ab3cbe37ee3b0edc280f8","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs:261-265 (send_in, SendTarget::Agent) and 917-921 (send_to_named) run a bare `UPDATE feedback SET target_session_id = ?2, untargeted_at = NULL WHERE thread_id = ?1 AND target_session_id IS NULL AND delivered_at IS NULL`. The only step between entering send_in and this UPDATE is targets_for (feedback.rs:105-146), which updates threads only. Store::send_to -> send_routed (feedback.rs:784-825) calls send_in directly. Release (feedback.rs:1013-1027) turns every undelivered targeted row of the thread into an untargeted row and keeps delivered rows, so a delivered (C,S) row can coexist with an untargeted row for C. crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:97 defines `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX feedback_comment_target ON feedback(comment_id, target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL`, which includes delivered rows. The handoff-to-session path (feedback.rs:1074-1084), take_in (threads.rs:373-382) and retarget_untargeted (feedback.rs:1655-1666) all delete or skip duplicates first and clear notified_at/push_failed_at; send_in and send_to_named do neither. Kind concern is right.","kind":"comment","references":"ec9ae232c212514a566830fec4df3cb14343a464f1372bdb27c87ba16e041831","summary":"confirmed: send_in and send_to_named retarget untargeted rows with no prior duplicate DELETE, so they can hit the feedback_comment_target unique index","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:04.741496Z","id":"0f895eb615f004e3f9b3cd0a505a7d2c0947c5e435d222e8feeec289d199b0c3","body":{"detail":"stale_view (crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs:421-423) is called only at feedback.rs:1190 (take_feedback_readable) and 1704 (take_notices); `grep -n stale_view feedback.rs` finds no other call. acknowledge_where (feedback.rs:1555-1615) decides `seen` from `vis.sees(...)` (1589-1602) and then records a piggyback delivery inside its own with_tx, never comparing vis.generation(). Its callers build the view first in a separate store call: crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs:769 (Visibility::for_session, then st.acknowledge at 773), routes/threads.rs:1092 and 1536 (same pattern). A visibility change committed between the two marks a row delivered under the older view. Kind concern is right.","kind":"comment","references":"517b3e30ac5e9a733de52cb2ffb8a28d8a88703243af459aef029f54cde89f28","summary":"confirmed: acknowledge_where never checks the view against the visibility generation","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:04.741659Z","id":"1a3eaeefd92757987d4ea930e5630a57b23d53fbe078505fa8480d41bbd8c149","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs:146-152 (REQUEST_STATE) selects `MAX(status = 'declined')` with no condition on approvals. crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs:2181-2196 (declines_in) drops a decline when an approval of that approver and author covering the thread has `created_at > decided_at OR revoked_at > decided_at`. A declined request keeps status 'declined' after a later approval: the only status updates are approvals.rs:1220 (open -> approved), 1420 (withdrawn), 1984 (declined) and viewers.rs:519 (open -> withdrawn). crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs:1146-1170 feeds Store::request_state into the agent's thread view. After decline, approve, revoke, the view reads `declined` while the delivery state has no decline. Kind concern is right.","kind":"comment","references":"da9843eba8b3f5d3ebfd1c1182383317dfdb9101758afc636b75be8dfe0a76aa","summary":"confirmed: REQUEST_STATE counts any declined request as in force, while declines_in ends a decline at a later approval or revocation","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:04.741816Z","id":"4f12ad91f19066e11d3a74c242d9534336b214725629b2a0a5edcc20a8efd73c","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs:1926-1928 says 'Once the approver holds fewer than [`MAX_OPEN_REQUESTS`], the overflow marker is cleared.' The code at approvals.rs:2001-2012 counts no open requests: it reads overflow_places, keeps each place for which held_without_request is still true, and calls set_overflow with what is left, under the comment 'The banner stays while routed content it counted is still held without a request.' Kind suggestion is right.","kind":"comment","references":"f2ce08a5b0c74a558ba6a1001e944866d3e0aff589a9be0602e563082ce5a76a","summary":"confirmed: decide_request's doc describes a count rule the code does not implement","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:04.741974Z","id":"df3b57c68a1a9d9e07a797f8ea666c357e2abb8a595f8c5079b4bbd27f8fc223","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:456-458: narrowing returns None when person.is_narrower_or_equal(access). The pending grant row holds the asked access in narrow_json (read at people.rs:1241 as `asked`); approve_grant replaces it with narrowing(person, asked) at 1297-1300 and writes it at 1302-1305, so it becomes NULL when the person's rights are within the ask. The invite path does the same at 1115-1118. grant_access (people.rs:442-452) and grant_caller_in (2541-2550, clax_core::rights::effective with grant_narrow None) then give the person's full current rights. The ask survives only in the grant.request audit record (people.rs:627, `.with(\"access\", g.access.to_json())`). Kind suggestion is right, since whether grants follow the person upward is a product choice.","kind":"comment","references":"8332718f9ffd0e03ff684a160447439939c4238a9bf4d0319c320eb3cf3ede88","summary":"confirmed: a grant whose asked access covers the person's current rights keeps no narrowing and follows later raises","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:01:04.742129Z","id":"3edbc7cd3b78c619ed515348fe29527ac8017e4e948a807ba5e9b24beff7f2ac","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:1552-1598: the token, `status = 'approved' AND manage_sha256 IS NOT NULL`, accept_t, the issue window and the answered check run in one self.with_tx, which returns. people.rs:1602-1608 then calls self.approve_touched in a new transaction. approve_in (crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs:543-556) checks only that the approver is a viewer with person = 1, person_revoked_at IS NULL and owner = 0; it never reads the grant's status, so a revoke_grant or disconnect_grant committed between the two transactions that leaves the viewer a person still lets the Via::Connect approval through. Kind suggestion is right given the narrow window.","kind":"comment","references":"f707bd244b6ca7359470e5895ed33fc52a0e6e241592bebd294541137f2d7168","summary":"confirmed: approve_owner_on_connect checks the grant in one transaction and approves in a second that does not recheck it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:18.843825Z","id":"0e362a51b52e4d75a6b98cd23a655abe731e228bda9b77953853079d2b62fff7","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:587-600 deletes only assets, versions, docs, leases and live_pages before 'DELETE FROM artifacts' (and drop_artifact_in, crates/clax-store/src/elevations.rs:298-338, touches only session_elevations). crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:52-54 declares watches.artifact_id REFERENCES artifacts(id) with no ON DELETE action, and crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:274 runs 'PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON'. crates/clax-store/src/live.rs:500-525 inserts the artifacts row at current_version 0 and calls materialize (scope_row, live.rs:197-215, inserts watches rows with source 'scope') in one with_tx; the version is written later by write_snapshot_async (live.rs:548-564), whose Err(e) returns with the version-0 row committed. zero_version_artifacts (artifacts.rs:547-556) selects every current_version = 0, non-deleted row, including that page, and crates/clax-commands/src/commands/doctor.rs:461-462 propagates the error with '?'.","kind":"comment","references":"04160d91ba261c333a0ad4ffedb33bf2f980d141e0f5184027a717a523bb9464","summary":"confirmed: delete_zero_version_artifacts leaves watches rows, so a zero-version live page with a scope watch fails the artifacts DELETE on its foreign key","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:18.844451Z","id":"e00544a1765b9f4c29e011c5abb978670bc3e88676a7ca5ceb0e0d21381e37bd","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:1027 calls self.check_quota(...) and the INSERT runs in a later self.with_tx at 1028-1036; crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs:98 does the same before its INSERT at forks.rs:175. check_quota (crates/clax-store/src/github.rs:312-342) uses self.with_read to COUNT(*) the person's non-deleted artifacts, and create_artifact_async takes no per-person lock between the two, so two concurrent creates at max_artifacts - 1 both pass.","kind":"comment","references":"2ad79590adb495d372f3c59723d4aa2d25346590a327813cb56d04a8930e47f3","summary":"confirmed: the cap is counted in a separate read before the inserting transaction, in both create and fork","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:18.844997Z","id":"160e71c143dfed3d534f70e0d52cb81809b7bc0fffed50f1dd7a0c25741e780c","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/assets.rs:176 checks get_artifact (live_artifact_in, artifacts.rs:203-210, filters deleted_at) in its own read; assets.rs:189 put_asset and 190-192 INSERT INTO assets follow with no lock_content and no liveness re-check. delete_artifact_async (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:368-455) holds lock_content across its mark and content.delete_artifact, does not delete assets rows, and only logs a failure of the content removal. get_asset (assets.rs:219-229) has no deleted filter, and the /_blob handler (crates/clax-server/src/routes/assets.rs:158-194) checks only SeesLive before asset_bytes_async, so bytes put after the removal are served.","kind":"comment","references":"55d8463c9bfe0ac7f1bade1f51cd6a25f354d63b3e5d818df8e4e2946a33de9d","summary":"confirmed: add_asset checks liveness outside its transaction and without lock_content, so it can race delete_artifact_async's content removal","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:18.845553Z","id":"802c5998c021c2ed544c6cee84a0da0dc7bc8ff7937f3a84b631d85d7eeabca9","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs:529-533 calls question_changed only for rows with in_terminal; questions.rs:1097-1108 (withdraw_hook_questions_on_start) never calls it; close_question calls it on every close (questions.rs:1001-1002). The inbox listener is fed only by the update hook on inbox_items (crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:307-321), which QUESTION_TOUCH (crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:585-586, run at inbox.rs:1233) fires. One part overstates: for a withdrawn question with no answers, answered_text (inbox.rs:1163-1176) equals question_text, so the inbox_fts text would not change either way; the missing change signal and the inconsistency with close_question stand.","kind":"comment","references":"e52804edf2a474d42e4400b7da6a76ebc01e6a3e7a2160242a51ec385a9bcbf1","summary":"confirmed: session-end and daemon-start withdrawals skip inbox::question_changed for non-terminal questions, so no inbox change is signalled","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:18.846112Z","id":"44fa646cae5acd5665ae61d3601c86e7d9effe2b563252b67b228aae318db4fe","body":{"detail":"Schema from crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:380-401 (questions_by_status ON questions(status, created_at, id)) in sqlite3 :memory:, then 'EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN SELECT id FROM questions WHERE thread_id = ? AND status = 'open' ORDER BY id' prints 'SEARCH questions USING INDEX questions_by_status (status=?)' and 'USE TEMP B-TREE FOR ORDER BY'. Closed questions, the part that grows forever, are never visited; the cost is bounded by open questions. What does hold: the UPDATE at crates/clax-store/src/site.rs:706-709 ('UPDATE questions SET artifact_id = ?2 WHERE thread_id = ?1') plans as 'SCAN questions' with the same schema, and neither query is in plans.rs question_queries() (plans.rs:562); that site.rs scan, run on thread moves, is a separate, smaller concern.","kind":"comment","references":"c453957c1c869106adfbec22ce5620e54a5cfa63c4181114d65cd8c6caa2964f","summary":"refuted: open_questions_in_thread does not scan the whole table: SQLite walks only open rows through questions_by_status","tags":["verified:refuted","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:18.846634Z","id":"bfc0a571fd89e28b0d838c95a553c461b88513fbcfdd1061ef90223618a6a29f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:749 reads links_of_remote with its own read before self.with_tx at 754; the INSERT INTO linked_threads at 776-781 has unlinked_at NULL and nothing in the transaction re-reads remote_links (the threads_since subquery at 761-762 falls back to l.created_at via COALESCE when the link row is gone). mirror_thread (linked.rs:530-598) checks only artifact_live before inserting linked_threads at 564-581. unlink_remote (linked.rs:466-482) marks unlinked_at only on rows existing at its commit. The comment query at linked.rs:808-814 filters by lt.remote_id, lt.artifact_id and unlinked_at IS NULL only, so a later relink to the same remote picks the stale rows up.","kind":"comment","references":"a2967b618a2d4b830469a252f3348d3ccdac0818d576bd10e6cc431afdd8c7c0","summary":"confirmed: scan_linked and mirror_thread write linked_threads from a link read outside their transaction, never re-checking remote_links","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:18.847183Z","id":"b46dcfa572232d998a847a8c8dce030db9d783c9973747c9322ea1405c68374c","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:1386-1396 comment_key is a with_read; record_comment_key (linked.rs:1400-1415) is its own with_tx with INSERT OR IGNORE. crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:745 checks the key in one store_call; the thread is created later and the key recorded after it at threads.rs:894-895; the comment path records at threads.rs:1152-1153 after the comment is written. Two concurrent requests both miss the key, and a failure between the write and record_comment_key leaves an unkeyed thread or comment.","kind":"comment","references":"b8ab72608f6012889aabb83bc1419dd84ee1f8a93e0a3b3b525b4e0d625e5dcd","summary":"confirmed: comment_keys is checked and recorded in transactions separate from the thread or comment write it keys","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:18.847992Z","id":"843c16b977b3b2df7b67e94a70a411822f3f2d1c03574a711a86272c95490262","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/live.rs:1047-1049 doc says each page watch removed records its own event; the main loop does (live.rs:1106-1124, artifact_watch_record(AuditKind::WatchStop, ...)). The loop over 'others' at live.rs:1143-1152 runs a plain 'DELETE FROM watches ... source = 'scope'' and pushes to removed with no record_audit call.","kind":"comment","references":"c6aabc94859c56db6d88ba500a29052ef4757603eb6248947cdf49d0d364b2be","summary":"confirmed: the 'others' loop in live_unwatch deletes scope-made watches without recording watch.stop","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:18.848580Z","id":"7f8870a8189e5b92858fdd450cebd35b5dc9f7b783dc1c269df49a5f94d75c79","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs:585-594 publish_key is a with_read; record_publish_key (remotes.rs:599-608) is its own with_tx with INSERT OR IGNORE. crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:413-424 (create) calls replayed() then create_artifact_async and only afterwards record_publish_key; artifacts.rs:772-800 (publish) does the same around publish_version_async. Nothing serialises two requests with the same key between the check and the record, and an error after the version commits leaves it unkeyed, contrary to the module doc at remotes.rs:24-27.","kind":"comment","references":"80a4f01bb15e055072d5ba9e0c67e9d91c2ef154177b08a5e78167d7ef08a9f7","summary":"confirmed: publish keys are looked up and recorded outside the transaction that makes the artifact or version","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:41.673323Z","id":"78dd23e7c4283560c30a4bef9dbbab7731c97b11e2ceef6fb0790dce12db04b3","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Refuted by reply 44fa646cae5acd5665ae61d3601c86e7d9effe2b563252b67b228aae318db4fe: EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN shows the query walks only open rows through questions_by_status.","supersedes":"c453957c1c869106adfbec22ce5620e54a5cfa63c4181114d65cd8c6caa2964f","tags":["reason:invalid","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:58.834264Z","id":"1c9d2fc2fcbaaf78cb10efee608bed9d34120d2e89ca4efb8e706dc7be2ed91b","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:307-327 installs update_hook (pushes every inbox_items change, dedupes approval_requests by rowid) and rollback_hook (clears both lists); lib.rs:521-522 also clears them when with_tx begins and lib.rs:534-535 takes them after commit, with no path that drops entries undone by ROLLBACK TO. `grep -rn 'SAVEPOINT\\|ROLLBACK TO\\|savepoint(' crates/clax-store/src` finds only backfill.rs:541/558, which runs in Store::assemble before the hooks (lib.rs:297 vs 307). inbox_items.seq is `INTEGER PRIMARY KEY` without AUTOINCREMENT (migrations.rs:897, 1424), so a rolled-back seq can be reused. No current failure, as the finding says.","kind":"comment","references":"f3deee1549760876d0e5033484bb0804cfc4d8f270b273c15c20e40fca17337d","summary":"confirmed: the change lists are cleared only by the rollback hook and at the start of with_tx, so a savepoint rollback inside a committed transaction would leak phantom seqs; latent today, suggestion is the right kind","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:58.834899Z","id":"14cf733c84b8dc262654229641e47e09a76c30c84e2ed76a0025d28f6e87c8e5","body":{"detail":"Every commit that ever added `CREATE TABLE session_elevations` to migration 24 (086356acb, ac3ee2d4f, 480d9987a, 5bb5cf264; `git log --all -S 'CREATE TABLE session_elevations'`) removes `ALTER TABLE sessions ADD COLUMN elevate_json TEXT` and adds `CREATE UNIQUE INDEX session_elevations_key` in the same migration text (`git show <c> -- '*migrations.rs' | grep session_elevations`). So a database with elevate_json was migrated by a copy that never made session_elevations: REPAIR_TABLES (migrations.rs:1287) makes it empty, and the loop at migrations.rs:1551-1568 inserts one row per sessions.id, a primary key, so no duplicate (session_id, NULL granter) can arise before REPAIR_INDEXES (migrations.rs:1457) makes the index. A database that has session_elevations got the index with it and has no elevate_json, so the branch does not run. Reordering would be harmless but fixes no reachable state.","kind":"comment","references":"ffd232e74ce1887d93c07e16c4cdb36ab4ef78963a32982f29359db1bf8d50f4","summary":"refuted: no database can hold both sessions.elevate_json and a session_elevations table without its unique index, and a freshly made table cannot get duplicates from the move","tags":["verified:refuted","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:58.835427Z","id":"7b892e094f2e2d26bed56e67c6688ddf9a076a2a8ef1720abc0db58408286c9b","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1586-1590: the `///` block directly above `fn legacy_viewer_cookies` opens 'Mints the install ID once: 128 random bits in lowercase hex. It holds no timestamp, …' and then 'Keeps every existing viewer's cookie…'; `fn install_id` at migrations.rs:1607 has no `///` lines above it.","kind":"comment","references":"260fe64542ac9839ccb8d720599fb577ec9f0d1bdabde2819b8e4940891476f2","summary":"confirmed: the install-ID doc sentences sit at the top of legacy_viewer_cookies' doc comment and install_id has no doc comment","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:58.835887Z","id":"7da19d28d9e361a1fbe60e3cb38295e287f1973dd5bcbdde2fe41d07740e8aab","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs:430-435: hosted_needs_setup() is a separate read, then `self.set_owner_name(name, true)?` runs, which is its own with_tx doing `UPDATE viewers SET display_name` (crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs:700-712); only afterwards does hosted.rs:436-442 run the setup transaction whose `INSERT OR IGNORE INTO hosted_setup` returning 0 yields NotFound, and its revoke_in/signed_in steps can also fail after the rename has committed. A second caller exists: github_sign_in's owner path calls hosted_setup_via, retrying with user.login on name_taken/invalid_name (crates/clax-store/src/github.rs:199-207).","kind":"comment","references":"cbc488f75583cf92188b7cc4b1129cf3c9caaf1c2548b624dd1a0f4b165d93fe","summary":"confirmed: the owner rename commits in its own transaction before the setup transaction's INSERT OR IGNORE decides who set up, so a losing or failing setup still renames the owner","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:58.836326Z","id":"33e905f1689f7e0c76ffb1dd0edf0e282df5769d6cb3f00f37f7ce811fb3377e","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs:337-414 updates sessions/artifacts/versions/assets person, invites, grants, authorship, comments, mentions, threads.resolved_by, viewer_seen, viewer_threads, private docs and cookies, then `DELETE FROM viewers`; none of the tables with a viewer_id column made at migrations.rs:774-790 (hosted_setup, browser_sessions, signin_links), 939-941 (github_identities), 956-963 (artifact_shares viewer_id, created_by) or 1172-1177 (legal_agreements) appears. fold's only callers are claim_for_owner (viewers.rs:763, 776), which returns Claim::Nothing unless the cookie's viewer is non-person and minted_local (viewers.rs:745-757), reached from crates/clax-server/src/routes/token.rs:62. The invariant that those rows are empty is not asserted anywhere; suggestion is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"29bc565de9f2f998b8d4f4fda83d6b60435a2f437f4dbf45d1a742487be578f7","summary":"confirmed: fold() does not touch browser_sessions, signin_links, github_identities, artifact_shares, legal_agreements or hosted_setup; safe today only because its callers fold minted-local non-person or unclaimed CLI owner rows","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:58.836769Z","id":"d67eec272ae4b03ee39f9e2f73ad2dc4fca9bc17a712dbf39b652762051a4e23","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs:331-346: share_artifact returns already_owner for a GitHub login only when github_identities already links it to the owner (`Some((_, true))`); with no link it stores a waiting share (`None => (None, Some(login))`). github_sign_in's owner path then calls `link(tx, &self.now(), user, &owner.id)` (crates/clax-store/src/github.rs:229), and link (github.rs:131-141) calls bind_github_shares, which at shares.rs:192-231 runs `UPDATE artifact_shares SET viewer_id = ?2` with no check of viewers.owner. SHARE_SELECT (shares.rs:233-235) then lists that row with the owner's public ID.","kind":"comment","references":"c6b2c70b37f45e9f9cebb159eb42cc4767b2513f50c0a8df07a1a2cec528a774","summary":"confirmed: bind_github_shares binds a waiting share to whatever row the login links to, the owner's included, though share_artifact refuses the owner","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:58.837205Z","id":"190ffa9d7a2ba8671d5743f78870101c3b4da703e4bd3220676ec7dba2730511","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs:1736-1775 (delete_thread_rows) deletes version_threads, live_pending, mentions, viewer_threads, feedback, batch_threads, thread_moves, page_authors, comments, threads and withdraws approval requests, but nothing from linked_threads/linked_comments/linked_outbox; linked_threads has no foreign key (migrations.rs:1001-1015). The delete route has no linked guard (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs:1716-1726). In crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs mirror(), linked_thread_by_remote (line 1491) finds the row with unlinked_at NULL; a new remote comment reaches Store::mirror_comment, whose `thread_in(tx, tid)?.ok_or(CoreError::NotFound)` (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:624) fails, and even with no new comment `st.get_thread(&tid)?.ok_or(NotFound)` (server linked.rs:1538) does. The error maps to Stop::Unreachable (server linked.rs:238-241) and read() returns at `self.mirror(l, rt).await?` (line 1422) before set_sync_cursor (1427), so the same thread is re-read and fails each cycle. The Failure line names concrete inputs a user hits; blocker kind stands.","kind":"comment","references":"3bc9d44f895ae70a36c4ee1e5d43e933f0c8026eb8eb1a6c01a75b4aa1d7c6f8","summary":"confirmed: deleting a mirrored thread leaves its live linked_threads row, and the next read of that remote thread errors with NotFound, aborting read() before the sync cursor moves on every cycle","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:58.837687Z","id":"52394ab065c7b8a956e34d950c50512347fecf91e1a4089d5c97da701520aff5","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/site.rs:674-711 (the `p.from != to.artifact_id` branch) updates version_threads, PENDING_TO, PICKS_TO/LEFT, watches, inbox::thread_moved, questions and sessions.delivered_artifact_id; `grep -n approval_requests crates/clax-store/src/site.rs crates/clax-store/src/joined.rs` prints nothing. REQUEST_STATE (crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs:145-152) filters `artifact_id = ?2`, the open lookup (approvals.rs:1088-1096) `artifact_id = ?3`, and withdraw_artifact_in (approvals.rs:1449-1466) withdraws by artifact_id, so a moved thread's request is missed at its new page and withdrawn with the old one.","kind":"comment","references":"3604d6f60cfbf480efcf3de48cec233a0b91dd48b27c7200669019b848271926","summary":"confirmed: commit_refile carries questions, inbox items, watches and pending rows of a moved thread but not its approval_requests, which stay on the old artifact_id that REQUEST_STATE and the open-request lookup filter by","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:03:18.132636Z","id":"b774d56da17f115afd307cf9c156f3c2b2c6aeec2dccceeb2cff915332519690","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Refuted by reply 14cf733c84b8dc262654229641e47e09a76c30c84e2ed76a0025d28f6e87c8e5: no reachable database holds elevate_json alongside a session_elevations table lacking its unique index.","supersedes":"ffd232e74ce1887d93c07e16c4cdb36ab4ef78963a32982f29359db1bf8d50f4","tags":["reason:invalid","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:05:25.580240Z","id":"376160a6afe8ab8bed18d7fab0f9aa2963dbb3250f7d1f1db6c0c3e69cb3c99e","body":{"detail":"inbox_groups groups all of a query's matches (GROUP BY artifact over the driver's walk, with a temporary B-tree; crates/clax-store/src/plans.rs allows it for the ' groups' shapes) so each group's total and unread are exact across pages, then reads each listed group's newest rows by inbox_by_artifact. The unread section reads only unread items (inbox_unread); the read section, unfolded, reads the recipient's whole read history. The route runs it in the bulk lane (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs list). Accepted: an inbox of tens of thousands of items groups in milliseconds, and the read section loads only when unfolded.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1569},"end":{"line":1623},"content_hash":"4cfd4b762e797f59ddf3b3d533f96188190c6dc698bea35078e50abd6aed2c34"},"summary":"Grouping the inbox by artifact reads every match to count each group","tags":["inbox","perf","revisit:a group=artifact read over 50 ms in just perf, or inboxes past 100k items","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:23:32.343289Z","id":"4a267f9970eceabb4a6868e84e90a3b00f518c9862042a99fbf20269ca99fc51","body":{"detail":"inbox_groups reads each listed group's rows with page_on over a copy of the query with `artifact` (or `no_artifact`) set. driver() (line 333) puts the unread filter ahead of the artifact one, so for read=unread (every load of /inbox, web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte fetchGroups) each of up to 20 (at most 100) per-group statements walks inbox_unread from the newest unread item, testing artifact_id as a residual, until it finds rows+1 of that artifact. A group whose items are older than most unread items scans nearly all of them. The waiver 376160a6af covers the one GROUP BY pass, not these per-group walks. inbox_by_artifact (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:923) is (recipient, artifact_id, seq) and would reach each group's rows directly with read_at as a residual.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1611},"end":{"line":1620},"content_hash":"df1c740c09b1b9f7d95a237924d06ecd5ef9c4845cd9e803e1a6267e19a50dff"},"suggested_fix":"Let the per-group statement drive by inbox_by_artifact when an artifact (or no_artifact) is set even under read=unread, e.g. a driver override for this call, and add its shape to shapes() so plans.rs checks it.","summary":"Each unread group's rows walk the whole unread index: a page of groups costs groups x unread items","tags":["review","review:inbox-by-artifact","inbox","perf","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:26:04.630084Z","id":"a1570f4196a8f4c57c6dd86f409b0b1e54d0caa688da254ac4616a6de5e360d8","body":{"detail":"inbox_groups (crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:1611-1620) runs page_on for each group with artifact/no_artifact set and ..q.clone() (read kept). driver() (line 334) returns Driver::Unread whenever q.read == ReadFilter::Unread, before the artifact check at line 336; Driver::Unread.index() is inbox_unread (line 304), and build() emits INDEXED BY for the driver and a `+` (residual) on the others. inbox_unread is (COALESCE(recipient,''), seq) WHERE read_at IS NULL (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:921), while inbox_by_artifact is (COALESCE(recipient,''), artifact_id, seq) (line 923). So each group's walk scans unread items newest-first until rows+1 of that artifact are found.","kind":"comment","references":"4a267f9970eceabb4a6868e84e90a3b00f518c9862042a99fbf20269ca99fc51","summary":"confirmed: per-group row statements under read=unread are forced onto inbox_unread, artifact as a residual","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:21:40.755951Z","id":"796273c3370ae49096fe572050218ad411a66e2241b99911ebe02bd38872d6eb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:961c77551","summary":"Fixed: Shape::GroupRows drives a group's rows by inbox_by_artifact whatever the read filter; shapes() adds ' group rows' for every named query, so plans::every_inbox_query_still_uses_an_index checks each plan, and groups_by_artifact_with_counts_across_pages asserts the Artifact driver for unread and no-artifact rows. //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test passes.","supersedes":"4a267f9970eceabb4a6868e84e90a3b00f518c9862042a99fbf20269ca99fc51","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:18:34.991584Z","id":"667322034aa18ec85de9c7ee90b05e461263d1f7ebb4cb7c2f849837e3d8e2fa","body":{"detail":"linked_threads (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1001-1015) and linked_outbox (migrations.rs:1034-1048) key a thread's link to a remote on artifact_id, and crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs reads them by it (enqueue at linked.rs:312-322, the artifact_live check at linked.rs:554). The `p.from != to.artifact_id` branch of commit_refile updates neither, so a linked thread moved by a merge, un-merge, owner move or join keeps naming its old page there. Whether it matters depends on whether a live page's artifact can be linked to a remote at all (no check in crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs refuses one), and on what a moved twin should do on the remote, whose remote_artifact_id stays the old page's: carrying artifact_id alone could sync the thread into the wrong remote artifact. Left for whoever owns linked.rs to decide: carry the rows, unlink the moved thread, or refuse moving a linked thread.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":704},"end":{"line":717},"content_hash":"d95498756bb27bbe7bec46899b7b10df78451c579860ff3581557558b8baca30"},"summary":"commit_refile carries a moved thread's questions and approval_requests to its new page, but not its linked_threads.artifact_id or linked_outbox.artifact_id rows","tags":["review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:18:34.992804Z","id":"bc42705147fcac8c5d7e7b8487f48e78103055c2bec7e8d6558526928fdfe79f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs give_untargeted_in drops the untargeted rows whose comment the session already has a row for, then retargets the rest and clears notified_at and push_failed_at; send_in, Store::send_to_named and Store::handoff call it. take_in (crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs:373-384) runs the same DELETE and UPDATE inline and uses the UPDATE's row count. The two copies agree today; a change to one (another column to clear) must be made to both. Replace the inline statements with `let given = super::feedback::give_untargeted_in(tx, tid, sid)?;`.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":373},"end":{"line":384},"content_hash":"6f5b99d693ea01dfc1e37ad2cf5dbf4bcf2e6a2d5c9c05148139cde083373a35"},"summary":"take_in hands a thread's untargeted rows to the taker with its own copy of feedback::give_untargeted_in's two statements","tags":["review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:14:01.397176Z","id":"c0da85cc6c8debfb96bf49a1257aec50f6004ee9f53c77ac970d74c5781de9cc","body":{"detail":"linked_threads (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1001-1015) and linked_outbox (migrations.rs:1034-1048) key a thread's link to a remote on artifact_id, and crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs reads them by it (enqueue at linked.rs:312-322, the artifact_live check at linked.rs:554). The `p.from != to.artifact_id` branch of commit_refile updates neither, so a linked thread moved by a merge, un-merge, owner move or join keeps naming its old page there. Whether it matters depends on whether a live page's artifact can be linked to a remote at all (no check in crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs refuses one), and on what a moved twin should do on the remote, whose remote_artifact_id stays the old page's: carrying artifact_id alone could sync the thread into the wrong remote artifact. Left for whoever owns linked.rs to decide: carry the rows, unlink the moved thread, or refuse moving a linked thread.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":704},"end":{"line":717},"content_hash":"d95498756bb27bbe7bec46899b7b10df78451c579860ff3581557558b8baca30"},"summary":"commit_refile carries a moved thread's questions and approval_requests to its new page, but not its linked_threads.artifact_id or linked_outbox.artifact_id rows","supersedes":"667322034aa18ec85de9c7ee90b05e461263d1f7ebb4cb7c2f849837e3d8e2fa","tags":["review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:14:01.519111Z","id":"fb8191847ca1c8211a2d6233d1660203bf2bcda82737bebbacba3a8c68d486da","body":{"detail":"`UPDATE questions SET artifact_id = ?2 WHERE thread_id = ?1` (crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs MOVE_THREAD, run here for every thread commit_refile moves to another page) plans as 'SCAN questions' against the schema of crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs; the EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN evidence is in reply 44fa646cae5acd5665ae61d3601c86e7d9effe2b563252b67b228aae318db4fe. Closed questions are kept, so the scan grows with every question ever asked. The fix is a migration adding the partial index `CREATE INDEX questions_by_thread ON questions(thread_id, id) WHERE thread_id IS NOT NULL` plus a question_queries() entry in crates/clax-store/src/plans.rs requiring it for MOVE_THREAD (and the index in the list migration_20_adds_questions_to_a_19_database checks). It waits for the migration numbers 39-43 that the unmerged flutter-app branch already uses on installed databases to land on main, so this index takes the next free number after them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":706},"end":{"line":709},"content_hash":"f20544708c3ba8518feddc5697d44cb34ed2a1aa7e34f08ebe3c5143b60f93f6"},"summary":"Moving a thread's questions (questions::MOVE_THREAD) plans as SCAN questions: questions.thread_id has no index","tags":["review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","revisit:after-flutter-app-migrations","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:20:51.915682Z","id":"271893ca1e80c74a28cf90870ab015a0a06cbd6a5013386acd688215402549ce","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5c173fc87","summary":"Fixed: feedback::give_untargeted_in drops untargeted rows the agent already has before retargeting; send_in, send_to_named and handoff use it. feedback::ownership::a_send_naming_an_agent_that_already_has_the_comment_drops_its_untargeted_row and a_mention_… pass (failed before with the UNIQUE error). threads.rs take_in's duplicate statements are concern bc427051.","supersedes":"ec9ae232c212514a566830fec4df3cb14343a464f1372bdb27c87ba16e041831","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:20:51.942848Z","id":"426310bb8e49f0179633505caf80b6ad5535ea10e3a8100483b19ca27b9c0246","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1351277fa","summary":"Fixed: acknowledge_where rebuilds a stale view inside its write transaction (Visibility::for_reader_in); feedback::delivery::an_acknowledge_under_a_view_older_than_a_revocation_marks_nothing_delivered passes.","supersedes":"517b3e30ac5e9a733de52cb2ffb8a28d8a88703243af459aef029f54cde89f28","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:20:51.969832Z","id":"01ef67e1d352631708fe2b5c01f65043a7960e3497f9d52fc34e0aca70cf6ea5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e72a5185f","summary":"Fixed: REQUEST_STATE ends a decline once a later approval covering the thread is made or revoked, as DECLINES does (quiet window and held_without_request follow in 2b6b86ed2); approvals::tests::a_decline_ends_for_the_request_state_once_an_approval_is_made_or_revoked_after_it and an_approval_and_revocation_after_a_decline_end_its_quiet_window pass.","supersedes":"da9843eba8b3f5d3ebfd1c1182383317dfdb9101758afc636b75be8dfe0a76aa","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:20:51.996867Z","id":"4c9cae6b898524f30adad151ac3775db8f2c43a3d5e03fef7bb1d26cad74088f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f696693f5","summary":"Fixed: decide_request's doc says it drops each place held without a request, then the marker once none are left.","supersedes":"f2ce08a5b0c74a558ba6a1001e944866d3e0aff589a9be0602e563082ce5a76a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:20:52.022366Z","id":"9034e159ef562ab0b8018ea57eef9645922b33a79774f4a75236ca74d66c03b8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2e16fb279","summary":"Fixed: session-end and daemon-start withdrawals touch every withdrawn question's inbox item; questions::tests::session_end_and_daemon_start_withdrawals_touch_the_inbox_items passes.","supersedes":"e52804edf2a474d42e4400b7da6a76ebc01e6a3e7a2160242a51ec385a9bcbf1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/live.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:20:52.048807Z","id":"860a0e4937f05b5b334b5cb42adae85159404fffa0746a770a7ab2235ddb7cfc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5bc8f3a20","summary":"Fixed: removing a scope-made watch on a split-off origin records watch.stop; joined::tests::removing_a_scope_removes_what_it_made_on_an_origin_split_off asserts the stop event and passes.","supersedes":"c6aabc94859c56db6d88ba500a29052ef4757603eb6248947cdf49d0d364b2be","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:20:52.076736Z","id":"2440f6be44a2e3d3946bd9cfee68dc94b7a0faa161dd24369f3ee3f63e8ee806","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ee9b0adb7","summary":"Fixed: commit_refile carries a thread's approval_requests to its new page; site::tests::a_moved_threads_approval_requests_follow_it passes. linked_threads/linked_outbox on a move are concern c0da85cc (needs-decision).","supersedes":"3604d6f60cfbf480efcf3de48cec233a0b91dd48b27c7200669019b848271926","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T17:59:30.442707Z","id":"7e42a85e24331698ce4b905339788f88bf5cd1da5b0976c059b5bd91af5d0d31","body":{"detail":"Store::lock_publish_key (crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs:608-614) holds an in-memory lock (ArtifactLocks::lock_key), so it serialises same-key publishes within one Store only. Across two processes on one database, both miss the key in replayed() (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs), and the second's version transaction fails in record_publish_key_in (remotes.rs:622-641) with publish_key_used instead of replaying the first's version. For a create, create_artifact_async (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs) has already committed the artifacts row at current_version 0 in its own transaction, so that row stays until clax doctor --fix removes it (delete_zero_version_artifacts). A hosted daemon is one process today, so no current path hits it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":602},"end":{"line":641},"content_hash":"1fc7be8b9f638e9afa128a6681864a168c04fa9b2e2f17068803e18c0d00d0de"},"suggested_fix":"If a hosted instance ever runs more than one process on one database, have the routes answer publish_key_used by re-running replayed(), and have create_artifact_async remove its own zero-version row when its version transaction fails.","summary":"The publish-key lock is per Store: two processes publishing with the same key fail the second with publish_key_used, and a create leaves a zero-version artifact","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:38:03.469124Z","id":"029e7a62f2c2d8e8fafe53e062a4b6c6790ba66b1559f0afec210e561a4766e2","body":{"detail":"Store::lock_publish_key (crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs:608-614) holds an in-memory lock (ArtifactLocks::lock_key), so it serialises same-key publishes within one Store only. Across two processes on one database, both miss the key in replayed() (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs), and the second's version transaction fails in record_publish_key_in (remotes.rs:625-648) with publish_key_used, which the route returns as an error instead of the first's version. A failed create removes its own artifact row (create_artifact_async, crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs), so nothing is left behind. A hosted daemon is one process today, so no current path hits it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":602},"end":{"line":648},"content_hash":"63d3066b26a8e8478b2ba46113e3099f304e686d8d6e4246318fbd6cf4c55be1"},"suggested_fix":"If a hosted instance ever runs more than one process on one database, have the routes answer publish_key_used by re-running replayed().","summary":"The publish-key lock is per Store: of two processes publishing with the same key at once, the second fails with publish_key_used instead of replaying","supersedes":"7e42a85e24331698ce4b905339788f88bf5cd1da5b0976c059b5bd91af5d0d31","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:45:21.119438Z","id":"43829cb353427ea4a52e3946784c3577abff12dcf1e67c9811f2ebc394461c9c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7185a16c9","summary":"Fixed: the member cap is counted inside the transaction that inserts the artifact (create and fork, BEGIN IMMEDIATE); github::tests::a_create_racing_another_never_takes_a_member_past_the_cap and a_fork_racing_a_create_… pass (failed before).","supersedes":"2ad79590adb495d372f3c59723d4aa2d25346590a327813cb56d04a8930e47f3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:45:21.154486Z","id":"a9079f961f814876e023c254b19a99c2af86b687ae1a449add9a215ed5976ba8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fc8f56157","summary":"Fixed: a zero-version delete also removes the artifact's watches, merged/pending/pick page rows, doc_authors and its assets' page_authors; artifacts::tests::a_zero_version_page_goes_with_its_watches_and_page_rows passes (FOREIGN KEY error before).","supersedes":"04160d91ba261c333a0ad4ffedb33bf2f980d141e0f5184027a717a523bb9464","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:45:21.190155Z","id":"9aa1f04e778c2c4588b1ef7d74abcfc9742e7f01790b7eada0f234a1b5471992","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d67ff072b","summary":"Fixed (d67ff072b, e63bcff63): upload checks liveness, writes bytes and inserts under the artifact's content lock with a re-check in the transaction; get_asset returns None for a deleted artifact. assets::tests::an_upload_racing_the_artifacts_delete_stores_nothing (fails without the re-check) and a_deleted_artifacts_assets_are_not_found pass.","supersedes":"55d8463c9bfe0ac7f1bade1f51cd6a25f354d63b3e5d818df8e4e2946a33de9d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:45:21.230654Z","id":"4891eea6f87484239209f71a16713ed97ceddf6ba97e77e1a39da29222b2a9ca","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:81603375a","summary":"Fixed (8cfa9c661, 81603375a): the Idempotency-Key is recorded in the version's own transaction under a per-key lock, a dead artifact's key is taken over, and a failed create removes its own row; remotes::tests a_publish_key_is_recorded_with_the_version_it_made, a_publish_key_is_held_by_one_publish_at_a_time, a_publish_key_whose_artifact_was_deleted_makes_a_new_one, a_create_whose_key_is_taken_leaves_no_artifact pass. Cross-process replay is concern 029e7a62.","supersedes":"80a4f01bb15e055072d5ba9e0c67e9d91c2ef154177b08a5e78167d7ef08a9f7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:45:21.272071Z","id":"b84ffd309cde4f0eafa6fcb0c6366dc482c967caafa9ac6d07b775a1ebda81e4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d04e2eae6","summary":"Fixed: the owner is named inside the hosted setup transaction after its INSERT OR IGNORE wins; hosted::tests::a_setup_that_loses_the_race_leaves_the_owner_named_by_the_winner passes.","supersedes":"cbc488f75583cf92188b7cc4b1129cf3c9caaf1c2548b624dd1a0f4b165d93fe","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:45:21.318125Z","id":"e202ac7f14181808518982514d18f65a027b5f2df8842ef5e7db9d03591135fd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d491ed84e","summary":"Fixed: the connect-time approval is made in the same transaction as its grant checks; people::tests::a_grant_revoked_while_answering_makes_no_approval passes.","supersedes":"f707bd244b6ca7359470e5895ed33fc52a0e6e241592bebd294541137f2d7168","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:45:21.367828Z","id":"a7034d07b0d0e802f65ee9181e678cc0e7d77e4dab32d8ecbcd331864e77693a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7d81f623e","summary":"Fixed: with_tx gives the inbox listener one change per seq whatever savepoints undid; inbox::tests::a_seq_reused_after_a_savepoint_rollback_is_heard_once passes (failed before).","supersedes":"f3deee1549760876d0e5033484bb0804cfc4d8f270b273c15c20e40fca17337d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:09:27.356786Z","id":"ec3e72bf288017bec48256d06abae1517a28a65abc483ae6bb2604882a5ae4a4","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1363-1368, record 0118687f.\n\nconnection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1500},"end":{"line":1505},"content_hash":"c1c86e26871ba066020c75f1d9b1b954ee91add027a8fb30f98694a07930d59d"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","supersedes":"0c155fcd8e655a7c43a62957f3e932a2edfb616520d5bb95bf78b5a0579db831","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:09:27.622455Z","id":"2569592d7a43b723d8aa14af64c57f7317ae0e4255cdb9d940d5179170650f5e","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1552-1556, record 6014047e.\n\nnote_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1744},"end":{"line":1748},"content_hash":"df46c2781c4e06aa0fe53e6fadd564b9bcbcad9e060403b47de165ac7d60413a"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","supersedes":"1633743c8a4457821492d2020d40038c1e265dd77dcbce8d60462a827c5176cb","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:09:27.813791Z","id":"6ed23feb51e1ef78b17f848bc62f9510bda808c76d9c2d3966a6f732b6115ef7","body":{"detail":"The doc block above legacy_viewer_cookies opens with 'Mints the install ID once: 128 random bits in lowercase hex…', which describes install_id (migrations.rs:1607), then goes on to describe the legacy cookies. rustdoc and editors show the install-ID text on the wrong function, and install_id is undocumented.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1597},"end":{"line":1619},"content_hash":"58340413419b701cf7c1e51846d980fe3ae18a6c79b36ddbc45681e2bfd4482d"},"suggested_fix":"Move the first two sentences ('Mints the install ID once … does not date the install.') to a doc comment on install_id, leaving legacy_viewer_cookies' doc to start at 'Keeps every existing viewer's cookie'.","summary":"install_id's doc comment is attached to legacy_viewer_cookies, and install_id has none","supersedes":"260fe64542ac9839ccb8d720599fb577ec9f0d1bdabde2819b8e4940891476f2","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/briefs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:29:04.701993Z","id":"753d564300b322b163bac8ed1835ef067957b1a491910f9f6dd6feceba95abf2","body":{"detail":"publish_keys (crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs record_publish_key_in) is keyed by an agent token's grant_id and records the version a publish made, in the version's own transaction (ValidatedPublish::publish_key). A brief's key belongs to a person's public ID or the owner (*owner), has no grant, answers the artifact, version 1 and the brief thread, and its briefs row also names the starter for the 'started from a brief by' line, so briefs keeps both in one row. It follows publish_keys' rules: the request holds the key's lock from look-up to record (Store::lock_brief_key), a key whose artifact is not live is taken over (record_brief), and an artifact whose key cannot be recorded is deleted (create_from_brief in crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs). It differs in one way: the key is recorded in its own transaction after the version and thread, not in the version's.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":8},"content_hash":"63148fd9005a95a3884fc8bb4385be1897506f0c446c3459ead5924527377b69"},"summary":"Keep a brief's Idempotency-Key in publish_keys (the agent-token publish keys) instead of briefs.key","tags":["revisit:publish keys are opened to browser persons, or briefs come from more than one daemon process on one database","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/briefs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:29:04.703061Z","id":"2d0284b930502c5caab1412271c29a8f560d9823bd1120bd9ddee9c5aa1ae81e","body":{"detail":"Store::lock_brief_key holds an in-memory lock (ArtifactLocks::lock_key), as Store::lock_publish_key does (record 029e7a62 on crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs). Across two processes both requests miss the key in brief_by_key; the second's record_brief returns false and create_from_brief (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs) deletes its artifact and answers 400 invalid_args instead of the first's artifact. Nothing is left behind but a soft-deleted artifact. A daemon is one process today, so no current path hits it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":66},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"a1bfc159b9d7fdf1321234918e245cfdfd8046dc5ec9523b0a3c653c1b93f4e5"},"summary":"The brief-key lock is per Store: the same keyed brief sent to a second process on one database is refused, not answered","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:06:14.763506Z","id":"8d50bbe307a0b1ad5e0903c2a8fb2097a58271ac703662d18e6d2e9ded66725b","body":{"detail":"Both options need no schema change (grants.narrow_json already holds a narrowing).\n\nA (recommended): keep the ask as a ceiling. narrowing() (crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:454-458) stores the asked access whenever it is not every right, instead of only when it does not cover the person's current rights; request_grant (people.rs:1115) and approve_grant (people.rs:1297-1301) then keep it, and grant_caller_in gives person-now intersected with the ask. Clients that ask for nothing are unchanged: the grant request route defaults the ask to Rights::full() (crates/clax-server/src/routes/grants.rs:523-526), so `clax connect` grants keep following the person. Only a client that explicitly asked for less is capped at its ask. Side effect: such grants report a `narrow` (Grant.narrow, people.rs:134-136) even while the person's rights sit inside it, so the People page would show them as narrowed from approval on.\n\nB: grants follow the person upward by design. Change no code; state it on narrowing()'s doc comment and in the grant section of the multi-person spec, and say in the approval UI that the client's ask is only applied while it is narrower than the person.\n\nRecommendation: A. A client's explicit ask is the least privilege it said it needs, and the default (no ask) keeps today's behaviour.","kind":"comment","references":"8332718f9ffd0e03ff684a160447439939c4238a9bf4d0319c320eb3cf3ede88","summary":"Decision needed: should an agent grant's effective rights follow its person's later raises past what its client asked for?","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:20:57.493498Z","id":"d6fecf127a99bb8661ebe42347e317b85abae095792469c6b33e1e277f448347","body":{"detail":"github_sign_in's setup branch (crates/clax-store/src/github.rs:207-218) calls hosted_setup_via (crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs:417), which commits the owner row, hosted_setup and the browser session in its own transaction, and only then runs link() in a second with_tx (github.rs:217). If the second transaction fails (a database error, or the process stopping between the two), the instance is set up with an owner row that no GitHub account is linked to: the owner's browser holds a session, but the account's next sign-in is matched only by owner_login, and a share waiting for the owner's login stays unbound until then. The non-setup owner branch (github.rs:220-238) links and signs in within one transaction.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":207},"end":{"line":218},"content_hash":"a7e40809c4592fd958289b70f379e6194cd1b40bc9cfd86f779e33d9fa77852b"},"suggested_fix":"Give hosted_setup_via a variant that runs inside a caller's transaction (or takes a closure run before commit), and call link() in that same transaction, with a test that makes link fail and expects no setup left.","summary":"The first GitHub owner sign-in sets up the instance and links the account in two transactions","tags":["review","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:27:08.722192Z","id":"f3f31806215e6cf1a88f902fba6347f9c9c2395941c4539ea5860f0c1f21c740","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ec1fcf651","summary":"Fixed (doc-only): the install-ID sentences are on fn install_id in crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs; legacy_viewer_cookies keeps only its own doc.","supersedes":"260fe64542ac9839ccb8d720599fb577ec9f0d1bdabde2819b8e4940891476f2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:27:08.749693Z","id":"4b9e43cbd137110a8a203e46e43442a052bffbf99283b9a24c1b4e565d4565b0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:55d076743","summary":"Fixed: the owner's GitHub sign-in drops shares waiting for that login and audits each as artifact.update share {op: remove, reason: owner}; shares::tests::a_login_share_waiting_for_the_owners_account_is_dropped_at_the_owners_sign_in passes (failed before).","supersedes":"c6b2c70b37f45e9f9cebb159eb42cc4767b2513f50c0a8df07a1a2cec528a774","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:27:08.775667Z","id":"6efaf3d48461db1576154f583ffe5aaa931dc831db7c4d47e176336668534dd3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a3a84b767","summary":"Fixed (a3a84b767, d14797576, 041bce39e): fold moves or drops credentials, legal_agreements, device_codes and artifact_shares, promotes into to owner when folding the owner row, and refuses with fold_incomplete if any viewer_id table still names the folded row; viewers::tests every_table_holding_a_viewer_row_is_folded, a_merged_viewers_hosted_rows_move_or_go_and_none_is_left, the_owner_rows_credentials_follow_it_when_a_browser_adopts_it, a_fold_that_leaves_a_row_naming_the_folded_viewer_is_refused_whole, folding_the_owners_row_makes_its_successor_the_owner pass.","supersedes":"29bc565de9f2f998b8d4f4fda83d6b60435a2f437f4dbf45d1a742487be578f7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:22:59.751090Z","id":"190ceb8f24299b14a6fd61d8eff08cd75c40048d3e1fd6e2f75553b595ac618c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ec1fcf651","summary":"Fixed on main: resolve f3f31806 (ec1fcf651) moved the install-ID sentences onto fn install_id; this record was a re-anchor of 260fe645 made before that fix merged.","supersedes":"6ed23feb51e1ef78b17f848bc62f9510bda808c76d9c2d3966a6f732b6115ef7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:08:23.746938Z","id":"54d28037ffbd2f6c0a476f7f4fa2dbdb46156cbb1315a6cd221585738a22754e","body":{"detail":"A group's first rows are its unread matches then its read ones (inbox.rs:1649-1668). Read items R9, R8, R7 and an older unread U5 list as [U5, R9, R8]; after the group's Mark read the reload (InboxPage.svelte:258) lists [R9, R8, R7]: the row just read disappears from view and R7 appears. A live read elsewhere keeps rows in place (takeItem), but the next refetch for any reason reorders them the same way. This works against the rule that Mark read and live reads keep everything in place.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1649},"end":{"line":1668},"content_hash":"b1de6d5b91a86b4c2dbdcf368f6faf5dabc64b34e732ad16c60badf0e9d4d355"},"suggested_fix":"After a group's Mark read, keep its listed rows and mark them read client-side rather than taking the server's reordered rows, or merge the refetched rows into the listed order (listed rows keep their positions, new ones appended).","summary":"A group's rows reorder after Mark read: unread-first rows become newest-first, so rows vanish and others appear in place","tags":["review","review:inbox-one-list","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:08:23.747138Z","id":"8cd1b419752ed66cd4c90fd1b63db05c440511466973be3ac809e62791b17b50","body":{"detail":"The unread part runs page_on with Shape::GroupRows, which driver() (inbox.rs:339-345) always drives by inbox_by_artifact; read_at IS NULL is residual and the LIMIT is rows+1. A group with rows or fewer unread items (the common case: 1 to 3 new) can never fill rows+1, so SQLite walks every item of that artifact for the recipient before stopping, once per group on every page of groups (up to 20, 100 with limit). The Groups shape already reads every match (waiver 376160a6), so this is a second full pass over the listed groups' items rather than a new order of cost. plans.rs checks the GroupRows shape for BY_ARTIFACT_PAGE (read all) and UNREAD_NO_ARTIFACT_PAGE but none with an artifact and read=read.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1650},"end":{"line":1655},"content_hash":"93c860b953ab207089be58f025eb1d7c2f8e72d2d9601eb358f6b058fc740797"},"suggested_fix":"Use the known count: query the unread part with limit min(rows, g.unread) and set more from g.unread > rows, so the walk stops at the last unread item; likewise the read part from g.total - g.unread. Add BY_ARTIFACT unread/read GroupRows shapes to shapes().","summary":"A group's unread rows walk every item of its page when it has few unread ones","tags":["review","review:inbox-one-list","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:10:19.182877Z","id":"1a6e6b23ad29b5537c84450b3cb0759c1e35db170610a4d52f64076cd13d8b27","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:1649-1668 fills a group's rows with page_on(ReadFilter::Unread) first, then the read part. After markUpTo (web/shell/src/q/InboxPage.svelte:253-258) the group has unread 0, so the refetch via load() (list = l, InboxPage.svelte:174) returns only the read part, newest first: an older just-read item that was listed first drops out of the rows and a newer read one takes a slot. The same load() runs on soon() (InboxPage.svelte:284, 299, 307). The page header (InboxPage.svelte:16-21) says items stay where they are as they change. A concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"54d28037ffbd2f6c0a476f7f4fa2dbdb46156cbb1315a6cd221585738a22754e","summary":"confirmed: a group's rows are unread-first, so a refetch after Mark read reorders them to newest-first","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:10:19.183057Z","id":"278a58f3be2c0406c42ee088e8ce2a13e148dd7a5532539d72deb508f49a6762","body":{"detail":"driver() at crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:339-343 returns Driver::Artifact for Shape::GroupRows whenever artifact or no_artifact is set, before the Unread check at :344; Driver::Artifact forces inbox_by_artifact (:313), whose key is (COALESCE(recipient,''), artifact_id, seq) (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1475) with no read_at column, so read_at IS NULL (:458) is applied per row. inbox_groups calls page_on(part(ReadFilter::Unread, rows)) (:1650-1653) with limit rows; when the group has rows or fewer unread items the LIMIT cannot be met and the scan runs over every item of that artifact for the recipient. shapes() (:744-922) has BY_ARTIFACT_PAGE (read: all) and UNREAD_NO_ARTIFACT_PAGE but no artifact+unread or artifact+read query. Cost, not a defect: concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"8cd1b419752ed66cd4c90fd1b63db05c440511466973be3ac809e62791b17b50","summary":"confirmed: GroupRows always drives by inbox_by_artifact with read_at as a residual filter","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:21:40.403729Z","id":"ed68dc8efc531bce2b9b2ff06dfdc3bed9ec1c66e6c243a4ea7c85477c258a1e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:03e9c77c6","summary":"Fixed: a Mark read shows the rows it read as read where they are, and the refresh keeps listed rows in their order (merged by ID, newer items on top), so rows reorder only on the next load or search. Evidence: inbox-page.test.ts 'keeps a group's rows where they are after its Mark read, the row it read shown read' (U5, R9, R8 kept, U5 shown read) passes in //web:unit.","supersedes":"54d28037ffbd2f6c0a476f7f4fa2dbdb46156cbb1315a6cd221585738a22754e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:21:40.472510Z","id":"26eecbb082d7cddb413c4b81b547423a798084e3590c25307bf7f5dc2228bcc9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:42abada77","summary":"Fixed: a group's unread part reads min(rows, unread) rows and its read part min(left, read), with no row past the limit (Shape::GroupRows), and 'more' comes from the counts; shapes() adds UNREAD_ARTIFACT_PAGE and READ_ARTIFACT_PAGE, so plans::every_inbox_query_still_uses_an_index checks their group-rows plans. //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test passes.","supersedes":"8cd1b419752ed66cd4c90fd1b63db05c440511466973be3ac809e62791b17b50","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:02:15.244248Z","id":"d0bfc77ca4599a2276f8acebf0dc5ebc042c4d1dee27b9f5946232cff05d1f42","body":{"detail":"Deleting a linked thread (Store::delete_thread_rows) drops its linked_outbox rows and keeps its linked_threads pairing ended with remote_thread_id still NULL when the 'thread' up-send had gone out but its answer had not come back. ack_outbox finds no outbox row (line 1019 returns Ok) and records nothing, so the pairing never learns the remote thread ID; the next read sees a remote thread no pairing names (linked_thread_by_remote) and mirrors it here as a new local thread. Fix direction: keep the remote thread ID on the ended pairing when the answer arrives (look the pairing up by the up-send's thread, not the outbox row), or record the up-sent thread's key so mirror can match it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1004},"end":{"line":1034},"content_hash":"857ce80f4e8c8e5a65d307aa7a629156b7351896061f47b0a9f4cde4af640f01"},"summary":"A local thread deleted while its 'thread' up-send is unacknowledged can come back as a new local thread","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:38:03.042554Z","id":"0072e3a4be220a103ac782d7e2af5136d1047a721baca29ee1b213a3ba15fa1d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5a0005618","summary":"Fixed: deleting a mirrored thread keeps its linked_threads pairing marked ended, so the next sync skips its twin instead of failing NotFound; //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test and //crates/clax-server/... pass. A deleted thread with an unacknowledged up-send is concern d0bfc77c.","supersedes":"3bc9d44f895ae70a36c4ee1e5d43e933f0c8026eb8eb1a6c01a75b4aa1d7c6f8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:38:03.067078Z","id":"fb9d0df974ff0c85422d195b07e67a882406322c6f60021e637b4a3ed1bed880","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1041691c7","summary":"Fixed: scan_linked and mirror_thread re-check the link in remote_links inside the transaction that writes for it; //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test passes.","supersedes":"a2967b618a2d4b830469a252f3348d3ccdac0818d576bd10e6cc431afdd8c7c0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:38:03.091161Z","id":"9a8eb75db62f826a3e7cc26a9f9a0997cf8e57e52e3f948602b81f1e717f0fe4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fde797b85","summary":"Fixed (fde797b85, 70b6e33ce): a keyed comment or thread records its key in the transaction that writes it, and a resend does the sends its first write did not reach; api_linked::a_resent_keyed_write_does_the_sends_its_first_write_did_not_reach passes (failed before). Follow-up state on replay is concern 5f1f58a1.","supersedes":"b8ab72608f6012889aabb83bc1419dd84ee1f8a93e0a3b3b525b4e0d625e5dcd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:08.971306Z","id":"1ad75b4f9a935bb594bb1020d452fa7cdf1bd36e045f962987e3928048bfd981","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1363-1368, record 0118687f.\n\nconnection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1535},"end":{"line":1540},"content_hash":"c1c86e26871ba066020c75f1d9b1b954ee91add027a8fb30f98694a07930d59d"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","supersedes":"ec3e72bf288017bec48256d06abae1517a28a65abc483ae6bb2604882a5ae4a4","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:09.025085Z","id":"eb8dfeebb1bcba6e262ec55db6bb003dd01a942fcc624fab1075e7873f0d2319","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1552-1556, record 6014047e.\n\nnote_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1806},"end":{"line":1810},"content_hash":"df46c2781c4e06aa0fe53e6fadd564b9bcbcad9e060403b47de165ac7d60413a"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","supersedes":"2569592d7a43b723d8aa14af64c57f7317ae0e4255cdb9d940d5179170650f5e","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:09.903444Z","id":"25096f72626e382c50b77edee0e1dde5d18f5536f6746be56756d6b42f3aa0a1","body":{"detail":"inbox_groups groups all of a query's matches (GROUP BY artifact over the driver's walk, with a temporary B-tree; crates/clax-store/src/plans.rs allows it for the ' groups' shapes) so each group's total and unread are exact across pages, then reads each listed group's newest rows by inbox_by_artifact. The unread section reads only unread items (inbox_unread); the read section, unfolded, reads the recipient's whole read history. The route runs it in the bulk lane (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs list). Accepted: an inbox of tens of thousands of items groups in milliseconds, and the read section loads only when unfolded.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1621},"end":{"line":1702},"content_hash":"c21e4c7179b4ee93301d6e354ee8a31dc042ecc2101279bbec0f7a94446d122b"},"summary":"Grouping the inbox by artifact reads every match to count each group","supersedes":"376160a6afe8ab8bed18d7fab0f9aa2963dbb3250f7d1f1db6c0c3e69cb3c99e","tags":["inbox","perf","revisit:a group=artifact read over 50 ms in just perf, or inboxes past 100k items","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:35:40.470225Z","id":"0769e2a22d9b899293ce7369395442afba5c63de45f317de70e05080399ffce9","body":{"detail":"Not taken: SQLite's NOCASE folds ASCII letters only, so 'Ärger' and 'ärger' would both be accepted. Migration 41 stores fold (clax_core::tags::fold, Rust's to_lowercase) with a UNIQUE constraint, one column more than the tags table the feature was first sketched with (id, name, colour, description, created_at, updated_at).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1190},"end":{"line":1209},"content_hash":"f9849f7e70e591978bbe2f18709d7cffa67d73224f8d14bb90afe33a670ca84f"},"summary":"Unique tag names through COLLATE NOCASE instead of a fold column","tags":["revisit:tag names need locale-aware or NFC-normalised comparison","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:35:40.470769Z","id":"a721a52740b73b1290b545ec118b6d96a876f564cc40d9618eca34a88d55f896","body":{"detail":"Not taken: GET /api/artifacts?tag= and the inbox's tag filter are open to guests, and an error listing the tags would name tags on artifacts the caller cannot see (GET /api/tags shows a guest only the tags in use on what it sees). An unknown name in a filter matches nothing instead. Writes (PUT/PATCH /api/artifacts/<aid>/tags) refuse unknown tags with the list, since only those who administer an artifact reach them.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":381},"end":{"line":390},"content_hash":"88a25aa245113758453fd4279e6a28bd67981689bb41cf5ee90fb03e9812f022"},"summary":"Refuse an unknown tag in a filter (400 unknown_tag) as the writes do","tags":["revisit:a filter typo that silently empties a view confuses people","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:35:40.470845Z","id":"b9b1153b9975702077af3b1164277e568ffc87263d9741786c7d5c353b866e38","body":{"detail":"The tag.delete record names the tag and how many live artifacts carried it (artifacts), not which. An artifact's own history (toolpath export per artifact) therefore does not show that it lost the tag. Accepted: tags are owner metadata, and one record per delete keeps a busy tag's delete one write.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":277},"end":{"line":301},"content_hash":"3aef9cfffd82dbca7375c566376195509f347a3b276aebe74170cba9426c1fbb"},"summary":"Deleting a tag records one tag.delete, not an artifact.update for each artifact that loses it","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:35:40.476049Z","id":"f6dd43ee604eccc67e27f31432a0a07a113109f1d64002bea11b9022c81b7ba9","body":{"detail":"Tag names are the owner's words (only the owner and the owner's agents make tags), so Vis::filter_artifact (crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs) leaves them alone, as the owner's own text. What a tag set says about an artifact is chosen by those who administer it (its creator among them): a person's agent that may read the artifact learns which tags its creator applied, though not any of that creator's own text. Accepted as the feature's point (shared tags, like GitHub labels).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":213},"end":{"line":220},"content_hash":"0d36aeb4acbe08e1bcc7f4993390602ec4cf2cff447be0b91c507e72dc5e97f9"},"summary":"Tags reach every reader of an artifact, agents included, unfiltered by approvals","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:53:17.992717Z","id":"6a3eb3d3de2bc8b80feda71cc2e711a8f307e1af33f502a0771be6252684881c","body":{"detail":"Failure: on a hosted Clax, Sam had a share of artifact A and holds inbox items about it; the owner removes the share and tags A 'layoffs'. GET /api/inbox?tag=layoffs (or /api/inbox/summary?tag=, crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs:495-511) returns Sam's items about A, so each request answers whether A carries that tag now. The items stay in the inbox after the share goes (crates/clax-http/src/views/inbox.rs:124-140 text_withheld_at withholds only their text, and the search's), and the tag term here does not consult it. Tag names are the owner's words, so this reveals the owner's current labelling of a page the person cannot read, not another person's text.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":488},"end":{"line":495},"content_hash":"69d5fa9999c3c1dff4c16b151ac8d3b64667f5b91499a5f0fa2fc43a1b94b80e"},"suggested_fix":"Leave the text_withheld_at artifacts (or those the recipient may not read) out of a tag filter's matches, as the search does for text.","summary":"An inbox tag filter tells a person which tags an artifact carries after they lost the right to read it","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags","security","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:55:11.181098Z","id":"c2f4e81488442f2d686db674ae1f97d6f0adcca9adb8cf6f24263d12643fd8e8","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:488-495 adds '+i.artifact_id IN (SELECT artifact_id FROM artifact_tags WHERE tag_id = ?)' per tag with no rights term; text_withheld_at is applied only when text.is_some() (:496) and only to Reply/Version/Finished kinds. crates/clax-http/src/views/inbox.rs:116-139 text_withheld_at lists the recipient's inbox artifacts whose comments they may no longer read, so the items persist after access goes. The summary path (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs:495-509) matches open questions by get_artifact + carries_all, also without a rights check. Concern (owner-chosen labels on a once-shared artifact) is the right severity.","kind":"comment","references":"6a3eb3d3de2bc8b80feda71cc2e711a8f307e1af33f502a0771be6252684881c","summary":"confirmed: the inbox tag term ignores text_withheld_at and the recipient's rights","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:14:34.568703Z","id":"0ceb8604df8d78c18dab8261c934ba333a0a988d94b4ecbf35012c229c8e20c0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:178bca1c4","summary":"Fixed in 178bca1c4: items about an artifact in text_withheld_at match no tag filter in the inbox list, grouping, mark-all and summary (questions too); api_hosted::a_tag_filter_matches_no_item_whose_text_is_withheld passes, and plans::every_inbox_query_still_uses_an_index covers the new PERSON_TAG_WITHHELD_PAGE shape (bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-store:all PASSED)","supersedes":"6a3eb3d3de2bc8b80feda71cc2e711a8f307e1af33f502a0771be6252684881c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:00.613653Z","id":"2eb022c9f93f2f45d225701a5bc3cf358bb49deeb5edd707d4263a3b45138f35","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1363-1368, record 0118687f.\n\nconnection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1589},"end":{"line":1594},"content_hash":"c1c86e26871ba066020c75f1d9b1b954ee91add027a8fb30f98694a07930d59d"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","supersedes":"1ad75b4f9a935bb594bb1020d452fa7cdf1bd36e045f962987e3928048bfd981","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:00.911123Z","id":"5ab9a83e4245981d00d2bdbf73d7825a012475ae84d9647b68bf6a8f9161e029","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1552-1556, record 6014047e.\n\nnote_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1860},"end":{"line":1864},"content_hash":"df46c2781c4e06aa0fe53e6fadd564b9bcbcad9e060403b47de165ac7d60413a"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","supersedes":"eb8dfeebb1bcba6e262ec55db6bb003dd01a942fcc624fab1075e7873f0d2319","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:01.082720Z","id":"a885e2354eb808178f2943fbbe892b6cc510792607fee93dd8d95bc298f3cb69","body":{"detail":"inbox_groups groups all of a query's matches (GROUP BY artifact over the driver's walk, with a temporary B-tree; crates/clax-store/src/plans.rs allows it for the ' groups' shapes) so each group's total and unread are exact across pages, then reads each listed group's newest rows by inbox_by_artifact. The unread section reads only unread items (inbox_unread); the read section, unfolded, reads the recipient's whole read history. The route runs it in the bulk lane (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs list). Accepted: an inbox of tens of thousands of items groups in milliseconds, and the read section loads only when unfolded.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1675},"end":{"line":1756},"content_hash":"c21e4c7179b4ee93301d6e354ee8a31dc042ecc2101279bbec0f7a94446d122b"},"summary":"Grouping the inbox by artifact reads every match to count each group","supersedes":"25096f72626e382c50b77edee0e1dde5d18f5536f6746be56756d6b42f3aa0a1","tags":["inbox","perf","revisit:a group=artifact read over 50 ms in just perf, or inboxes past 100k items","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:03.612888Z","id":"7b39335005c54fac341380b08bcd9eccd453a94c4954ea71d4b3a087de551fc1","body":{"detail":"Not taken: GET /api/artifacts?tag= and the inbox's tag filter are open to guests, and an error listing the tags would name tags on artifacts the caller cannot see (GET /api/tags shows a guest only the tags in use on what it sees). An unknown name in a filter matches nothing instead. Writes (PUT/PATCH /api/artifacts/<aid>/tags) refuse unknown tags with the list, since only those who administer an artifact reach them.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":397},"end":{"line":409},"content_hash":"dd6642da9cd67b683ee2d98691087ba265ead45e2da9a6502c1cb08ca762f36d"},"summary":"Refuse an unknown tag in a filter (400 unknown_tag) as the writes do","supersedes":"a721a52740b73b1290b545ec118b6d96a876f564cc40d9618eca34a88d55f896","tags":["revisit:a filter typo that silently empties a view confuses people","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:03.781792Z","id":"c9cd2dc9a668f4b36a8db762ba3aaa63a0efe2f8027ccbd48591caef8c733942","body":{"detail":"The tag.delete record names the tag and how many live artifacts carried it (artifacts), not which. An artifact's own history (toolpath export per artifact) therefore does not show that it lost the tag. Accepted: tags are owner metadata, and one record per delete keeps a busy tag's delete one write.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":298},"end":{"line":316},"content_hash":"8a836e4d1bdfbd7d939a8c18b77543b4510334dcb30ab4b37040a7b80b2c0157"},"summary":"Deleting a tag records one tag.delete, not an artifact.update for each artifact that loses it","supersedes":"b9b1153b9975702077af3b1164277e568ffc87263d9741786c7d5c353b866e38","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backfill.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:36:39.663674Z","id":"9c8e7a8631870ee873167d78f4d3788bc66b42f9ef497eacebe479da099ab1de","body":{"detail":"Failure: in CI runs 39440289806, 39352509329, 39283609761 and 39266520838 (ci.yml on main, 2026-10-19/20) it panicked at line 2420 with 3.83 s and 3.86 s of CPU. AGENTS.md asks for no wall-clock budgets in checks and for performance to be measured on demand (just perf). Its failure also fails tests::the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection (crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:897), which reruns the suite on one connection.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2408},"end":{"line":2421},"content_hash":"c22de098aa9cee0dadd117a1aaade941801d6312b96bb9cabe5ad23f3e18a07b"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the event count assertion and move the CPU budget to just perf.","summary":"backfill_on_perf_seed_under_3s is a 3 s CPU budget and fails CI on main","tags":["flaky","tests","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backfill.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T16:40:18.482648Z","id":"9808a2e8b87ad3320c840f47509d04908f82657d0b7bacd97bf8f9e0c38156be","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0c18ceef3","summary":"Fixed in 0c18ceef3: the test is now backfill_on_perf_seed_records_every_event and checks the event count only, with no time assertion. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test on macOS: PASSED (it includes tests::the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection, which reruns it).","supersedes":"9c8e7a8631870ee873167d78f4d3788bc66b42f9ef497eacebe479da099ab1de","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backfill.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T16:40:20.755762Z","id":"1c99e0720eebf1d4024760d107b0b9fc12137812df16fbee6dace0c162101c5a","body":{"detail":"The perf seed's backfill time is measured on demand only by the ignored test backfill_at_scale (CLAX_BACKFILL_SCALE=1 for the seed the correctness test uses). just perf (scripts/run.sh perf) runs the Bazel targets //scripts:perf_daemon_full, //scripts:perf_clients_full, //web:perf_usable_full and //web:bundle_size, none of which runs Rust unit tests, so adding it there would need a new Bazel target running this ignored test with --ignored.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2412},"end":{"line":2440},"content_hash":"3a03f72f787bb37d637cfac349e94436aebd8d2a19e17a1962db328a60ef2dc1"},"summary":"Backfill timing is not part of just perf","tags":["perf","revisit:the backfill's time on an upgrade becomes a release concern","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:07:28.796836Z","id":"69bc76e02d7f4aa857025c33d0189330af7f1d3ad9c990eeedd7272d2c32ed08","body":{"detail":"MovingAppData (crates/clax-http/src/app_data_host.rs) moves an artifact's rows only when its store is first called, so an artifact no request touches keeps its rows in the instance indefinitely. viewers::fold (crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs) still rewrites those tables for unmoved artifacts and artifacts.rs still deletes from them on delete. Dropping the tables needs a step that moves every remaining artifact first (or a migration-time move), then removes the three tables, the doc_seq column and the instance-side folds of documents.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1210},"end":{"line":1223},"content_hash":"f858f9ed7e07685d53dd0b9a1cc8a0633c4f2e7fce1ac13c58c7ea3a5d7d0b41"},"summary":"Migration 42 leaves the instance's docs, doc_authors and leases tables (and artifacts.doc_seq) in place, emptied artifact by artifact on each store's first call; a later release must drop them once every live artifact is in app_data_moved","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:07:28.797195Z","id":"deff44912c049306b6ff04712744f40709c7e9093b37c9e7e2f095ffecca803f","body":{"detail":"Store::record_audit is no longer called for document changes (crates/clax-store/src/app_data/mod.rs record_in), so the journal appender (which reads the instance's audit_events) and audit::tool_call_record's produced list carry no document writes. Store::export_with merges every moved live artifact's AppData::audit_since rows after the instance's rows, gathered with one host call per artifact per export (crates/clax-server/src/routes/toolpath.rs app_data_audit), which on the Worker is one Durable Object call each. Records written before an artifact moved stay in the instance's audit_events. Deleting an artifact removes artifacts/<id>/, its data.sqlite with its audit records, where the instance's audit outlived deletion.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":655},"end":{"line":690},"content_hash":"5bc16f9faf082a6b7569b0827007736a2ed5c5d39610af480f8327e4c67bd02f"},"summary":"doc.write and doc.move records now live in each artifact's store: the journal never sees them, a tool.call's produced omits them, an export numbers them past the snapshot's newest seq (so their step IDs change between exports), and a deleted artifact's are lost with its store","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:31:59.028134Z","id":"e63879315d3db05de52e374649bdc37af0c825d94913c5ad4ba0d072faea13c9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dfde3cd1","summary":"Fixed: each change's store audit records are copied into the instance's audit_events (Store::mirror_app_data_audit, app_data_moved.audit_seq), so the journal, produced and exports hold them, with stable seqs, and a deleted artifact's history stays; the export's per-artifact gathering is gone. bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__* passes api_toolpath::every_mutation_records_one_event and doc_write_records_hash_not_content against the instance's table; //crates/clax-http:clax_http_lib_test passes app_data_host::tests::each_changes_records_are_copied_into_the_instances_history_once.","supersedes":"deff44912c049306b6ff04712744f40709c7e9093b37c9e7e2f095ffecca803f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:31:59.418601Z","id":"fb39b95843f11754b71cd6df7126151c56fe1052d70767ed7cc322d0b162e3a8","body":{"detail":"On the local daemon they empty as it starts: serve.rs runs app_data_host::move_pending, which moves every live artifact the instance still holds rows of, one at a time. On the Worker each artifact moves at its store's first call, so an artifact no request touches keeps its rows. viewers::fold (crates/clax-store/src/viewers.rs) still rewrites those tables for unmoved artifacts and artifacts.rs still deletes from them. Dropping them needs every artifact moved first, then the three tables, the doc_seq column and the instance-side folds of documents removed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1210},"end":{"line":1228},"content_hash":"26c30b9d7c5c22e3d31e1dd515a715330ca5d5eb89d27179ba9782209fca686e"},"summary":"Migration 42 leaves the instance's docs, doc_authors and leases tables (and artifacts.doc_seq) in place; a later release must drop them once every artifact is in app_data_moved","supersedes":"69bc76e02d7f4aa857025c33d0189330af7f1d3ad9c990eeedd7272d2c32ed08","tags":["deferred-work","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:38:44.071984Z","id":"a71cc281e14d7c88f543f72b88162c06b101c201c25ef3616b51559b8dff6d89","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e63879315d3db05de52e374649bdc37af0c825d94913c5ad4ba0d072faea13c9","summary":"Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-http:clax_http_lib_test passes app_data_host::tests::each_changes_records_are_copied_into_the_instances_history_once; the clax-server integration shards pass api_toolpath::every_mutation_records_one_event and api_toolpath::doc_write_records_hash_not_content, and //crates/clax-cli:integration__* passes comments::tool_commands_are_recorded_as_the_owner_on_cli, each reading the instance's audit_events.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/site_sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T17:39:50.649416Z","id":"fe113cbee3b5546c4dba53aedad88a236c314de46a1a2b51003fe39202327909","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/world.rs reuses push_approvals (open_push_approval, use_push_approval) so the approval is one use and waits on one question per session and artifact without a migration. Its rows say remote_id 'site:world', which no remote has, and their upto is the version current when asked, which nothing reads for them.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"fbcca644c73b7ac0fda1894c68f4be90f8a83f55e2c08bd183ea3b89e598bd67"},"summary":"An approval to open a site to the world kept in a table of its own rather than in push_approvals under the remote_id 'site:world'","tags":["revisit:a second kind of approval needs the same row, or push_approvals is rebuilt","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:11:53.382960Z","id":"cfdf43b82f158183a57571815f40e53529f5ac4ec8e0022ba902b92e7e321c7b","body":{"detail":"check_page_asset (crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs) runs for via_page uploads, which every site API upload is (site_api.rs sets x-clax-via: page). Uploads with the token or an agent's grant (the asset_upload tool, scripts) keep is_supported's set (any image/, video/ or font/ type and the text types) and the 20 MiB cap: they are the owner's own, not a page's.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":165},"end":{"line":169},"content_hash":"9ddad356bdb627ef94f82100106014f9af2932e38d133615cea0c326fdbeb197"},"summary":"Only a page's upload meets the contract's asset rules; an agent's or the owner's own upload keeps the broader type set","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/assets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T16:04:20.341472Z","id":"6ccba1055775eccefaeac4c19d98fa01268cb72b4ac293aaa7739ead61320a0f","body":{"detail":"check_page_asset (crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs) runs for via_page uploads, which every site API upload is (site_api.rs sets x-clax-via: page). Uploads with the token or an agent's grant (the asset_upload tool, scripts) keep is_supported's set (any image/, video/ or font/ type and the text types) and the 20 MiB cap: they are the owner's own, not a page's.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":208},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"9ddad356bdb627ef94f82100106014f9af2932e38d133615cea0c326fdbeb197"},"summary":"Only a page's upload meets the contract's asset rules; an agent's or the owner's own upload keeps the broader type set","supersedes":"cfdf43b82f158183a57571815f40e53529f5ac4ec8e0022ba902b92e7e321c7b","tags":["site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T16:04:20.380694Z","id":"425b4665faa85e18db89e4643a8e5c5c4be539af098004589e7ee959f8d524c4","body":{"detail":"Store::fork_assets copies the source's assets whose ID appears in the forked version's files as a whole run of letters and digits (crates/clax-store/src/assets.rs named_ids). An asset a page names only at run time (an ID built in script, or kept in a db document, which a fork does not copy either) stays the source's alone, so the fork's /_clax/blob/<id> for it answers 404. Copying all of the source's assets would cover those at the cost of copying uploads the fork's version never uses (each up to 20 MiB, crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs MAX_ASSET_BYTES).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":278},"end":{"line":307},"content_hash":"2a7b9dc75c2d3170a9dda52f8823b033e22a6a0d397c65cf8c5caa4bb89bd1a9"},"summary":"Copy every asset of the source into a fork, not only those its version's files name by ID","tags":["forks","site-origins","revisit:a forked page is reported loading an asset it names only at run time","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T16:04:20.380800Z","id":"d3492f5bba56de4ebc8bb1cff9d5d6bddb9b3e326f42fd10bc9026d536f87a04","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1265},"end":{"line":1288},"content_hash":"9f879d94ee66718a19655af602ab7ab206f16d454ec272c96174ffc906813f6b"},"summary":"Migration 45 (assets keyed by artifact and ID) follows this branch's 44 (site sessions); main also numbers migrations 43 to 47 (at b0150ae3), so this branch's 42 to 45 renumber when it lands","tags":["site-origins","migrations","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T16:04:20.381053Z","id":"b419e52faa98fbd0ae81348dbdbe560605f51518f27a4b3f1bdf4bf180134301","body":{"detail":"Evidence, all passing at d21f9ff0: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test (678 passed) incl. forks::tests::a_fork_copies_the_assets_its_version_names_under_the_same_ids (named assets copied with bytes, uploader and an asset.upload carrying forked_from; the source's delete_asset and delete_artifact leave the fork's) and migrations::tests::migration_45_names_each_asset_within_its_artifact; //crates/clax-server:integration__6 api_assets::a_forks_page_loads_its_assets_from_its_own_site (the fork's site serves /_clax/blob/<source asset ID> 200 with the same bytes before and after the source deletes the asset and itself; the page is unrewritten); just worker-test (clax-worker lib, 49 passed) incl. repos::tests::forks::a_forks_page_loads_its_assets_from_its_own_site on the Worker's content store (stand-in git, assets in a bucket). An asset named only at run time is not copied: alternative recorded on crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs:278:307.","kind":"comment","references":"3f605810ac353760dd7f00a5dd173cad7dd7b7ebf066e5a9b7718bb25f2a5aa8","summary":"Fixed by git:d21f9ff0 (option (a) of this record): migration 45 keys assets by (artifact_id, id), a fork copies the assets its version's files name, bytes and row, under the same IDs, and its site serves its own copy; proposing close","tags":["forks","site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T18:24:59.680874Z","id":"4c27de11d1eb92400e9301299546257eec97c7e71d4a1cb818cb62990d1c2b70","body":{"detail":"Store::fork_assets finds the source's assets whose ID appears in the forked version's files as a whole run of letters and digits (crates/clax-store/src/assets.rs named_ids), refuses too_many_assets past MAX_FORK_ASSETS or MAX_FORK_ASSET_BYTES (crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs), and Store::copy_asset_bytes copies them. An asset a page names only at run time (an ID built in script, or kept in a db document, which a fork does not copy either) stays the source's alone, so the fork's /_clax/blob/<id> for it answers 404. Copying all of the source's assets would cover those at the cost of copying uploads the fork's version never uses (each up to 20 MiB, MAX_ASSET_BYTES), and would meet the fork caps sooner.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":281},"end":{"line":327},"content_hash":"ef5b16a377337bd376dc26fd79305ad788a91c81d06e66a3750a564d37ef04db"},"summary":"Copy every asset of the source into a fork, not only those its version's files name by ID","supersedes":"425b4665faa85e18db89e4643a8e5c5c4be539af098004589e7ee959f8d524c4","tags":["forks","site-origins","revisit:a forked page is reported loading an asset it names only at run time","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:07:12.169556Z","id":"9518bf391d1e92ab5f0d6a76d01fc4027543b3c4756bd4e37515a51adf703130","body":{"detail":"SEED_MODELS seeds input/cached/output micro-USD per Mtok for claude-haiku-5-5 (0.10/0.01/0.50 USD), claude-sonnet-5-5 (2/0.20/10), claude-opus-5-5 (4/0.20/20) and claude-fable-5-1 (10/0.25/50). Haiku 5.5's cache-read price was not published in the table used; 0.01 USD is taken as a tenth of input. Haiku 5.5's higher rate for prompts over 100K tokens (0.50/2.50 USD) and cache-write prices are not modelled: a long Haiku prompt is under-charged. Each line's source text says '(check)'; an admin can correct it with put_cost_line, which applies to new usage only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":370},"end":{"line":401},"content_hash":"51475fad8d851d25f4f50a7f4dc91af7bcef4825cff37069360fecd9d477c23e"},"suggested_fix":"Check each figure against the published pricing page before launch; add cache-write lines and a long-context Haiku line if the bot uses them.","summary":"Seeded token prices are Anthropic list prices as cached on 2026-10-06; Haiku 5.5's cache-read price is a guess","tags":["claxbot","pricing","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:07:12.169658Z","id":"084b70324502c6df35c190a2cf34a5928ac8f08e1f1c45b7e811ef466a9d7cd7","body":{"detail":"script.compute uses 17 micro-USD per GiB-second, a generic serverless figure (the Worker Loader bills CPU time, not GiB-seconds); do.requests (0.15 USD per million) and toolpath.storage (0.20 USD per GB-month) are Durable Object list prices. The bot layer must estimate requests and bytes per step, as spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 13 notes; nothing reads actual billing. The per-run harness fee is a fixed 1 credit with no underlying cost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":438},"end":{"line":470},"content_hash":"65ba91f0fed26544b7fa7897c9d42ef00e0fee4b9054798dae37b8d2c944c6c3"},"summary":"Infrastructure cost lines are estimates, not Cloudflare billing","tags":["claxbot","pricing","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:07:12.169715Z","id":"2e234b3da260e4aff6718daf93e25aea174b50418b2584955b57829285f52512","body":{"detail":"charge_in splits each row's credits into free_milli (what the weekly allowance had left) and paid. Raising a person's lift mid-week makes later rows free again but leaves earlier paid rows paid, so usage_report's revenue counts credits the person now has allowance for. The spec's usage row has a boolean `free`; the store keeps the integer free_milli instead (UsageRow::free() derives the boolean) so a row straddling the allowance is split exactly.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":554},"end":{"line":600},"content_hash":"272667741d0124a6f0cfdbd1e229c60d2f0c7a8da6dea522591abfa4bf0a2029"},"summary":"A row's free part is fixed when charged: a lift raised later does not turn paid credits back into free ones","tags":["claxbot","credits","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit_query.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:07:12.169755Z","id":"9abccad85a3b5e2fb18e0d1ce83a914f14e406b26b416286dcf6984f7933c571","body":{"detail":"scope_sql matches the actor's type and person through json_extract on every row, and text search is LIKE over kind, actor and body; only the kind groups (audit_events_kind, migration 42) and the artifact filter use an index. On a home with a large journal a member's audit page reads the whole table per page. Measure with just perf before relying on it for hosted instances with many members.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"d7bb25025f4757fcd69bb6306ff2ad397d8b829adb7b0a0653e33fc047b9f3cd"},"suggested_fix":"Store the actor's person key in an indexed column (or a side table) when an event is recorded, and scope on it.","summary":"A non-admin's audit query and every text search scan audit_events with json_extract","tags":["claxbot","audit","perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit_query.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:07:12.169787Z","id":"b03b7acadcd56decb6069bdc4f5094890cc367ee1d623bca8549ec7e939a052e","body":{"detail":"scope_sql admits events whose artifact_id or artifact2_id names an artifact with artifacts.person = the reader. A person a share gives an artifact to does not see its events unless they acted in them; an artifact the owner created is the owner's (who reads everything as an admin).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":117},"content_hash":"d7bb25025f4757fcd69bb6306ff2ad397d8b829adb7b0a0653e33fc047b9f3cd"},"summary":"'Artifacts they own' in audit scoping means artifacts the person created, not artifacts shared with them","tags":["claxbot","audit","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:07:12.169893Z","id":"471980d1cc25a9f75b951b1ea23da561c5c13a3fe5ab33fd5e8f7ba6f6b11cf5","body":{"detail":"Each DraftChange::Write stores its full content as a BLOB; the store does not bound a file's size, a draft's total, or how long an ended run's draft is kept (a stopped run's draft must stay viewable, spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 6.3). The caller (clax-bot's files.write) must cap sizes, and a later change should prune drafts of runs that ended long ago or were published.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1342},"end":{"line":1348},"content_hash":"f325b86717df6d16cb53a01e25fcfa70401e2fc07ca66842609fd40e9968b1f2"},"summary":"Run drafts are kept whole in bot_draft_files with no size cap and never pruned","tags":["claxbot","storage","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:07:12.169940Z","id":"2c28ec5827cd3add44c72fdd298611db986de6e2bbf585b19712873ac4c91f83","body":{"detail":"claim_run takes a run held by another driver only after lease_secs since that claim. A native daemon restarts with a new driver ID, so its own runs claimed before the restart stay held until the lease lapses. The native driver should release (or reclaim with lease 0) every live run on start, since one daemon holds a home.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":404},"end":{"line":410},"content_hash":"924513cb8644ce16f99b38711cd302da22b500ec681557fd6a972d4e3f45449d"},"summary":"A restarted daemon waits out its own stale run claims unless it releases them","tags":["claxbot","runs","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:07:12.169971Z","id":"c3e970b29a59f0f8c319f99b05c26db8f5d7fd5cf21434682eb84f2a62ea08b5","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 9.1 names no kind for a cancel request, so the trail shows only the run's stopped step and bot.run_end with the reason the driver gives. Who pressed Stop is not recorded; the route could record it in the reason or a new kind could be added.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":608},"end":{"line":621},"content_hash":"273a7ed40d9b54e80a3138989ff97c51f99cfaedfa2341368a93cbd3b7df7b25"},"summary":"cancel_run records no audit event","tags":["claxbot","audit","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/secrets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:07:12.170007Z","id":"b3b5706936e6c9ce7c7fb6a64634caf34d6e27631056ee56d3af2ca80b2b1fe3","body":{"detail":"Kek::load_or_create never replaces an existing secrets/kek, and open_for_use answers kek_mismatch when the KEK differs; there is no re-seal path. Restoring clax.db without its secrets/kek, or a Worker redeployed with a new CLAX_KEK, needs every key set again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":70},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"d7113ad9cd234f8cb64f600c4f305446b30d6805cb3c8dc14f5d9e8104a905c1"},"suggested_fix":"Add a rotate step that opens every row with the old KEK and seals it under the new one in one transaction.","summary":"No key-encryption-key rotation; a lost or replaced KEK makes every sealed key unopenable","tags":["claxbot","secrets","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:07:12.170096Z","id":"71c70474a2dfa40f292e8702aed7c53e886068fa3bada5e7fb0b0d726b4d19ad","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1210},"end":{"line":1235},"content_hash":"f78f2169f9d520179c3e9b5aa6d8cc67d2bf235cce4d40a269099724f8625ec5"},"summary":"Migration 42 (ClaxBot) takes the next number after main's 41 (tags); it renumbers if another branch lands a 42 first","tags":["claxbot","migration","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:31:40.090536Z","id":"02b6b3240e706791a7043f199c7ccfb2265bd078052597ac9bdacb09929d4380","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d93bbba3","summary":"cancel_run now takes an AuditCtx and records bot.cancel {run, by} in its transaction when it changes the run; bot_runs::tests::cancel_is_recorded_and_stops_at_the_next_step passes (bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test --nocache_test_results: PASSED)","supersedes":"c3e970b29a59f0f8c319f99b05c26db8f5d7fd5cf21434682eb84f2a62ea08b5","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:31:40.112198Z","id":"9e4cf2eb2d068bc7b6335c7a87cd81ee988ec072a2c6fe2ca313f76ee47cff7b","body":{"detail":"SEED_MODELS seeds input/cached/output micro-USD per Mtok for claude-haiku-5-5 (0.10/0.01/0.50 USD), claude-sonnet-5-5 (2/0.20/10), claude-opus-5-5 (4/0.20/20) and claude-fable-5-1 (10/0.25/50). Haiku 5.5's cache-read price was not in the table used; 0.01 USD is a tenth of input. Cache-write lines are 1.25 times input (cache_write_price), the 5-minute write rate; 1-hour writes are not modelled. Haiku 5.5's higher rate for prompts over 100K tokens (0.50/2.50 USD) is not modelled either, so a long Haiku prompt is under-charged. Each line's source says '(check)'; an admin corrects it with put_cost_line or price_model, for new usage only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":456},"end":{"line":485},"content_hash":"572b73ab9668510558ab64848f989d061e9c2a5c3e44692986f754a228b0e8c2"},"suggested_fix":"Check each figure against the published pricing page before launch; add a long-context Haiku line if the bot uses long Haiku prompts.","summary":"Seeded token prices are Anthropic list prices as cached on 2026-10-06; Haiku 5.5's cache-read price and every cache-write price are derived","supersedes":"9518bf391d1e92ab5f0d6a76d01fc4027543b3c4756bd4e37515a51adf703130","tags":["claxbot","pricing","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:31:40.134356Z","id":"5dc5409dfbc46360a91c6513c3b0612ea82828068041b0f9c05787203ffbf59c","body":{"detail":"script.compute uses 17 micro-USD per GiB-second, a generic serverless figure (the Worker Loader bills CPU time, not GiB-seconds); do.requests (0.15 USD per million) and toolpath.storage (0.20 USD per GB-month) are Durable Object list prices. The bot layer must estimate requests and bytes per step, as spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 13 notes; nothing reads actual billing. The per-run harness fee is a fixed 1 credit with no underlying cost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":539},"end":{"line":568},"content_hash":"472eedd205fb34de0a9ca8d86131c26fe43b4ffbf7a32069a95c56d7aa016f55"},"summary":"Infrastructure cost lines are estimates, not Cloudflare billing","supersedes":"084b70324502c6df35c190a2cf34a5928ac8f08e1f1c45b7e811ef466a9d7cd7","tags":["claxbot","pricing","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:31:40.152646Z","id":"275ef400517f27b1086c74cf62887213573e250e0a935ac69bb5e5eca833d415","body":{"detail":"charge_in splits each row's credits into free_milli (what the weekly allowance had left) and paid. Raising a person's lift mid-week makes later rows free again but leaves earlier paid rows paid, so usage_report's revenue counts credits the person now has allowance for. The spec's usage row has a boolean `free`; the store keeps the integer free_milli instead (UsageRow::free() derives the boolean) so a row straddling the allowance is split exactly.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":653},"end":{"line":697},"content_hash":"1f5970ffe4ec28dcff516cfefbbbb3e2005819ea2d6b57637b065e0c0a32f399"},"summary":"A row's free part is fixed when charged: a lift raised later does not turn paid credits back into free ones","supersedes":"2e234b3da260e4aff6718daf93e25aea174b50418b2584955b57829285f52512","tags":["claxbot","credits","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit_query.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:31:40.173772Z","id":"1398adf259b7490faf7398f3eec4999855363e765b2274838beda390aa50e974","body":{"detail":"scope_sql matches the actor's type and person through json_extract on every row, checks shares through correlated subqueries over artifact.update events (by audit_events_artifact), and text search is LIKE over kind, actor and body; only the kind groups (audit_events_kind, migration 42) and the artifact filter use an index directly. On a home with a large journal a member's audit page reads the whole table per page. Measure with just perf before relying on it for hosted instances with many members.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":141},"content_hash":"0ecab5910d3db13cbe46b3a846a581bdc40650cb20de116ebeced0ec7c0c36d4"},"suggested_fix":"Store the actor's person key in an indexed column (or a side table) when an event is recorded, keep share periods in a table, and scope on them.","summary":"A non-admin's audit query and every text search scan audit_events with json_extract","supersedes":"9abccad85a3b5e2fb18e0d1ce83a914f14e406b26b416286dcf6984f7933c571","tags":["claxbot","audit","perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit_query.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:31:40.193179Z","id":"5bd4d23ebe1a52085943e80e2b951d02c6c35b016ccc83272e01e0e2447b629f","body":{"detail":"scope_sql admits, for a non-admin, events on artifacts they created and, as the implemented default, events on an artifact shared with them from the artifact.update that set the share to the one that removed it (a share as it is now also counts from its created_at, for shares made by GitHub login before the person had a public ID). audit_query::tests::a_share_shows_its_artifact_s_events_while_it_held pins it. Open questions for the owner: should a share's events stay visible after it is removed (it is not now), and should a viewer-only share see every event on the artifact (it does now), or only views and comments?","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":141},"content_hash":"0ecab5910d3db13cbe46b3a846a581bdc40650cb20de116ebeced0ec7c0c36d4"},"summary":"Audit scoping now includes artifacts shared with the reader, while the share held: the owner should confirm this default","supersedes":"b03b7acadcd56decb6069bdc4f5094890cc367ee1d623bca8549ec7e939a052e","tags":["claxbot","audit","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:31:40.214088Z","id":"3b82221477aba0e31d61e0f79ba28984563a45fafed0c628a7ea1d5212fcab62","body":{"detail":"Each DraftChange::Write stores its full content as a BLOB; the store does not bound a file's size, a draft's total, or how long an ended run's draft is kept (a stopped run's draft must stay viewable, spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 6.3). The caller (clax-bot's files.write) must cap sizes, and a later change should prune drafts of runs that ended long ago or were published.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1345},"end":{"line":1351},"content_hash":"f325b86717df6d16cb53a01e25fcfa70401e2fc07ca66842609fd40e9968b1f2"},"summary":"Run drafts are kept whole in bot_draft_files with no size cap and never pruned","supersedes":"471980d1cc25a9f75b951b1ea23da561c5c13a3fe5ab33fd5e8f7ba6f6b11cf5","tags":["claxbot","storage","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:31:40.234900Z","id":"d4c12e57d4c0a2d5e69060cee473587941d7da36b781b3d4791249fe887902ca","body":{"detail":"claim_run takes a run held by another driver only after lease_secs since that claim (begin_step and commit_step now refuse a driver that does not hold it). A native daemon restarts with a new driver ID, so its own runs claimed before the restart stay held until the lease lapses. The native driver should release (or claim with lease 0) every live run on start, since one daemon holds a home.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":456},"end":{"line":462},"content_hash":"924513cb8644ce16f99b38711cd302da22b500ec681557fd6a972d4e3f45449d"},"summary":"A restarted daemon waits out its own stale run claims unless it releases them","supersedes":"2c28ec5827cd3add44c72fdd298611db986de6e2bbf585b19712873ac4c91f83","tags":["claxbot","runs","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/secrets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:31:40.255305Z","id":"6b6a7a33e7dd6ab9c636b64d416ac4bc86c3ab5aa98855d20b20c93f687cbe90","body":{"detail":"Kek::load_or_create never replaces an existing secrets/kek, and open_for_use answers kek_mismatch when the KEK differs; there is no re-seal path. Restoring clax.db without its secrets/kek, or a Worker redeployed with a new CLAX_KEK, needs every key set again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":85},"end":{"line":145},"content_hash":"5ea3356f88f01b8aaf17d72a1eec4b71e1e7cc963370a2f297a14b6bf18b044b"},"suggested_fix":"Add a rotate step that opens every row with the old KEK and seals it under the new one in one transaction.","summary":"No key-encryption-key rotation; a lost or replaced KEK makes every sealed key unopenable","supersedes":"b3b5706936e6c9ce7c7fb6a64634caf34d6e27631056ee56d3af2ca80b2b1fe3","tags":["claxbot","secrets","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:31:40.274937Z","id":"348256e5c059c9ad1d3536048a690deca3f6d5a37faeee52667f65c15440611e","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1210},"end":{"line":1236},"content_hash":"88d21b3aecd9d20a9b454f89f4ffaaecc821d6928f7331ab18b29cf93d3bb1b4"},"summary":"Migration 42 (ClaxBot) takes the next number after main's 41 (tags); it renumbers if another branch lands a 42 first","supersedes":"71c70474a2dfa40f292e8702aed7c53e886068fa3bada5e7fb0b0d726b4d19ad","tags":["claxbot","migration","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:31:40.293787Z","id":"651f09e1c1ae3f1da17ec4f3484afc2fcb7daaf51d7082ae6ad6c0cf0780e66d","body":{"detail":"Branch origin/flutter-app numbers its own migrations 42 to 47, so this branch's 42 and those cannot both land under the same numbers: whichever branch lands on main second must renumber its migrations to follow the other's. Homes migrated by either branch's unmerged builds (a dev home at schema 42 from this branch, or at 42-47 from flutter-app) hold a different schema under the same numbers and must be reset, not upgraded; migration 37's repair does not cover them.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1210},"end":{"line":1236},"content_hash":"88d21b3aecd9d20a9b454f89f4ffaaecc821d6928f7331ab18b29cf93d3bb1b4"},"summary":"Migration 42 collides with the flutter-app branch, which also writes migrations 42 to 47","tags":["claxbot","migration","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:32:34.197079Z","id":"296245160b1b37ea7f76479fa990b7ffc670a105cb1fc988afc142a9ffefe725","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs:757-783, record 102e3b6a.\n\nMeasured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":775},"end":{"line":801},"content_hash":"52e810ab13e4b4c1906f3b6d191494a2b7dbc5c619a6c49ab2c0c512f581f5a7"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"0e4f092370e31dcb4f89bb6cf9a6af26d09b32d88d9d0182e1eeab2a0b372ac6","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:32:34.215187Z","id":"10d7efccbab7cb6b6a91ecde6573bf87afbcdcb54ac2650c35e04cfa92d187b4","body":{"detail":"rust-int commit c308495e6 (2026-10-14) made push_approvals without upto (NOT NULL, no default), so the table is rebuilt. No version is recorded for such a row; 0 approves none, where the artifact's current version could approve one the owner never saw. Only a local daemon writes push_approvals, so a hosted database has no such rows. Tested by migrations::tests::repair::migration_37_carries_inbox_items_and_push_approvals_through_their_rebuilds.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1532},"end":{"line":1537},"content_hash":"509eff3ee94ddc389fc0d7753e67ce2f24f39e0c2fdde5f3f3b2d03d71a541b8"},"summary":"Migration 37 keeps a push_approvals row that lacks upto with upto = 0, so its push asks the owner again","supersedes":"b7e429cbb788218dcb929923f327ebcb3e2ba16c8d91617b26d70c5ee85036cf","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:32:34.232755Z","id":"745b385d5d6eb2b62989fd987133fcb6636c943d53db7ccfd00e6fcdeb8dfec2","body":{"detail":"Copies of migrations 24 and 25 from 2026-10-10 (git log -S page_person -- crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs: ddfff6383, 051681542, 86fcda318, 4b6a1d656) add versions.page_person and comments.page_person, which the final migrations replace with versions.by_page/file_authors_json and page_authors. repair() does not drop or carry them: no code reads them, the meaning of their values does not map onto page_authors rows one for one, and only development homes of that week can hold them. Such a home keeps two dead nullable columns, so its schema differs from a new one's by them. tests/fixtures/old-migrations holds no fixture of that shape.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1667},"end":{"line":1721},"content_hash":"97f8ba2c1a6b0fbb7fe081538a2a7104b5856c69479604a8d5eacc2088d7c2c3"},"summary":"Migration 37's repair leaves comments.page_person and versions.page_person where an early multi-person build added them","supersedes":"4717eb4eec3e51168f8b9ae20f459f5d18c962be9ade6236a718c9d53a9ada9e","tags":["migrations","revisit:a home made by a 2026-10-10 multi-person build is still in use","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit_query.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:34:28.391621Z","id":"4a2d7e107419eda86dcc2d6876831acdaf2d38181826e814a71be39bd097a57f","body":{"detail":"scope_sql matches the actor's type and person through json_extract on every row, checks shares through correlated subqueries over artifact.update events (by audit_events_artifact), and text search is LIKE over kind, actor and body; only the kind groups (audit_events_kind, migration 42) and the artifact filter use an index directly. On a home with a large journal a member's audit page reads the whole table per page. Measure with just perf before relying on it for hosted instances with many members. Since c8ccd472 the share check is three correlated subqueries per candidate event: one over artifact.update share set/remove events on the event's artifact (audit_events_artifact) and two over person.revoke events for the reader (an audit_events_kind range, then json_extract on the body), which end a share period at a revocation; each is an index range scan per row the outer query examines.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":151},"content_hash":"5a3fd47bd0a4f34a76e20c92401c8f0660925aa0ef3efdda475244f46bdeae08"},"suggested_fix":"Store the actor's person key in an indexed column (or a side table) when an event is recorded, keep share periods in a table, and scope on them.","summary":"A non-admin's audit query and every text search scan audit_events with json_extract","supersedes":"1398adf259b7490faf7398f3eec4999855363e765b2274838beda390aa50e974","tags":["claxbot","audit","perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit_query.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:34:28.424804Z","id":"86e0241bb348efcf9a48e80a41d46e6b6985f1574f22537f9a22245f958b67ab","body":{"detail":"scope_sql admits, for a non-admin, events on artifacts they created and, as the implemented default, events on an artifact shared with them from the artifact.update that set the share to the one that removed it (or to the person's revocation, even if they connect again under the same public ID; a share as it is now also counts from its created_at unless revoked since, for shares made by GitHub login before the person had a public ID). audit_query::tests::a_share_shows_its_artifact_s_events_while_it_held pins it. Open questions for the owner: should a share's events stay visible after it is removed (it is not now), and should a viewer-only share see every event on the artifact (it does now), or only views and comments? audit_query::tests::revoking_a_person_ends_their_shares_in_the_trail_even_after_they_reconnect pins the revocation rule.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":151},"content_hash":"5a3fd47bd0a4f34a76e20c92401c8f0660925aa0ef3efdda475244f46bdeae08"},"summary":"Audit scoping now includes artifacts shared with the reader, while the share held: the owner should confirm this default","supersedes":"5bd4d23ebe1a52085943e80e2b951d02c6c35b016ccc83272e01e0e2447b629f","tags":["claxbot","audit","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:35:14.358162Z","id":"4162a67f8452134e3fc646c7e5fdca0661b0823313a214f35a2afae1bd512773","body":{"detail":"SEED_MODELS seeds input/cached/output micro-USD per Mtok for claude-haiku-5-5 (0.10/0.01/0.50 USD), claude-sonnet-5-5 (2/0.20/10), claude-opus-5-5 (4/0.20/20) and claude-fable-5-1 (10/0.25/50). Haiku 5.5's cache-read price was not in the table used; 0.01 USD is a tenth of input. Cache-write lines are 1.25 times input (cache_write_price), the 5-minute write rate; 1-hour writes are not modelled. Haiku 5.5's higher rate for prompts over 100K tokens (0.50/2.50 USD) is not modelled either, so a long Haiku prompt is under-charged. Each line's source says '(check)'; an admin corrects it with put_cost_line or price_model, for new usage only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":500},"end":{"line":529},"content_hash":"572b73ab9668510558ab64848f989d061e9c2a5c3e44692986f754a228b0e8c2"},"suggested_fix":"Check each figure against the published pricing page before launch; add a long-context Haiku line if the bot uses long Haiku prompts.","summary":"Seeded token prices are Anthropic list prices as cached on 2026-10-06; Haiku 5.5's cache-read price and every cache-write price are derived","supersedes":"9e4cf2eb2d068bc7b6335c7a87cd81ee988ec072a2c6fe2ca313f76ee47cff7b","tags":["claxbot","pricing","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:35:14.390704Z","id":"f8ab86dbd48fda8d39912de9eaf50311c762fb0c7450b47fbe8febf600e47250","body":{"detail":"script.compute uses 17 micro-USD per GiB-second, a generic serverless figure (the Worker Loader bills CPU time, not GiB-seconds); do.requests (0.15 USD per million) and toolpath.storage (0.20 USD per GB-month) are Durable Object list prices. The bot layer must estimate requests and bytes per step, as spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 13 notes; nothing reads actual billing. The per-run harness fee is a fixed 1 credit with no underlying cost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":583},"end":{"line":612},"content_hash":"472eedd205fb34de0a9ca8d86131c26fe43b4ffbf7a32069a95c56d7aa016f55"},"summary":"Infrastructure cost lines are estimates, not Cloudflare billing","supersedes":"5dc5409dfbc46360a91c6513c3b0612ea82828068041b0f9c05787203ffbf59c","tags":["claxbot","pricing","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:35:14.423708Z","id":"112b5f529f411ea194ea60f1af8666f54843c927fa53cde9faf04fd29416066d","body":{"detail":"charge_in splits each row's credits into free_milli (what the weekly allowance had left) and paid. Raising a person's lift mid-week makes later rows free again but leaves earlier paid rows paid, so usage_report's revenue counts credits the person now has allowance for. The spec's usage row has a boolean `free`; the store keeps the integer free_milli instead (UsageRow::free() derives the boolean) so a row straddling the allowance is split exactly.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":697},"end":{"line":742},"content_hash":"6246146b22c9265da004deae05c803e9f6aa8b1055d3c753c1baf6b8609a38b1"},"summary":"A row's free part is fixed when charged: a lift raised later does not turn paid credits back into free ones","supersedes":"275ef400517f27b1086c74cf62887213573e250e0a935ac69bb5e5eca833d415","tags":["claxbot","credits","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:35:14.458045Z","id":"cff53e1f3536d3303da58ea2eca3bf18778c5816848a2ba8d4a8c4b699fd9b20","body":{"detail":"claim_run takes a run held by another driver only after lease_secs since that claim (begin_step and commit_step now refuse a driver that does not hold it). A native daemon restarts with a new DriverId (minted once per process), so its own runs claimed before the restart stay held until the lease lapses. The native driver should release (or claim with lease 0) every live run on start, since one daemon holds a home.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":506},"end":{"line":512},"content_hash":"4eed9b27e294f5748ced810e0b627f386d85661b2d905325873e23e1db028bca"},"summary":"A restarted daemon waits out its own stale run claims unless it releases them","supersedes":"d4c12e57d4c0a2d5e69060cee473587941d7da36b781b3d4791249fe887902ca","tags":["claxbot","runs","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/secrets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:35:14.492842Z","id":"4b8901dad28646be450c541c2de76c599323026cab4bc88c9750092721040d27","body":{"detail":"Kek::load_or_create never replaces an existing secrets/kek, and open_for_use answers kek_mismatch when the KEK differs; there is no re-seal path. Restoring clax.db without its secrets/kek, or a Worker redeployed with a new CLAX_KEK, needs every key set again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":133},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"113f3bc6a205cfe544e39fe93ca1521e94b3be40f087de261a4a24a37601c88b"},"suggested_fix":"Add a rotate step that opens every row with the old KEK and seals it under the new one in one transaction.","summary":"No key-encryption-key rotation; a lost or replaced KEK makes every sealed key unopenable","supersedes":"6b6a7a33e7dd6ab9c636b64d416ac4bc86c3ab5aa98855d20b20c93f687cbe90","tags":["claxbot","secrets","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:29:23.092991Z","id":"755a2bf5a1cced7f901cf07c6b257e790166715fdf7791824d4fd5a13c68fd85","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"cff53e1f3536d3303da58ea2eca3bf18778c5816848a2ba8d4a8c4b699fd9b20","summary":"clax_bot::Driver::resume(take_over: true) (crates/clax-bot/src/driver.rs) claims every live run with lease 0 before queueing it, for the native daemon to call on start; it closes this once the server wires it.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:30:15.916762Z","id":"6808d6f072ef8578afa81fc51d58d08a06118b860300795b0a53ae6407f76d28","body":{"detail":"claim_run takes a run held by another driver only after lease_secs since that claim (begin_step and commit_step now refuse a driver that does not hold it). A native daemon restarts with a new DriverId (minted once per process), so its own runs claimed before the restart stay held until the lease lapses. The native driver should release (or claim with lease 0) every live run on start, since one daemon holds a home.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":511},"end":{"line":517},"content_hash":"4eed9b27e294f5748ced810e0b627f386d85661b2d905325873e23e1db028bca"},"summary":"A restarted daemon waits out its own stale run claims unless it releases them","supersedes":"cff53e1f3536d3303da58ea2eca3bf18778c5816848a2ba8d4a8c4b699fd9b20","tags":["claxbot","runs","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:30:15.953305Z","id":"7ccd0c6001b67d22f2f9af1d3facde89d85d15baecdf014739f8cadb470e9a51","body":{"detail":"Each DraftChange::Write stores its full content as a BLOB; the store does not bound a file's size, a draft's total, or how long an ended run's draft is kept (a stopped run's draft must stay viewable, spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 6.3). The caller (clax-bot's files.write) must cap sizes, and a later change should prune drafts of runs that ended long ago or were published.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1346},"end":{"line":1352},"content_hash":"f325b86717df6d16cb53a01e25fcfa70401e2fc07ca66842609fd40e9968b1f2"},"summary":"Run drafts are kept whole in bot_draft_files with no size cap and never pruned","supersedes":"3b82221477aba0e31d61e0f79ba28984563a45fafed0c628a7ea1d5212fcab62","tags":["claxbot","storage","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:30:15.985848Z","id":"d09ff22d6afea73fec902468a569a3d8c141ff3ffb1e8e5d7c3cb9d63ce1d44b","body":{"detail":"rust-int commit c308495e6 (2026-10-14) made push_approvals without upto (NOT NULL, no default), so the table is rebuilt. No version is recorded for such a row; 0 approves none, where the artifact's current version could approve one the owner never saw. Only a local daemon writes push_approvals, so a hosted database has no such rows. Tested by migrations::tests::repair::migration_37_carries_inbox_items_and_push_approvals_through_their_rebuilds.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1533},"end":{"line":1538},"content_hash":"509eff3ee94ddc389fc0d7753e67ce2f24f39e0c2fdde5f3f3b2d03d71a541b8"},"summary":"Migration 37 keeps a push_approvals row that lacks upto with upto = 0, so its push asks the owner again","supersedes":"10d7efccbab7cb6b6a91ecde6573bf87afbcdcb54ac2650c35e04cfa92d187b4","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:30:16.018029Z","id":"d9322447ccf856d4e411203c1b10f8367f389d95af51b864986dcaea96e9a30a","body":{"detail":"Copies of migrations 24 and 25 from 2026-10-10 (git log -S page_person -- crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs: ddfff6383, 051681542, 86fcda318, 4b6a1d656) add versions.page_person and comments.page_person, which the final migrations replace with versions.by_page/file_authors_json and page_authors. repair() does not drop or carry them: no code reads them, the meaning of their values does not map onto page_authors rows one for one, and only development homes of that week can hold them. Such a home keeps two dead nullable columns, so its schema differs from a new one's by them. tests/fixtures/old-migrations holds no fixture of that shape.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1668},"end":{"line":1722},"content_hash":"97f8ba2c1a6b0fbb7fe081538a2a7104b5856c69479604a8d5eacc2088d7c2c3"},"summary":"Migration 37's repair leaves comments.page_person and versions.page_person where an early multi-person build added them","supersedes":"745b385d5d6eb2b62989fd987133fcb6636c943d53db7ccfd00e6fcdeb8dfec2","tags":["migrations","revisit:a home made by a 2026-10-10 multi-person build is still in use","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:53:22.917427Z","id":"23c3df0941a6d139b11c57eaf60cf9364c6ed2ab532c3fe22bf64f771df4507e","body":{"detail":"Every call a script makes is journaled (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs RunHost::journal): reads keep their answers (a threads.read's comments, a db.list page), draft operations a null result. Nothing prunes the rows once their step commits, though only an open step's journal is ever read again (Tick::script, Tick::unreported_calls). A committed run's rows could be pruned at its run_end, or reads' answers dropped at commit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1350},"end":{"line":1361},"content_hash":"92152c95c44c8873a9a882474f1319fab4298453c7156b707c8ed68eea2257d6"},"summary":"Call journal rows (bot_calls) are kept for every step forever","tags":["storage","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:54:00.014298Z","id":"febf6a7175c050e80c8580e660b18d073875bdd0a9e7c350a0acb1c7c13fbefd","body":{"detail":"Each DraftChange::Write stores its full content as a BLOB; the store does not bound a file's size, a draft's total, or how long an ended run's draft is kept (a stopped run's draft must stay viewable, spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 6.3). The caller (clax-bot's files.write) must cap sizes, and a later change should prune drafts of runs that ended long ago or were published.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1362},"end":{"line":1368},"content_hash":"f325b86717df6d16cb53a01e25fcfa70401e2fc07ca66842609fd40e9968b1f2"},"summary":"Run drafts are kept whole in bot_draft_files with no size cap and never pruned","supersedes":"7ccd0c6001b67d22f2f9af1d3facde89d85d15baecdf014739f8cadb470e9a51","tags":["claxbot","storage","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:54:00.034464Z","id":"c0a3d7347f94d1517edea0d6c7330d4fe2d91a88ecf5267c783643dbfeca070a","body":{"detail":"rust-int commit c308495e6 (2026-10-14) made push_approvals without upto (NOT NULL, no default), so the table is rebuilt. No version is recorded for such a row; 0 approves none, where the artifact's current version could approve one the owner never saw. Only a local daemon writes push_approvals, so a hosted database has no such rows. Tested by migrations::tests::repair::migration_37_carries_inbox_items_and_push_approvals_through_their_rebuilds.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1549},"end":{"line":1554},"content_hash":"509eff3ee94ddc389fc0d7753e67ce2f24f39e0c2fdde5f3f3b2d03d71a541b8"},"summary":"Migration 37 keeps a push_approvals row that lacks upto with upto = 0, so its push asks the owner again","supersedes":"d09ff22d6afea73fec902468a569a3d8c141ff3ffb1e8e5d7c3cb9d63ce1d44b","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:54:00.055244Z","id":"2e4d59a6e4fa66a84aceda57eaa353de941db9afb02d5d81e1a6acadde8349ba","body":{"detail":"Copies of migrations 24 and 25 from 2026-10-10 (git log -S page_person -- crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs: ddfff6383, 051681542, 86fcda318, 4b6a1d656) add versions.page_person and comments.page_person, which the final migrations replace with versions.by_page/file_authors_json and page_authors. repair() does not drop or carry them: no code reads them, the meaning of their values does not map onto page_authors rows one for one, and only development homes of that week can hold them. Such a home keeps two dead nullable columns, so its schema differs from a new one's by them. tests/fixtures/old-migrations holds no fixture of that shape.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1684},"end":{"line":1738},"content_hash":"97f8ba2c1a6b0fbb7fe081538a2a7104b5856c69479604a8d5eacc2088d7c2c3"},"summary":"Migration 37's repair leaves comments.page_person and versions.page_person where an early multi-person build added them","supersedes":"d9322447ccf856d4e411203c1b10f8367f389d95af51b864986dcaea96e9a30a","tags":["migrations","revisit:a home made by a 2026-10-10 multi-person build is still in use","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:54:00.076100Z","id":"95446b29a5762a2b11bb6490a97f8618baa19750d9db9363fdcea6d6a180661a","body":{"detail":"claim_run takes a run held by another driver only after lease_secs since that claim (begin_step and commit_step now refuse a driver that does not hold it). A native daemon restarts with a new DriverId (minted once per process), so its own runs claimed before the restart stay held until the lease lapses. The native driver should release (or claim with lease 0) every live run on start, since one daemon holds a home.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":527},"end":{"line":533},"content_hash":"4eed9b27e294f5748ced810e0b627f386d85661b2d905325873e23e1db028bca"},"summary":"A restarted daemon waits out its own stale run claims unless it releases them","supersedes":"6808d6f072ef8578afa81fc51d58d08a06118b860300795b0a53ae6407f76d28","tags":["claxbot","runs","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:54:00.095562Z","id":"9bf20b503f753dbf31e46a7d65761e2c14dce3adbd96bac816ffbb38a49dcdb5","body":{"detail":"SEED_MODELS seeds input/cached/output micro-USD per Mtok for claude-haiku-5-5 (0.10/0.01/0.50 USD), claude-sonnet-5-5 (2/0.20/10), claude-opus-5-5 (4/0.20/20) and claude-fable-5-1 (10/0.25/50). Haiku 5.5's cache-read price was not in the table used; 0.01 USD is a tenth of input. Cache-write lines are 1.25 times input (cache_write_price), the 5-minute write rate; 1-hour writes are not modelled. Haiku 5.5's higher rate for prompts over 100K tokens (0.50/2.50 USD) is not modelled either, so a long Haiku prompt is under-charged. Each line's source says '(check)'; an admin corrects it with put_cost_line or price_model, for new usage only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":517},"end":{"line":546},"content_hash":"572b73ab9668510558ab64848f989d061e9c2a5c3e44692986f754a228b0e8c2"},"suggested_fix":"Check each figure against the published pricing page before launch; add a long-context Haiku line if the bot uses long Haiku prompts.","summary":"Seeded token prices are Anthropic list prices as cached on 2026-10-06; Haiku 5.5's cache-read price and every cache-write price are derived","supersedes":"4162a67f8452134e3fc646c7e5fdca0661b0823313a214f35a2afae1bd512773","tags":["claxbot","pricing","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:54:00.114759Z","id":"53c1ae7436b5c1df7a6480cedd8f559c6a4b1f9569597c26e30f4875b0d81cd1","body":{"detail":"script.compute uses 17 micro-USD per GiB-second, a generic serverless figure (the Worker Loader bills CPU time, not GiB-seconds); do.requests (0.15 USD per million) and toolpath.storage (0.20 USD per GB-month) are Durable Object list prices. The bot layer must estimate requests and bytes per step, as spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 13 notes; nothing reads actual billing. The per-run harness fee is a fixed 1 credit with no underlying cost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":600},"end":{"line":629},"content_hash":"472eedd205fb34de0a9ca8d86131c26fe43b4ffbf7a32069a95c56d7aa016f55"},"summary":"Infrastructure cost lines are estimates, not Cloudflare billing","supersedes":"f8ab86dbd48fda8d39912de9eaf50311c762fb0c7450b47fbe8febf600e47250","tags":["claxbot","pricing","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:54:00.135741Z","id":"72e815288e41791c8bc6a3b6c9cd15472c74834e0b4228a29ff09684cf117cfc","body":{"detail":"charge_in splits each row's credits into free_milli (what the weekly allowance had left) and paid. Raising a person's lift mid-week makes later rows free again but leaves earlier paid rows paid, so usage_report's revenue counts credits the person now has allowance for. The spec's usage row has a boolean `free`; the store keeps the integer free_milli instead (UsageRow::free() derives the boolean) so a row straddling the allowance is split exactly.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":714},"end":{"line":761},"content_hash":"d75822278b76d931c5f63b1d0f6e7bcc36e87c974c7c68ae1789ce9b473dbf7a"},"summary":"A row's free part is fixed when charged: a lift raised later does not turn paid credits back into free ones","supersedes":"112b5f529f411ea194ea60f1af8666f54843c927fa53cde9faf04fd29416066d","tags":["claxbot","credits","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:08.942998Z","id":"da4fb14ff694e693999c39eaa449786f94f16b1001a559b5177e3f6e76cf8cc4","body":{"detail":"Every call a script makes is journaled (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs RunHost::journal): reads keep their answers (a threads.read's comments, a db.list page), draft operations a null result. Nothing prunes the rows once their step commits, though only an open step's journal is ever read again (Tick::script, Tick::unreported_calls). A committed run's rows could be pruned at its run_end, or reads' answers dropped at commit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1351},"end":{"line":1362},"content_hash":"92152c95c44c8873a9a882474f1319fab4298453c7156b707c8ed68eea2257d6"},"summary":"Call journal rows (bot_calls) are kept for every step forever","supersedes":"23c3df0941a6d139b11c57eaf60cf9364c6ed2ab532c3fe22bf64f771df4507e","tags":["storage","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:08.962135Z","id":"7040ee53490a2ed442f493b37668e8ceb72bee7e9d304c733cd16c3402cf3f91","body":{"detail":"Each DraftChange::Write stores its full content as a BLOB; the store does not bound a file's size, a draft's total, or how long an ended run's draft is kept (a stopped run's draft must stay viewable, spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 6.3). The caller (clax-bot's files.write) must cap sizes, and a later change should prune drafts of runs that ended long ago or were published.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1363},"end":{"line":1369},"content_hash":"f325b86717df6d16cb53a01e25fcfa70401e2fc07ca66842609fd40e9968b1f2"},"summary":"Run drafts are kept whole in bot_draft_files with no size cap and never pruned","supersedes":"febf6a7175c050e80c8580e660b18d073875bdd0a9e7c350a0acb1c7c13fbefd","tags":["claxbot","storage","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
