{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:09.023387Z","id":"9cce0f73c8e992e95d7e40bea0ece200c985cd4789439536c8b84cf6327516de","body":{"detail":"SEED_MODELS seeds input/cached/output micro-USD per Mtok for claude-haiku-5-5 (0.10/0.01/0.50 USD), claude-sonnet-5-5 (2/0.20/10), claude-opus-5-5 (4/0.20/20) and claude-fable-5-1 (10/0.25/50). Haiku 5.5's cache-read price was not in the table used; 0.01 USD is a tenth of input. Cache-write lines are 1.25 times input (cache_write_price), the 5-minute write rate; 1-hour writes are not modelled. Haiku 5.5's higher rate for prompts over 100K tokens (0.50/2.50 USD) is not modelled either, so a long Haiku prompt is under-charged. Each line's source says '(check)'; an admin corrects it with put_cost_line or price_model, for new usage only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":544},"end":{"line":573},"content_hash":"572b73ab9668510558ab64848f989d061e9c2a5c3e44692986f754a228b0e8c2"},"suggested_fix":"Check each figure against the published pricing page before launch; add a long-context Haiku line if the bot uses long Haiku prompts.","summary":"Seeded token prices are Anthropic list prices as cached on 2026-10-06; Haiku 5.5's cache-read price and every cache-write price are derived","supersedes":"9bf20b503f753dbf31e46a7d65761e2c14dce3adbd96bac816ffbb38a49dcdb5","tags":["claxbot","pricing","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:09.043724Z","id":"d073fc18d640ef465c5d7e914af5cbefcf97d8e3e7e2b83e08448865898f3707","body":{"detail":"script.compute uses 17 micro-USD per GiB-second, a generic serverless figure (the Worker Loader bills CPU time, not GiB-seconds); do.requests (0.15 USD per million) and toolpath.storage (0.20 USD per GB-month) are Durable Object list prices. The bot layer must estimate requests and bytes per step, as spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 13 notes; nothing reads actual billing. The per-run harness fee is a fixed 1 credit with no underlying cost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":627},"end":{"line":656},"content_hash":"472eedd205fb34de0a9ca8d86131c26fe43b4ffbf7a32069a95c56d7aa016f55"},"summary":"Infrastructure cost lines are estimates, not Cloudflare billing","supersedes":"53c1ae7436b5c1df7a6480cedd8f559c6a4b1f9569597c26e30f4875b0d81cd1","tags":["claxbot","pricing","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:09.063056Z","id":"77c2b8f85307cc8cd36179adae214f67d6811b51a6e47d4b688c37b2c363f92a","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/feedback.rs give_untargeted_in drops the untargeted rows whose comment the session already has a row for, then retargets the rest and clears notified_at and push_failed_at; send_in, Store::send_to_named and Store::handoff call it. take_in (crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs:373-384) runs the same DELETE and UPDATE inline and uses the UPDATE's row count. The two copies agree today; a change to one (another column to clear) must be made to both. Replace the inline statements with `let given = super::feedback::give_untargeted_in(tx, tid, sid)?;`.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":373},"end":{"line":384},"content_hash":"aa84df2792040d26314833e358ad750e5baa06e53bdccf7aab21af46eaf1dc6d"},"summary":"take_in hands a thread's untargeted rows to the taker with its own copy of feedback::give_untargeted_in's two statements","supersedes":"bc42705147fcac8c5d7e7b8487f48e78103055c2bec7e8d6558526928fdfe79f","tags":["review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:09.084739Z","id":"9b6bc51825adb7a86f0084d64246b7ccbf83a7738e5edc603124af68410517b3","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/threads.rs:841-853, record f05ee8bd.\n\nBefore 274f3832 the clip was written inside the thread transaction after the liveness, version and anchor checks. create_thread_inner now takes the content lock, checks liveness and puts the clip first; invalid_anchor, unknown_version and route checks fail later in the transaction and the clip is removed at threads.rs:926. A failed removal is only logged, leaving an unreferenced clip under clips/ (FsContent) or the clip-<thread> asset key. The content lock also makes a clipped thread wait for a publish of the same artifact in progress. Checking the version and anchor in a read before the put would keep refusals free of content I/O.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":840},"end":{"line":852},"content_hash":"55721932152d318f5441cccd6a0eba409d1de7a73bedf32d33e2e75dd31d2b8a"},"summary":"A clipped thread now writes its clip before the version and anchor are checked, so every refused clipped request writes and deletes a clip","supersedes":"115c3cbdc86d98ea5bc94a48ad2a2f52ab71f94f5c089139932e60823be5b9a7","tags":["content-store","review","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:09.106217Z","id":"dc708ff01c1ecb5e6f6d86229d2da06dda80094a1e4abb1289a2a0190aa5a694","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1154-1174, record f6358543.\n\nA push to Cloudflare Artifacts whose pushed event is lost, late or never delivered (no subscription, locally: the queue is simulated and receives none, crates/clax-worker/wrangler.jsonc queues) stays unrecorded until the next publish of the artifact, so viewers see the older version meanwhile. The prototype also reconciles lazily on reads, at most every RECONCILE_EVERY_MS (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts reconcileLazily). Fix: reconcile from the artifact read routes when main has moved past the current version's commit, rate-limited per artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1151},"end":{"line":1171},"content_hash":"0e964bf56304bdae01de79078bc14ac3f2efdcccc88f3520368fba6e0fd6bf28"},"summary":"Pushed commits are recorded on a push, an Artifacts event or a publish, but not when an artifact is read","supersedes":"6dbd24d8ca07de749b55acdb966d0f733668729ba077d8793a3208070c02dafe","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:09.126179Z","id":"3656c1e5397be6e9aca57bdf4147c4be69d178fb504adfbc7a391e938c145f72","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1246-1268, record 8c8d734d.\n\nrecord_version_locked calls revoke_blind_tokens with the publisher for VersionStep::Write when expected > 0, which is ContentStore::repo_tokens (DoLedger: POST token/live to RepoDO) even when no token is held. That is one subrequest on every publish's path (time to usable), plus a Visibility per agent token. Skipping needs to know no agent token is live without asking RepoDO, for example a held-token count the instance keeps from mint and revoke answers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1293},"end":{"line":1315},"content_hash":"1b2e03465f769a1d419beb6d2bc69ef9c92b6239ab7701881342bbd69dac3f3c"},"summary":"Every publish of an existing artifact asks the push ledger for the repository's tokens before its commit: on the Worker one RepoDO call per publish","supersedes":"b3ddffd255fec19e18df53ad65cf1e950d390c7ae90d58dd8a2a17e1c9e1a351","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:09.145666Z","id":"ff97a62d2bb286e7e15365f86e56a63b10a7bee5609a9f2805623e12738ca9fe","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1284-1293, record bd81b2ff.\n\nArtifactLocks (content/mod.rs) serialise version writes within one process, so there the loser waits and then sees Conflict (concurrent_publishes_with_same_if_version_yield_one_winner). Across processes the loser's content write fails first; it is mapped to Conflict only when the artifact has already moved past the expected version. Nothing is corrupted (the loser removes nothing it did not write). The daemon is the only writer of versions today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1331},"end":{"line":1340},"content_hash":"a077ecaccb7d3bf6415711bbe4967512283b6957f9885a76f4fc55e1b23d1f7a"},"summary":"Two processes publishing the same version at once: the loser gets the content store's AlreadyExists error, not Conflict, while the winner has not yet recorded it","supersedes":"df2d0cb05a2220e63b4c9b7580be5a967e85a24c8367324213a738e89b82e06d","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:09.167166Z","id":"197295aecc76f2319e99b2d56cd3a916e880619850c40666a0b309169655827b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1415-1432, record 7e511288.\n\nStore::version_meta resolves p.person, else the session's person, else the owner, before the content write; version_authors (artifacts.rs:817) resolves the row's person again inside the transaction. They agree today (tests a_version_write_names_its_publisher_agent_and_note), but a change to one rule that misses the other makes git's Clax-Publisher disagree with the row.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1462},"end":{"line":1479},"content_hash":"659cd84b5806cab81ba2b715b2b2ccbb63d959613000065b76ba0e6914ffc86e"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the person once before the content lock and pass it to version_authors.","summary":"The publisher the content store is told and the one the version row records are resolved by separate code","supersedes":"98301473f1f373e458193db70f6a438e1b18328b2aee02d82f711e3b7a2b5cc0","tags":["review","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:09.186217Z","id":"2c37029b02828c934e828a9b4780bd19b57331e09c3884c2407398d106606827","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs:757-783, record 102e3b6a.\n\nMeasured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":780},"end":{"line":806},"content_hash":"52e810ab13e4b4c1906f3b6d191494a2b7dbc5c619a6c49ab2c0c512f581f5a7"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"296245160b1b37ea7f76479fa990b7ffc670a105cb1fc988afc142a9ffefe725","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:09.205567Z","id":"824e68bf5b338ead176b3940c5567b44a2aae108a94469daf8fd54a71f3cffb1","body":{"detail":"charge_in splits each row's credits into free_milli (what the weekly allowance had left) and paid. Raising a person's lift mid-week makes later rows free again but leaves earlier paid rows paid, so usage_report's revenue counts credits the person now has allowance for. The spec's usage row has a boolean `free`; the store keeps the integer free_milli instead (UsageRow::free() derives the boolean) so a row straddling the allowance is split exactly.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":741},"end":{"line":801},"content_hash":"f0e8aab29e983ee8904d40ccaa4aa61d54bdf58133ebe269a25d2312aa9c2eca"},"summary":"A row's free part is fixed when charged: a lift raised later does not turn paid credits back into free ones","supersedes":"72e815288e41791c8bc6a3b6c9cd15472c74834e0b4228a29ff09684cf117cfc","tags":["claxbot","credits","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:57.910127Z","id":"74dc6d7880b1766be31d6d772e300a8c93a787d3dda432f46215f03a2ba1ff37","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1154-1174, record f6358543.\n\nA push to Cloudflare Artifacts whose pushed event is lost, late or never delivered (no subscription, locally: the queue is simulated and receives none, crates/clax-worker/wrangler.jsonc queues) stays unrecorded until the next publish of the artifact, so viewers see the older version meanwhile. The prototype also reconciles lazily on reads, at most every RECONCILE_EVERY_MS (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts reconcileLazily). Fix: reconcile from the artifact read routes when main has moved past the current version's commit, rate-limited per artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1196},"end":{"line":1216},"content_hash":"0e964bf56304bdae01de79078bc14ac3f2efdcccc88f3520368fba6e0fd6bf28"},"summary":"Pushed commits are recorded on a push, an Artifacts event or a publish, but not when an artifact is read","supersedes":"dc708ff01c1ecb5e6f6d86229d2da06dda80094a1e4abb1289a2a0190aa5a694","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:57.930864Z","id":"9e981f04fd64ac201842d212af0fe42aab302c692a10a991408e7ce5fde6f481","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1246-1268, record 8c8d734d.\n\nrecord_version_locked calls revoke_blind_tokens with the publisher for VersionStep::Write when expected > 0, which is ContentStore::repo_tokens (DoLedger: POST token/live to RepoDO) even when no token is held. That is one subrequest on every publish's path (time to usable), plus a Visibility per agent token. Skipping needs to know no agent token is live without asking RepoDO, for example a held-token count the instance keeps from mint and revoke answers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1340},"end":{"line":1362},"content_hash":"1b2e03465f769a1d419beb6d2bc69ef9c92b6239ab7701881342bbd69dac3f3c"},"summary":"Every publish of an existing artifact asks the push ledger for the repository's tokens before its commit: on the Worker one RepoDO call per publish","supersedes":"3656c1e5397be6e9aca57bdf4147c4be69d178fb504adfbc7a391e938c145f72","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:57.951079Z","id":"c17fcd31f86e23938f0b386683d6d3ee2410cfeb4467fc3d61e976473575e58a","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1284-1293, record bd81b2ff.\n\nArtifactLocks (content/mod.rs) serialise version writes within one process, so there the loser waits and then sees Conflict (concurrent_publishes_with_same_if_version_yield_one_winner). Across processes the loser's content write fails first; it is mapped to Conflict only when the artifact has already moved past the expected version. Nothing is corrupted (the loser removes nothing it did not write). The daemon is the only writer of versions today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1378},"end":{"line":1387},"content_hash":"a077ecaccb7d3bf6415711bbe4967512283b6957f9885a76f4fc55e1b23d1f7a"},"summary":"Two processes publishing the same version at once: the loser gets the content store's AlreadyExists error, not Conflict, while the winner has not yet recorded it","supersedes":"ff97a62d2bb286e7e15365f86e56a63b10a7bee5609a9f2805623e12738ca9fe","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:57.971112Z","id":"cd8c71c0ae96230e7b804cd67124b732527d36b47df98636b2830a62add0f69b","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1415-1432, record 7e511288.\n\nStore::version_meta resolves p.person, else the session's person, else the owner, before the content write; version_authors (artifacts.rs:817) resolves the row's person again inside the transaction. They agree today (tests a_version_write_names_its_publisher_agent_and_note), but a change to one rule that misses the other makes git's Clax-Publisher disagree with the row.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1509},"end":{"line":1526},"content_hash":"659cd84b5806cab81ba2b715b2b2ccbb63d959613000065b76ba0e6914ffc86e"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the person once before the content lock and pass it to version_authors.","summary":"The publisher the content store is told and the one the version row records are resolved by separate code","supersedes":"197295aecc76f2319e99b2d56cd3a916e880619850c40666a0b309169655827b","tags":["review","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.277111Z","id":"94bcaf5105b0fcc29e7bd3d807ea78e8f98cf54d9067c96858d6cb8aad4020aa","body":{"detail":"claim_run takes a run held by another driver only after lease_secs since that claim (begin_step and commit_step now refuse a driver that does not hold it). A native daemon restarts with a new DriverId (minted once per process), so its own runs claimed before the restart stay held until the lease lapses. The native driver should release (or claim with lease 0) every live run on start, since one daemon holds a home.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":591},"end":{"line":597},"content_hash":"4eed9b27e294f5748ced810e0b627f386d85661b2d905325873e23e1db028bca"},"summary":"A restarted daemon waits out its own stale run claims unless it releases them","supersedes":"95446b29a5762a2b11bb6490a97f8618baa19750d9db9363fdcea6d6a180661a","tags":["claxbot","runs","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.299486Z","id":"7bdacc9e7bac4493fb5a906480f9acc6a9e561366b4a9ac09353ef0ad17a4da7","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs:757-783, record 102e3b6a.\n\nMeasured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":787},"end":{"line":813},"content_hash":"52e810ab13e4b4c1906f3b6d191494a2b7dbc5c619a6c49ab2c0c512f581f5a7"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"2c37029b02828c934e828a9b4780bd19b57331e09c3884c2407398d106606827","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:57.298278Z","id":"97eb77d913e9b18e829ee9d70e112ae835f9cf0e9ab490370f63d353b17f76e2","body":{"detail":"Every call a script makes is journaled (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs RunHost::journal): reads keep their answers (a threads.read's comments, a db.list page), draft operations a null result. Nothing prunes the rows once their step commits, though only an open step's journal is ever read again (Tick::script, Tick::unreported_calls). A committed run's rows could be pruned at its run_end, or reads' answers dropped at commit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1353},"end":{"line":1364},"content_hash":"92152c95c44c8873a9a882474f1319fab4298453c7156b707c8ed68eea2257d6"},"summary":"Call journal rows (bot_calls) are kept for every step forever","supersedes":"da4fb14ff694e693999c39eaa449786f94f16b1001a559b5177e3f6e76cf8cc4","tags":["storage","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:57.429788Z","id":"7956d1227cf1ac0ab6547ed016dc743e7dcf0419e4ab2084974090371f439177","body":{"detail":"Each DraftChange::Write stores its full content as a BLOB; the store does not bound a file's size, a draft's total, or how long an ended run's draft is kept (a stopped run's draft must stay viewable, spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 6.3). The caller (clax-bot's files.write) must cap sizes, and a later change should prune drafts of runs that ended long ago or were published.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1365},"end":{"line":1371},"content_hash":"f325b86717df6d16cb53a01e25fcfa70401e2fc07ca66842609fd40e9968b1f2"},"summary":"Run drafts are kept whole in bot_draft_files with no size cap and never pruned","supersedes":"7040ee53490a2ed442f493b37668e8ceb72bee7e9d304c733cd16c3402cf3f91","tags":["claxbot","storage","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:57.519330Z","id":"67bf21a85522d9b8bd81bab2eb82aeb0e1697d81c3d41ec8d9109dc213920ae6","body":{"detail":"rust-int commit c308495e6 (2026-10-14) made push_approvals without upto (NOT NULL, no default), so the table is rebuilt. No version is recorded for such a row; 0 approves none, where the artifact's current version could approve one the owner never saw. Only a local daemon writes push_approvals, so a hosted database has no such rows. Tested by migrations::tests::repair::migration_37_carries_inbox_items_and_push_approvals_through_their_rebuilds.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1552},"end":{"line":1557},"content_hash":"509eff3ee94ddc389fc0d7753e67ce2f24f39e0c2fdde5f3f3b2d03d71a541b8"},"summary":"Migration 37 keeps a push_approvals row that lacks upto with upto = 0, so its push asks the owner again","supersedes":"34df70d60071a6c2f4d61add4dfe73a5825c7441e5337b612f1cf2294343ea80","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:57.561514Z","id":"6604697f87f19e7b34f32ef1376a28d90b324047f3975e0c5ca37834d73dc20a","body":{"detail":"Copies of migrations 24 and 25 from 2026-10-10 (git log -S page_person -- crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs: ddfff6383, 051681542, 86fcda318, 4b6a1d656) add versions.page_person and comments.page_person, which the final migrations replace with versions.by_page/file_authors_json and page_authors. repair() does not drop or carry them: no code reads them, the meaning of their values does not map onto page_authors rows one for one, and only development homes of that week can hold them. Such a home keeps two dead nullable columns, so its schema differs from a new one's by them. tests/fixtures/old-migrations holds no fixture of that shape.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1687},"end":{"line":1741},"content_hash":"97f8ba2c1a6b0fbb7fe081538a2a7104b5856c69479604a8d5eacc2088d7c2c3"},"summary":"Migration 37's repair leaves comments.page_person and versions.page_person where an early multi-person build added them","supersedes":"e70d22d61d74dbac0f6c2e361bf3e84f682cec51fbe35f23db3e8b5cd28874bb","tags":["migrations","revisit:a home made by a 2026-10-10 multi-person build is still in use","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:43:26.303402Z","id":"fad075e82fd5fb2342d2ee4980c706ec343fd37969f153b60c652c002d0cd29e","body":{"detail":"claim_run takes a run held by another driver only after lease_secs since that claim (begin_step and commit_step now refuse a driver that does not hold it). A native daemon restarts with a new DriverId (minted once per process), so its own runs claimed before the restart stay held until the lease lapses. The native driver should release (or claim with lease 0) every live run on start, since one daemon holds a home.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":759},"end":{"line":765},"content_hash":"4eed9b27e294f5748ced810e0b627f386d85661b2d905325873e23e1db028bca"},"summary":"A restarted daemon waits out its own stale run claims unless it releases them","supersedes":"94bcaf5105b0fcc29e7bd3d807ea78e8f98cf54d9067c96858d6cb8aad4020aa","tags":["claxbot","runs","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T04:16:59.349802Z","id":"b64fd8cd88b53f2327d6204ba0e869ea0e88f2fe378bbcdc8fa11a734ac05c11","body":{"detail":"The app's recovery (_settleDocs in apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart) sent a record's document writes again with their pins when docs_done was false. On the queue a version's documents are written only inside its publish step, and an imported record's publish:<base> step is already committed, so the job the import writes (turn:1 and publish:<base>, then the reply) ends done and the record's db writes are never made. Test a_ledger_change_with_nothing_left_to_apply_is_done (base 2: documents never written, replied) imports it queued with a reply owing no thread.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":634},"end":{"line":667},"content_hash":"39b71fa2355b01786bd6b304f5e37fe5dcb04913404ea942cd4beea10826e35f"},"suggested_fix":"Either a step the queue commits for a landed version's pinned document writes (the store's batch with if_version pins in the step's transaction), or the import leaving such a record out and saying so in left_out.","summary":"A ledger change whose version landed with documents unwritten imports without them: the queue has no step that writes a landed version's documents","tags":["queue","import","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T05:10:21.379098Z","id":"bba5e5a7dba4b650143ceaae43cf90a16897ecc85d079363eb6efb0366381d92","body":{"detail":"Not taken: SQLite's NOCASE folds ASCII letters only, so 'Ärger' and 'ärger' would both be accepted. Migration 41 stores fold (clax_core::tags::fold, Rust's to_lowercase) with a UNIQUE constraint, one column more than the tags table the feature was first sketched with (id, name, colour, description, created_at, updated_at).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1213},"end":{"line":1232},"content_hash":"f9849f7e70e591978bbe2f18709d7cffa67d73224f8d14bb90afe33a670ca84f"},"summary":"Unique tag names through COLLATE NOCASE instead of a fold column","supersedes":"0769e2a22d9b899293ce7369395442afba5c63de45f317de70e05080399ffce9","tags":["revisit:tag names need locale-aware or NFC-normalised comparison","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T05:10:21.928293Z","id":"e55979d40a6c36ac310ff8363eb84bf88d1fcdcbd6d49424f399face9d1f9ace","body":{"detail":"Layouts adopt_earlier_flutter_app recognises: the app's from 24 (no invites table), from 27 (invites, no hosted_setup), from 38 (hosted_setup, no questions.thread_id), and from 38 + k + 1 after the first k of MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38 (k = 0: from 39, the phone's and Mac's homes at 43, build 652f225fcffa; k = 2: from 41, builds up to 652f225fcffa, homes at 41 to 46; k = 3 is this numbering). An adopted home gets the migrations it lacks below APP_MIGRATION (42), SQL and Rust step each, after the copy Store::open takes, and its user_version becomes the app migration it holds here (43 -> 46, 46 -> 47). Tests: migrations::tests::every_installed_home_opens_at_the_last_migration_keeping_every_table_and_row (every fixture in tests/fixtures/old-migrations, flutter-app-652f225fcffa, flutter-app-652f225fcffa and main-25f2a9169 among them), the_owners_homes_are_adopted_or_migrated_by_their_schema, the_app_after_every_k_of_mains_migrations_opens_under_this_numbering, every_layout_adopts_into_a_later_main_numbering, a_home_at_each_of_mains_versions_gets_the_apps_migrations_after_a_copy.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1233},"end":{"line":1390},"content_hash":"a7a59c527cd5da2daffe26ff185b4ddb49c11f758107993ff65bcab78c95beb5"},"summary":"The app's migrations are 42 to 47, after main's 39 to 41 (legal_agreements, briefs, tags); homes of every earlier flutter-app numbering are adopted by schema","supersedes":"b79e68dedf116715ea171f76c54f6ce3eee8840af63364e3dfdf9383e2c816e1","tags":["migrations","rebase","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T05:10:22.424913Z","id":"1a78295f7305f73d5df3149ba171ba215fe2e911ede980a7c37362db6babaf7a","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/tests/fixtures/old-migrations/flutter-app-652f225fcffa.sql (and flutter-app-652f225fcffa.sql, the same migrations from the build last installed on the phone) replay the old migrations' SQL with rows the tests insert. crates/clax-embed/tests/old_homes.rs opens crates/clax-embed/tests/fixtures/homes/flutter-app-43.sql, a dump of the macOS app's home, through the core (reply e4a3a8b7). The owner's phone home itself has not been copied off and opened by this numbering's build; spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §10.2 asks for that before any install.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1533},"end":{"line":1660},"content_hash":"639cc3dc7f55d121abf036cc51fea4c0cee7a97fbcff2bfd55ec833445fd170a"},"suggested_fix":"Copy the phone's home off (adb exec-out run-as) and open the copy with this build on the Mac, comparing counts, before flashing.","summary":"Adoption of an installed home at 43 is tested only on a home the store's tests build from the 652f225fcffa fixture, not on a home written by the installed app's own clax","supersedes":"a12d81ff2ea90885dd2f7ef01f3158e2439a188a76c31a575578ce567fedc53a","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T05:10:22.788238Z","id":"a1d56f8d4bfa3058d76abcd5ed03ba2df923a30879cdd9d49d2a90d6ba10b92c","body":{"detail":"Commits 652f225fcffa to 652f225fcffa's parent made the jobs migration (then 46) without job_step_marks; 652f225fcffa to 652f225fcffa's parent added it as 47; 652f225fcffa folded it into 46. Since main's 41 moved the app's migrations to 42 to 47, such a home at 46 is of the earlier numbering from 41 (k = 2): adopt_earlier_flutter_app holds it to the jobs migration's tables (jobs_tables_disagree) and refuses it with MigrationFailed naming job_step_marks, leaving it as it was, instead of opening it and failing at the first publish step. A home at 47 from 652f225fcffa to 652f225fcffa's parent is refused too (its version is not one of the from-41 layout's, 41 to 46). Only agents' dev homes can hold either shape; AGENTS.md has a branch's dev homes reset, not upgraded. Test: migrations::tests::a_database_whose_jobs_tables_disagree_is_refused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1433},"end":{"line":1447},"content_hash":"9d77f220ec1c8f7113eca1abb029e119043807bef34f474dccd1120ad7c1371b"},"suggested_fix":"Reset such a dev home (move its clax.db aside).","summary":"A dev home of builds 652f225fcffa to 652f225fcffa's parent, at 46 without job_step_marks, is now refused on open","supersedes":"12475f7b271acc4604b2b57d69373862a682d462abc7231cb06eb3db709e2dec","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:02:33.180922Z","id":"27bf735697388bdbc60f4ffe92b733cab7fd3ca25df3d6361b3027a6923eca39","body":{"detail":"adopt_earlier_flutter_app (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs) knows the app's migrations by APP_MIGRATION_MARKS, which still lists six (42 to 47). A home at 48 opened by a build whose numbering inserts a main migration before APP_MIGRATION gets first..=last = 42..=47 and is refused (its version is not one of that build's), left unchanged. migrations::tests::a_home_of_this_numbering_takes_a_later_main_migration_and_the_apps_renumbering now builds its home only up to JOBS_MIGRATION (47) for that reason. Main and the app are one line since f1c07f346, so new migrations are appended and the case should not arise; no installed build holds 48.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1388},"end":{"line":1430},"content_hash":"86ae2d3e9f145670b9e9f7853b2e1a14681786bafdaf238b7fe358f0119b9353"},"suggested_fix":"If a main migration is ever inserted below the app's again, add Mark::Table(\"app_bundles\") to APP_MIGRATION_MARKS and extend the frozen-fixture adoption tests to seven app migrations.","summary":"Migration 48 (app_bundles and the rest) has no mark in APP_MIGRATION_MARKS, so a later numbering that places a main migration below the app's refuses a home at 48","tags":["migration","risk","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:02:33.181029Z","id":"c7d2faa98ab56d077bc2a94aab3da0f1bba888ab5e4e379ec19a9f2332e25fd0","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md §5.9 says the bundle is counted against the version's size limit. Store::put_app_bundle_async refuses only bundles over MAX_BUNDLE_BYTES (32 MiB); it does not add the bundle's size to the version's files when checking the version size cap, so a version near its cap may carry up to 32 MiB more.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":174},"end":{"line":267},"content_hash":"872ef881591a59882755645d7f1c4f76451bacac3aa280bbdb792a93a8d5083c"},"suggested_fix":"Decide whether the remote's bundle route (Task 2) adds the bundle's size to the version's size before calling put_app_bundle_async, or whether the separate cap stands.","summary":"A stored bundle is capped at MAX_BUNDLE_BYTES on its own, not counted against its version's size limit","tags":["app-push","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:02:33.181068Z","id":"9be460c9927da35dc76426758a335c3f4ee1fd5e5eda103356dd6a715608284a","body":{"detail":"versions.content_sha256 is content_manifest_sha256 over the version's files, written as sha256:<hex>, and is NULL on versions written before content hashes. A bundle whose content hash is computed another way (bare hex, or over a different file set such as one including the bundle's own manifest) is refused bundle_mismatch, and every bundle for a version with a NULL hash is refused. The app's bundle writer and the core's push (plan Tasks 4 and 9) must compute it with clax_core::audit::content_manifest_sha256 over the published files.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":107},"end":{"line":112},"content_hash":"c9c9cca9a8c9c0794d732622f78d45b4a307aa4108f86798f826a3ff8f29eb30"},"summary":"bundle_mismatch compares the caller's content_sha256 to versions.content_sha256 as strings (sha256:<hex> of the file manifest)","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:32:16.492289Z","id":"8eb28e5c1e9768a255f512f682967d4445a32b7a693b90f78049c301250bd5b4","body":{"detail":"Failure: put_app_bundle with bundle_version 7 on version 1, then 1<<63 on version 2, then 8 on version 3: the third is accepted (Ok(8)) because the row stores (1<<63) as i64 = i64::MIN and SELECT MAX(bundle_version) answers 7. The release counter goes back, which bundle_version_order (lines 135-147) exists to refuse. Shown with a scratch test in crates/clax-store/tests/app_bundles.rs on 8385aac40, not committed. The app's Dart ints cannot produce such a value, but the clax-bundle-version header of the hosted PUT bundle route (plan Task 2) can carry one.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":225},"end":{"line":238},"content_hash":"545cfa9adbff18f035c4782fe9f68d3101f7a9a1bb5716f41c6cc8cb173c7a52"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse bundle_version > i64::MAX as u64 with Invalid bundle_version_order (or invalid_args) before the checks, and test 1<<63.","summary":"A bundle_version above i64::MAX is stored as a negative number, so a later lower release counter is accepted","tags":["review","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:32:16.492566Z","id":"e97c89f9a85b4b53cb75f5e6ba2854eb8229b2dd2a11944b5d1eb9083e2340f7","body":{"detail":"check_bundle compares content_sha256 to the version's (lines 107-112) before it looks for the held row (lines 113-121), so a retry of the same bytes with another content_sha256 is refused, not answered. Lineage and bundle_version are ignored on the replay, as documented.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":160},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"51a09cc6c625c95b78742685f980f8a94e6a799e271ddf5ff9b9b025522f2c20"},"suggested_fix":"Say 'whatever its lineage and release counter' in the doc, or move the held-row check first.","summary":"The doc says the same bytes again answer the held row whatever the other arguments, but a different content_sha256 is refused bundle_mismatch first","tags":["review","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/device.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:32:16.492921Z","id":"af90eb5144ddb530b50921750a1632c7872c291b7f2d8b1e299551ba5bddc596","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md §5.2 has the approval page say what the device may do, sharing included, and approve_device (device.rs:233-238) marks the grant person_device for kind clax-app. peek_device returns only client_name, peer_ip and the times, so a person approving a code someone else started as clax-app is not shown the wider right. Plan Task 3 does not list device.rs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":63},"content_hash":"dae1167b1cf91dcfabfde6519bd12bb038f79a859724d0f26c545aab6bdac8fa"},"suggested_fix":"Add client_kind to DeviceRequest and peek_device's SELECT; the approval page names the sharing right for clax-app.","summary":"DeviceRequest carries no client_kind, so the approval page cannot tell a Clax app sign-in (whose token may manage sharing) from an agent's","tags":["review","security","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:32:16.493261Z","id":"71f8354aefa51a35bdd9692323d50757d9b96b39a26525774f90487ca67b8e60","body":{"detail":"Spec §5.6 has artifacts created by an app publish start with comments off. create_artifact (artifacts.rs:1113) takes no comments value and the column defaults to 1, so the hosted POST /api/artifacts with comments: false (plan Task 2) leaves the artifact open to comments between the two transactions, and for good if the second fails.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":268},"end":{"line":290},"content_hash":"15478d96e2b91401369b70d01dee3311f1a566f22335eebfde332f507d5c287d"},"suggested_fix":"Let create_artifact_async take the initial comments value and write it in the INSERT at artifacts.rs:1185.","summary":"No store call creates an artifact with comments off: an app publish must create it and then set_comments in a second transaction","tags":["review","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:32:16.494910Z","id":"443b04d3749f944509108b7725a09326b4ac11d840afc52755755997a39e4e57","body":{"detail":"The version's size limit is clax_core::publish::MAX_BODY_BYTES (64 MiB, crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs:11). put_app_bundle_async checks only MAX_BUNDLE_BYTES; it should also refuse when the version's files' total plus the bundle's size is over MAX_BODY_BYTES.","kind":"comment","references":"c7d2faa98ab56d077bc2a94aab3da0f1bba888ab5e4e379ec19a9f2332e25fd0","summary":"The spec settles this: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-app-push-pull-design.md:449-454 (§5.9) says the stored bundle is counted against the version's size limit, so it is a conformance gap, not an owner decision","tags":["review","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:54:00.429813Z","id":"10cba325cfce58f62894fb1aefb5f4032f277c6d10a59c0e31be58283a5be79e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a05a1fab4","summary":"check_bundle refuses bundle_too_large when the version's files (versions.files_json sizes) plus the bundle exceed clax_core::publish::MAX_BODY_BYTES. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all PASSED; just test-affected 6b408ac93: Executed 269 out of 324 tests: 324 tests pass. app_bundles::tests::a_bundle_counts_against_its_versions_size_limit passes and fails with the check replaced by `if false`.","supersedes":"c7d2faa98ab56d077bc2a94aab3da0f1bba888ab5e4e379ec19a9f2332e25fd0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:54:00.511151Z","id":"8fdc85f2bee6537f40dffe5767223906650c4066337080188f973aa489f54e8a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a05a1fab4","summary":"put_app_bundle_async refuses invalid_args for bundle_version over i64::MAX before anything is written. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all PASSED; just test-affected 6b408ac93: Executed 269 out of 324 tests: 324 tests pass. tests/app_bundles.rs a_bundle_version_over_what_the_database_keeps_is_refused passes and fails with the check removed.","supersedes":"8eb28e5c1e9768a255f512f682967d4445a32b7a693b90f78049c301250bd5b4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:54:00.645557Z","id":"6195ede424dc222c4ce12c23e55165f07be509483711f9e35301e2933db329f1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a05a1fab4","summary":"The doc on put_app_bundle_async now says the replay needs the version's content_sha256 and that another content_sha256 is refused first; it also lists invalid_args and the version size limit under bundle_too_large.","supersedes":"e97c89f9a85b4b53cb75f5e6ba2854eb8229b2dd2a11944b5d1eb9083e2340f7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/device.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:54:01.409405Z","id":"ab304cd5fa16e720c02d57cc99224391d88044af67daabe0e33b1894f14f8f2c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a05a1fab4","summary":"DeviceRequest has client_kind: Option<String>, read by peek_device. device::tests::device_kind_clax_app_marks_grant asserts it for each kind and fails with client_kind read as None. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all PASSED; just test-affected 6b408ac93: Executed 269 out of 324 tests: 324 tests pass. ","supersedes":"af90eb5144ddb530b50921750a1632c7872c291b7f2d8b1e299551ba5bddc596","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:54:01.707228Z","id":"40051e56cdfecf0aa25dbf19f8802ffbef2d8ee366dfbad5a9df4e34e26fb98d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a05a1fab4","summary":"Store::create_artifact_with_comments(_async) sets artifacts.comments in version 1's transaction (create_artifact_then_async's then); create_artifact keeps the default. artifacts::tests::an_artifact_is_created_with_the_comments_it_is_given passes and fails when the update ignores its value. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all PASSED; just test-affected 6b408ac93: Executed 269 out of 324 tests: 324 tests pass. ","supersedes":"71f8354aefa51a35bdd9692323d50757d9b96b39a26525774f90487ca67b8e60","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T05:54:01.924872Z","id":"58fd9675ebcc969ff9bc90268c7cd188ce76e7cbd4fd5e47ceef6c8bcf36b5e1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a05a1fab4","summary":"APP_MIGRATION_MARKS ends with Mark::Table(\"app_bundles\"); MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38's and APP_MIGRATION_MARKS' docs say a migration appended after the app's is the app's. migrations::tests::a_home_of_this_numbering_takes_a_later_main_migration_and_the_apps_renumbering opens a home at 48 under a numbering with a main 42 and reaches 49; it fails with the mark renamed to a missing table. The earlier-layout adoption tests stay at six app migrations (EARLIER_APP_MIGRATIONS). bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all PASSED; just test-affected 6b408ac93: Executed 269 out of 324 tests: 324 tests pass. ","supersedes":"27bf735697388bdbc60f4ffe92b733cab7fd3ca25df3d6361b3027a6923eca39","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/app_bundles.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T08:37:25.428030Z","id":"c66728bd9da7947300a2572976182aba52b462b8b50e5ba790f5a57912b9ee26","body":{"detail":"bundle_version may be anything up to i64::MAX (put_app_bundle_async). check_bundle refuses each later bundle whose bundle_version is not above the highest stored, so a bundle uploaded with i64::MAX (by an editor, or by a client bug) makes every later PUT /api/artifacts/<aid>/versions/<n>/bundle answer 400 bundle_version_order. Neither the owner nor the route can remove a bundle row, so the app can never publish an update again on that artifact.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":158},"end":{"line":172},"content_hash":"be018d771e3b81ba41453f0e40f1d5a002e86e2582e1ad6f9411d8eaecacf92a"},"suggested_fix":"Bound the step (for example bundle_version at most the highest plus some margin), or give the owner a way to drop a version's bundle.","summary":"One bundle with a huge bundle_version blocks every later bundle of the artifact, with no way back","tags":["review","app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:06:53.716466Z","id":"46715b0dbdefdd2fbe560690e263ae1da29793f82fa1ed607648f00a164f7800","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs:297-333, record 245fe67c.\n\nThe prototype names a guest 'Name (guest)' wherever Clax shows a name to an agent or an approver. Here a guest is a plain viewer row with viewers.guest = 1; feedback, comments_read and approval views show the bare name. Names cannot collide with members' or other guests' (check_guest_name), which limits impersonation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":310},"end":{"line":346},"content_hash":"fa6b1bcabd7d4ab1064bfd5c639d34232f3e0b5b95de9eb1b91c01616fba37b0"},"suggested_fix":"Mark guest authors in the agent-facing views and approval cards.","summary":"Guests are not labelled as guests to agents or approvers","supersedes":"c7d64cc60b5c58a54fdddf71a734327f4b75e17c12f3178caf05aac74e9263d3","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:44:35.581229Z","id":"9404ce76f727b359494529094d04a1c676a451791800f51c7931bc36259a8c08","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs adds forked_from to the create audit record (create_record(...).with(\"forked_from\", ...)); create_artifact_forked_from_async sets forked_from_id and forked_from_version in version 1's transaction after the create record is written, so the audit log does not say where the artifact came from.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1154},"end":{"line":1194},"content_hash":"31439096d03b6f292e4924405b3bdf23c1b9012af75d74047569553971e5c608"},"summary":"A create with forked_from records its lineage on the artifact row but not in the artifact.create audit record, as a fork's does","tags":["app-push","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:23:17.904959Z","id":"e7f3033f61c11dd488d4876c5acb4ff0094fc251936570d5324ee08ea08085d7","body":{"detail":"Failure: Mia (a member, not the hosted owner) publishes an app from her Clax app, turns Comments on and shares it with Bob at Can comment; Bob comments in his browser; Mia's core syncs (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs) and an agent session on her core reading GET /api/artifacts/<aid>/threads gets Bob's comment body in full, authored \"Bob (on <remote>)\", though Mia never approved Bob. Since the device reads threads as its person's browser (PERSON_DEVICE_ROUTES, crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs), the remote no longer withholds unapproved authors; insert_mirrored writes author_public_id NULL and the local visibility (Reader::Owner for the core's own agents, crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs Caller::reader) has no approval to check for a remote author, so the approval gate that kept strangers' text from agents (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs) does not apply to mirrored comments. Before, the device read as an agent channel and such comments never came down. Seen by an observing run of api_linked::a_members_device_brings_down_a_strangers_comment (agent view printed, then removed). Options: keep remote authors' public IDs on mirrored comments and withhold them from local agents until the person approves them (here, or by reading the remote's approvals); or mirror only what the remote's agent-channel view shows and fetch the rest for the person's own view alone.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":663},"end":{"line":683},"content_hash":"26f242ce9e03f6df5450fb02f5f427bb03aa610e2bc1dbd8de84d4f571bf5f05"},"summary":"A person's Clax app now mirrors strangers' comments on their apps, and the local core's own agents read them unwithheld: nothing here withholds a mirrored author by the person's approvals","tags":["app-push","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:49:54.136541Z","id":"019724c9779b0cb1a7830345b81c59521d070b8be5e7e7470c7c7acc18f4a8cf","body":{"detail":"A mirrored comment by anyone other than the signed-in person keeps its hosted author as remote:<origin>#<public ID> (linked_comments.author_key, migration 48; mirrored_author_key in crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs). The local core's agents see it withheld until the person approves that key here (sees_one never lets *unconnected coverage reach a remote key; owner_sees_all ends once a keyed comment exists; approve_in accepts a key some mirrored comment has). The person's own mirrored comments carry no key. api_linked::a_members_device_brings_down_a_strangers_comment_withheld_from_her_agents_until_approved: Bob's comment comes to Mia's agent withheld through feedback and GET threads, her own note reads in full, and after she approves Bob's key through the request's decide route her agent reads his text. Mutations each failing that test (or the store unit test visibility::tests::an_author_on_a_public_clax_is_withheld_whatever_covers_viewers_who_are_not_connected): no key stored; own comments keyed; *unconnected covering a remote key; owner_sees_all ignoring keyed comments; approve_in refusing remote keys.","kind":"comment","references":"e7f3033f61c11dd488d4876c5acb4ff0094fc251936570d5324ee08ea08085d7","span":{"start":{"line":663},"end":{"line":683},"content_hash":"e6a11882d091b74e20a1b490ff5a8bf2aca05a554c31de205dca3b161a497d74"},"summary":"The owner decided: \"Withhold until approved\". Built in a1f58e923; the close is the owner's","tags":["security","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:49:54.136671Z","id":"44809b859ee56f3436bfa2ae585c2bbad0afcb8e7ee226202dac0a551fbd5ae8","body":{"detail":"mirrored_author_key maps (None, \"agent\") to remote:<origin>#*owner. When the signed-in person is that hosted Clax's owner, her other agents' comments there come down keyed and withheld from her local agents, since `me` is her public ID, never *owner. She can approve remote:<origin>#*owner to read them. Comparing against the hosted owner when the remote says the signed-in person owns it would key them as her own.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":390},"end":{"line":405},"content_hash":"7125871aad3ff311860d0bf9ba52ec9be13c05cfbdf5e5f3284b326068866901"},"summary":"A mirrored agent comment with no agent.person is keyed as the hosted owner's agent, so it is withheld even from the hosted owner's own phone agent until she approves her own key","tags":["security","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:00:04.846329Z","id":"45b9730736b3570efe4b2fca4d549140967eec748c94812dae541ae346cecbe9","body":{"detail":"mirrored_author_key (lines 390-405) leaves the signed-in person's own comments unkeyed. insert_mirrored then writes them with author_public_id NULL and via_page 0, so authors_of_comment (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:137-151) gives Author::Unconnected for a viewer comment. Effects: (1) with the owner's *unconnected switch off, the owner's agents lose her own words from the hosted Clax. (2) A connected local person's agents, under that person's *unconnected approval, read the owner's mirrored words as an unconnected viewer's, without any approval of the owner. (3) A hosted page-written comment (via_page) loses the page's authors here. That matters when Mia's browser ran a version a collaborator co-authored: the comment then reads as hers alone, or as unconnected. All of these withhold in the safe direction or concern the owner's own words, so none reaches a local agent unapproved from a stranger.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":726},"end":{"line":731},"content_hash":"b2b14bd31c0ce37d8ecd20066eb1a00d4190bf8116daf41fb58ef1f66e2fe876"},"suggested_fix":"Give unkeyed mirrored comments the owner's author: write the owner's local public ID as author_public_id for a viewer comment, as the agent branch already reads as Owner through agent_person NULL. Keep via_page comments keyed unless the hosted Clax says every page author is the person.","summary":"The person's own mirrored viewer comments have no author here: they read as an unconnected viewer's, not the owner's","tags":["security","severity:minor","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:00:04.846455Z","id":"825063ae6c63ed1d6caf015217084b753dcab5753ea65a22032abb901798381b","body":{"detail":"owner_sees_all is false while any linked_comments row has author_key. Visibility::for_reader (crates/clax-store/src/visibility.rs:130) then filters the owner's agents on every artifact, and VisFor::build (crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs:435-440) sets DeliveryViewer::Agent { every: false } for every agent. So after one stranger's comment is mirrored, the owner's agents read only their own sessions' delivery state on every thread of the home, as when a person is connected. Nothing else they see changes: Author::Unconnected stays covered by the owner's *unconnected approval, and no local Person exists. Deleting every keyed thread does not restore the fast path until another write bumps the visibility generation. A home with no remote is unchanged (the NOT EXISTS clause holds).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":448},"end":{"line":471},"content_hash":"28e1951cacdd4171516831357d03f948cff8204bdb142fd517a524fa7b8b0f7a"},"suggested_fix":"Accept as documented (as for people present), or scope `every` to the absence of keyed comments on the thread's artifact.","summary":"The first mirrored comment from someone else ends the owner's fast path everywhere on this home, not only on the linked artifact","tags":["severity:minor","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:15.612725Z","id":"79e46b9a3b23827c2f26246e8f8bf3ec229e0ba3ebca3849738456e7dc55dc5a","body":{"detail":"Failure: a local daemon (no client_kind, so a plain agent token) linked to a hosted Clax with `clax push`; its person Ada approved Bob on the hosted Clax; Bob comments on the public copy. The sync (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs mirror) reads threads with that agent token, so the remote's agent-channel filter has already dropped every author Ada has not approved (`.filter(|c| c[\"withheld\"] != true)`). mirrored_author_key still keys Bob's comment as remote:<origin>#<Bob's ID> whatever the token was, and authors_of_comment / Visibility::sees (crates/clax-store/src/visibility.rs) withhold it from the daemon's own agents until the local owner approves that key too, and the first such comment ends the owner_sees_all fast path. On main the same comment reached the daemon's agents (it was stored with no author, read as an unconnected viewer under the owner's `*unconnected` approval). So every daemon user of linked threads now gets an approval request for people they already approved, and older mirrored comments by the same author (author_key NULL, written before migration 48) stay visible while newer ones are withheld. Only a person's device (the Clax app's clax-app token, crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs PERSON_DEVICE_ROUTES) reads threads unfiltered and needs the local gate.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":390},"end":{"line":405},"content_hash":"7125871aad3ff311860d0bf9ba52ec9be13c05cfbdf5e5f3284b326068866901"},"suggested_fix":"Key a mirrored comment only when the link's token read it unfiltered: record on the remotes row whether the sign-in was a clax-app (person-device) one, and have mirrored_author_key return None for a plain agent token's remote, whose reads the remote already filtered by the person's approvals. Add an api_linked test with a daemon (no kind) remote where an approved stranger's comment reaches the local agent unwithheld.","summary":"A daemon's mirrored comments are now withheld from its local agents even though the remote already let them through by the person's own approvals there","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:15.612991Z","id":"eed4c2bdada14c267ddd98e0bb28f4d9ff5be1521517cfc06d635156b478c136","body":{"detail":"Commits 54eb8fcc6 and 47404f94e shipped migration 48 without `ALTER TABLE linked_comments ADD COLUMN author_key` and its index; 7f40149fb added them in place. A home opened by a build in between (dev homes, e2e homes, any device install of the branch) is at user_version 48, so migrate runs nothing, and adoption sees the migration's only mark, Mark::Table(\"app_bundles\") (APP_MIGRATION_MARKS), as present. Every statement that names the column then fails with SQLite's `no such column`: COMMENT_SELECT and COMMENTS_OF_MANY (crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs, the remote_author subquery), so every thread and comment read; owner_sees_all (crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs), so every agent read; and insert_mirrored, so every linked sync. AGENTS.md has such homes reset, but nothing says so: the failure is an opaque SQL error on every page rather than a refusal at open, as the jobs migration's partial tables get (jobs_tables_disagree, record a1d56f8d).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1421},"end":{"line":1423},"content_hash":"398a0f0bf3c1f8a61230639853948289b2dacab61b0127c66a0b0c1589ff6019"},"suggested_fix":"At open, refuse a database at APP_PUSH_MIGRATION or above that lacks linked_comments.author_key (or the linked_comments_by_author index) with MigrationFailed naming the reset, as jobs_tables_disagree does for the jobs tables; or, if any such home must keep working, move the column and index to a migration 49.","summary":"Migration 48 gained linked_comments.author_key after builds had applied it; a home at 48 without the column passes open and then fails every thread read","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:21:15.613053Z","id":"d34014a10a4b8d77f712aa38564f2bbf2fb895fca3c7593ada2ef6c282f6dd62","body":{"detail":"The upsert replaces remote_artifact_id, url, pushed_n and remote_n, and leaves sync_cursor, download_only and every linked_threads row of the link untouched (link_remote_without_push_sets_base moves a1 from b1 to b2 and checks only the link's columns). The outbox (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs, `let raid = &link.remote_artifact_id`) posts a reply, resolve or reopen on a thread mirrored from the old copy to /api/artifacts/<new raid>/threads/<old remote thread ID>/..., which the remote refuses as no such thread of that artifact, and the next incremental read of the new copy asks `since=<the old copy's cursor>`, skipping its threads with older activity until a full read. unlink_remote, by contrast, marks the old threads unlinked (linked_threads.unlinked_at). POST /api/remotes/<rid>/links (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs link) reaches this with any remote_artifact_id.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":459},"end":{"line":488},"content_hash":"2972908e542bc697f9e9467e88b3c4d197c2f879dd1aa2393140cd28b2714bf0"},"suggested_fix":"When the upsert changes remote_artifact_id, in the same transaction mark the link's linked_threads unlinked as unlink_remote does and reset sync_cursor to NULL (and download_only as a new link has it); extend link_remote_without_push_sets_base to assert both.","summary":"link_remote moves a link to another public artifact but keeps the old copy's linked threads live and its sync cursor","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:23:17.211395Z","id":"3654c8d7c25a4221d23d8c32fafda7ae2c51c6b58826303e91c92a744bbb5ff3","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/remotes.rs:173 passes b.kind to public::start_sign_in (crates/clax-server/src/public.rs:730-739), which names a client_kind only when given; only the Clax app sends clax-app (apps/clax_app/lib/remote/remote_api.dart:50). On the remote, a plain agent token is Caller::PersonAgent with its person's rights (crates/clax-http/src/identity.rs:322-357); only a device (identity.rs:312-320, PERSON_DEVICE_ROUTES in crates/clax-http/src/agent.rs:1758) reads as its person's browser. The sync keeps only comments with withheld != true (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs:1670). mirrored_author_key (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:390-405) keys every author but the signed-in person as remote:<origin>#<id> with no regard to the token kind; authors_of_comment returns Author::Person(key) for it (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:137-140); sees_one lets a remote key through only by reader match or an approval of that key, never *unconnected (crates/clax-store/src/visibility.rs:268-276); owner_sees_all turns false once any linked_comments.author_key IS NOT NULL (crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs:455-460). On main the column does not exist (`git grep author_key main -- crates` prints nothing), so mirrored comments read as Author::Unconnected. A pre-48 row has author_key NULL and still reads as Unconnected (threads.rs:619 subquery yields NULL), so old and new comments by one author diverge as stated. The owner's 'Withhold until approved' answer (record 019724c9) was given on e7f3033f, whose failure is the device's unfiltered read.","kind":"comment","references":"79e46b9a3b23827c2f26246e8f8bf3ec229e0ba3ebca3849738456e7dc55dc5a","summary":"confirmed: a daemon's remote reads through the agent channel's filter, yet its mirrored comments are keyed and withheld again here","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:23:17.211774Z","id":"28fe851eae6abfb103f435c3f452fd4bcdcb0009285972a2e2ba97adeef46bff","body":{"detail":"`git show 54eb8fcc6:crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs | grep author_key` and the same for 47404f94e print nothing; at 7f40149fb it is line 1421 (`ALTER TABLE linked_comments ADD COLUMN author_key TEXT;`), now crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1421-1423. `git log 54eb8fcc6^..7f40149fb -- crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs` lists 54eb8fcc6, 47404f94e, e1bd068e8, 7f40149fb. Migration 48's only adoption mark is Mark::Table(\"app_bundles\") (migrations.rs:1579-1587). Statements naming the column: crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs:619 and 638 (remote_author subqueries), crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs:459 and 600, crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:377, 720, 735. No open-time check mentions author_key (`grep -n author_key crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs` hits only the migration text and its comment), unlike jobs_tables_disagree (migrations.rs:1706, 1726).","kind":"comment","references":"eed4c2bdada14c267ddd98e0bb28f4d9ff5be1521517cfc06d635156b478c136","summary":"confirmed: migration 48 gained author_key in place after two commits shipped it without; nothing at open detects the gap","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:23:17.212080Z","id":"6b0b694c54e228f86c8d7be44506317f12e3fc447945af1e2bb9d8737faf299d","body":{"detail":"The upsert at crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs:469-478 sets remote_artifact_id, url, pushed_n, remote_n, auto and pushed_at only; sync_cursor, download_only and linked_threads are untouched. unlink_remote (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:533-548) sets linked_threads.unlinked_at instead. The outbox builds paths from link.remote_artifact_id (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs:1006) and the thread's lt.remote_thread_id (linked.rs ~1097-1109: `/api/artifacts/{raid}/threads/{rtid}/comments`), though linked_threads stores its own remote_artifact_id (migrations.rs:1028). The route (crates/clax-server/src/routes/remote_apps.rs:292-326) accepts any remote_artifact_id, then calls links_changed and kick; a kick runs cycle(false) (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs:438), whose read uses l.sync_cursor as since (linked.rs:1546-1549, 1561-1562) until the backstop's full read (linked.rs:439).","kind":"comment","references":"d34014a10a4b8d77f712aa38564f2bbf2fb895fca3c7593ada2ef6c282f6dd62","summary":"confirmed: moving a link to another public artifact keeps the old copy's linked threads live and its sync cursor","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/approvals.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:08:31.107003Z","id":"d799b05884960ebc72305366a7777032bd384c3fce806e1ef48b815aa1eaf88d","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs mirrored_author_key returns None for a remote whose client_kind is 'agent' (migration 49), so a home linked with a plain agent token never writes an author_key and keeps owner_sees_all. A home linked by the Clax app's device token still drops the fast path everywhere after its first stranger's comment. Scoping `every` per artifact would split the per-home visibility cache (Visibility::for_reader, generation-keyed). Proposal: waive for device-linked homes, where the cost is reading own-session delivery state only; the owner decides.","kind":"comment","references":"825063ae6c63ed1d6caf015217084b753dcab5753ea65a22032abb901798381b","summary":"Proposed waiver: since 70676ef59 only device-linked homes key mirrored comments","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:08:31.107294Z","id":"2bc9ab8b4d060f1e8ac67a6f500987a9525e5bf47560d401cc209eba542d05d9","body":{"detail":"Writing the signed-in person's own mirrored viewer comments with the home's owner public ID as author_public_id breaks crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs:324, which asserts a mirrored author is never a local person (crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs mark_comment: 'A remote's author says where they are, never a local person'). The other route is an author_key that reads as the owner (remote:<origin>#*owner-like, or a new key), which touches remote_author_labels, approvals and anchors. Which of the two (or leaving the safe-direction withholding) is the owner's call.","kind":"comment","references":"45b9730736b3570efe4b2fca4d549140967eec748c94812dae541ae346cecbe9","summary":"Needs a decision: writing the owner's public ID on her own mirrored comments conflicts with 'never a local person'","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:08:31.107562Z","id":"8520b1afec536ddfdedec723926ce3c659af5c03b90add3e40674d3fd20bbd82","body":{"detail":"The sync cannot tell that the signed-in person owns the hosted Clax: the device sign-in answer and remotes row carry only person_public_id. Keying her agents' comments as her own needs a protocol addition (e.g. an `owner: true` in the device sign-in or /api/people/me answer, stored on the remote). Today it withholds in the safe direction and she can approve remote:<origin>#*owner. Since 3acda5ff0 an agent comment naming no person is keyed remote:<origin>#*agent, so approving *owner covers only the hosted owner's agents.","kind":"comment","references":"44809b859ee56f3436bfa2ae585c2bbad0afcb8e7ee226202dac0a551fbd5ae8","summary":"Needs a decision: keying the hosted owner's agents as her own needs the hosted Clax to say she is its owner","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:11:51.510656Z","id":"aa94dceadec7af62739872188406f7ba220b2010ed36c97e803eedc73a3c84cd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9ce07753a","summary":"Fixed: migration 49 adds remotes.client_kind and its rust_step adds linked_comments.author_key and its index where a home at 48 lacks them. Test migrations::tests::a_home_at_48_without_the_author_key_gets_it_and_the_fresh_schema (//crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test) passes; with the rust_step removed it fails. bazelisk test (clax-store, clax-core, clax-http, clax-server lib + integration__1..6, clax-embed:old_homes, clax-mcp) at 3acda5ff0: 'Executed 15 out of 15 tests: 15 tests pass.'","supersedes":"eed4c2bdada14c267ddd98e0bb28f4d9ff5be1521517cfc06d635156b478c136","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:11:51.583875Z","id":"1d9b728bcaff9608ba6f9184a90954ca96f34fea30a74f2596921c8e89ed6cba","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:70676ef59","summary":"Fixed (no conflict with withholding unapproved hosted authors): comments read through a plain agent token, already filtered by the hosted Clax's approvals, are unkeyed; device-read comments stay keyed. Remotes record client_kind at sign-in, or are probed once. Tests api_linked::a_daemons_agent_reads_a_comment_its_person_approved_there_unwithheld, api_linked::a_remote_signed_in_before_kinds_were_kept_is_asked_its_kind (//crates/clax-server:integration__5) and linked::tests::a_mirrored_comment_is_keyed_unless_an_agent_token_read_it (//crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test) pass; mutating the agent guard, the probe or the kind write each failed its test. bazelisk test (clax-store, clax-core, clax-http, clax-server lib + integration__1..6, clax-embed:old_homes, clax-mcp) at 3acda5ff0: 'Executed 15 out of 15 tests: 15 tests pass.'","supersedes":"79e46b9a3b23827c2f26246e8f8bf3ec229e0ba3ebca3849738456e7dc55dc5a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:11:51.657712Z","id":"3a2e87d1ef18cd7138477c60d17a11ed866a2621e5e756895acb4e0f5fd23364","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7046e6a6a","summary":"Fixed: link_remote to another remote_artifact_id clears sync_cursor and download_only, sets threads_since and marks the old copy's linked_threads unlinked. Test linked::tests::a_link_moved_to_another_public_copy_ends_the_old_copys_threads_and_read (//crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test) passes; with the reset removed it fails. bazelisk test (clax-store, clax-core, clax-http, clax-server lib + integration__1..6, clax-embed:old_homes, clax-mcp) at 3acda5ff0: 'Executed 15 out of 15 tests: 15 tests pass.'","supersedes":"d34014a10a4b8d77f712aa38564f2bbf2fb895fca3c7593ada2ef6c282f6dd62","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backfill.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.466478Z","id":"4382b49f564c0456409afaf732c6c844b5d5f43202e571458f3a87dc01da1049","body":{"detail":"The perf seed's backfill time is measured on demand only by the ignored test backfill_at_scale (CLAX_BACKFILL_SCALE=1 for the seed the correctness test uses). just perf (scripts/run.sh perf) runs the Bazel targets //scripts:perf_daemon_full, //scripts:perf_clients_full, //web:perf_usable_full and //web:bundle_size, none of which runs Rust unit tests, so adding it there would need a new Bazel target running this ignored test with --ignored.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2420},"end":{"line":2448},"content_hash":"3a03f72f787bb37d637cfac349e94436aebd8d2a19e17a1962db328a60ef2dc1"},"summary":"Backfill timing is not part of just perf","supersedes":"1c99e0720eebf1d4024760d107b0b9fc12137812df16fbee6dace0c162101c5a","tags":["perf","revisit:the backfill's time on an upgrade becomes a release concern","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.523446Z","id":"838883fee4e07f44af294a43fef0685c18753b8763112216f1deaba591926f23","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs:66-89, record c1fa8f66.\n\nSeen in Linux perf runs: a single commit held up by the disk. The writer runs WAL with SQLite's default synchronous=FULL, so every commit syncs the WAL, and the background PASSIVE checkpoint runs every CHECKPOINT_INTERVAL (2 s). Every delivery of a write waits on its commit, so one slow commit moves a whole cluster of deliveries (scripts/perf-clients.py:23-29 explains how the realtime gate copes).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":270},"end":{"line":293},"content_hash":"19a1b1cc49fe118705a9d82f6b9227495d66a06ae11378ed14f24dfb809e7ed5"},"suggested_fix":"Measure commit times on Linux with synchronous=NORMAL (durable across a crash of the process, not of the machine, in WAL mode) and with a different checkpoint cadence before choosing.","summary":"On Linux, store commits occasionally take 25 to 120 ms","supersedes":"6994f9b1b4eb6a225409e1ec9fc54143052bcc85d38216601b4796ba446773cb","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/exec.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.578483Z","id":"c3d3f844e33f8592e66c3ccaee2c3729504c7b95b21c9737b7762ed42898f7f9","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/exec.rs:916-946, record 7600eccb.\n\nOn the pool a started job runs to completion on its worker (call_on_worker), but inline the request future owns the job: a client gone or a timeout layer dropping the handler between ContentStore::write_version and the version transaction (store/artifacts.rs:1145) skips both the record and the remove_version that a failed transaction runs. FsContent and a create-only git backend then refuse version n as already present (artifacts.rs a_stray_version_directory_refuses_the_publish_and_records_nothing), so the artifact cannot be published again until the stray is removed (clax doctor natively; nothing on a Durable Object). A dropped clipped thread creation leaves an unreferenced clip; a dropped create_artifact a zero-version row. Removing an unrecorded n before writing it is safe only where one process writes the content (a Durable Object), not natively with several daemons (record 4f959f4e).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":953},"end":{"line":983},"content_hash":"68f7616e26a49e70da13008ab0b933c12adca6dea763e30fb402f4ea0f4602dd"},"suggested_fix":"On one connection, make an unrecorded version n replaceable: when write_version reports n present and the row still says n - 1, remove_version(n) under the content lock and write again; or run the job to completion detached from the request (ctx.waitUntil on a Worker).","summary":"A call_async job awaited inline (one connection, wasm32) stops wherever its future is dropped, so a cancelled publish can leave version n written but unrecorded, which refuses every later publish of n","supersedes":"dc11e4cdbdc735c4d574637cc64a5f799ecfc7ea0f263334669692e4c646eb7f","tags":["content-store","wasm","review","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.633377Z","id":"358b66eba9ba32dbea514d6edda85f7209b8c33f5db04464e67ad1ad23cd7f3a","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1363-1368, record 0118687f.\n\nconnection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1595},"end":{"line":1600},"content_hash":"c1c86e26871ba066020c75f1d9b1b954ee91add027a8fb30f98694a07930d59d"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","supersedes":"2eb022c9f93f2f45d225701a5bc3cf358bb49deeb5edd707d4263a3b45138f35","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.693055Z","id":"693eda0b3ba339509ef7d1fa80f2cb7815c6d4db655cc509a2a5a23160af66a3","body":{"detail":"inbox_groups groups all of a query's matches (GROUP BY artifact over the driver's walk, with a temporary B-tree; crates/clax-store/src/plans.rs allows it for the ' groups' shapes) so each group's total and unread are exact across pages, then reads each listed group's newest rows by inbox_by_artifact. The unread section reads only unread items (inbox_unread); the read section, unfolded, reads the recipient's whole read history. The route runs it in the bulk lane (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs list). Accepted: an inbox of tens of thousands of items groups in milliseconds, and the read section loads only when unfolded.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1681},"end":{"line":1762},"content_hash":"c21e4c7179b4ee93301d6e354ee8a31dc042ecc2101279bbec0f7a94446d122b"},"summary":"Grouping the inbox by artifact reads every match to count each group","supersedes":"a885e2354eb808178f2943fbbe892b6cc510792607fee93dd8d95bc298f3cb69","tags":["inbox","perf","revisit:a group=artifact read over 50 ms in just perf, or inboxes past 100k items","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.755229Z","id":"d66522f45b75e146d3ce0504de997d5ad88a35df890f4f7fb20e654f9666b357","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1552-1556, record 6014047e.\n\nnote_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1866},"end":{"line":1870},"content_hash":"df46c2781c4e06aa0fe53e6fadd564b9bcbcad9e060403b47de165ac7d60413a"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","supersedes":"5ab9a83e4245981d00d2bdbf73d7825a012475ae84d9647b68bf6a8f9161e029","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.820312Z","id":"6477983099e7f640860110ba37df8f645350203741bb47b12c8c65e88848346a","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs:757-783, record 102e3b6a.\n\nMeasured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":955},"end":{"line":981},"content_hash":"52e810ab13e4b4c1906f3b6d191494a2b7dbc5c619a6c49ab2c0c512f581f5a7"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"7bdacc9e7bac4493fb5a906480f9acc6a9e561366b4a9ac09353ef0ad17a4da7","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.881237Z","id":"275be26fcc9ddd3e2a5bf19c1847acb23c38e9129da079b86a66dd599baff1d9","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:1001-1014, record bb077166.\n\nthread_id is the PRIMARY KEY; scan_linked queues a fresh local thread only when no linked_threads row names it (crates/clax-core/src/store/linked.rs scan_linked), so the first remote scanned takes it and the other never gets it, nor its replies. Threads mirrored from either remote are separate local threads.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1024},"end":{"line":1037},"content_hash":"422e16fad9ac387965892c1a684d9f7f45d108c71b2cd3fbe0fa9890e34ef65e"},"summary":"linked_threads is keyed by the local thread alone, so an artifact linked to two remotes sends its local threads to only one of them","supersedes":"04e01c765df218cd9c8312c9cbb882c2615e1d9fe6a1b734e34a1ac96bf7e7bc","tags":["review","linked-threads","revisit:an artifact is pushed to a second remote","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:08.947091Z","id":"53bf35f4ffee89bd17eb42aa12a48d3ae1fdcdf7069addda90d25913f4121167","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:1052-1059, record 7dd62168.\n\nA hosted daemon keeps every key a linked local daemon's up-sends named (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs comment_key), as publish_keys keeps every publish's. Rows are small, but nothing removes them, not even when the thread or grant is deleted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1075},"end":{"line":1082},"content_hash":"4ba09b7472a4ca6e5001974915649601eee612783ece3677d8a9dc4398698508"},"suggested_fix":"Delete a grant's keys with the grant and a thread's with the thread, or prune keys older than the outbox could resend (a day).","summary":"comment_keys is never pruned: one row per thread or comment an agent token wrote with an Idempotency-Key","supersedes":"a58bd84e0d2804e7ec40da9b07e779d8e4df15c451cad189c2208f9f9b1298ff","tags":["review","status:deferred","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.006613Z","id":"05857288c5bfcf332ff2b8397b9298e83724dacd6b7d544623f66c2782eac566","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:1095-1101, record e614fbdc.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1118},"end":{"line":1124},"content_hash":"40e0ef842deae344eeb6cb9ab562cb44f1e01fd90bba9720a79e05d2a441f941"},"summary":"question_keys is never pruned: one row per question an agent token asked with an Idempotency-Key","supersedes":"00c5000167bdb7f982510f61c39a508ec8c07fc9eb9a6e84b4771a0aa533e3ac","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.063139Z","id":"b029ee365ca50a41d3eca2cb26f48a38cc9f626dfaa169858cc7d05ad7d6325a","body":{"detail":"Failure: a home whose user_version is 29 and whose migration 29 was 98b628173's device publishing (crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs blob c196df9e8, branch rust-int, 2026-10-14T01:08) fails Store::open with 'table device_codes already exists' when the current migration 30 runs. The next commit, b8015c192 two minutes later, renumbered it, so only a home opened by that one build is affected. Migration 37 cannot reach it; a fix would have to change migration 30 (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS) or detect the shape before it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1137},"end":{"line":1152},"content_hash":"2b824f6033e11d7da18d8730e9656465a8171749c6546b89674f0c4a734d95ad"},"summary":"A database left at schema 29 by rust-int commit 98b628173 fails migration 30 before migration 37 can repair it","supersedes":"00c6643bdb6839bef67db1331c2989054334da8a66fef43507e1dde5156967d6","tags":["migrations","revisit:a home made by rust-int commit 98b628173 is reported","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.118521Z","id":"35d42f858707909a0672157b1c99262b240c4ec42526d9663b0c808ad63e2fb1","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:774-776, record fa9ef7ec.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":797},"end":{"line":799},"content_hash":"7b8c2cfc4b3987a8e331333cde1cdfbfbebd527f736765bcd9ae5f2176add692"},"summary":"Migration 27 (hosted sign-in) takes the next number after multi-person's 26; it renumbers if another branch lands first","supersedes":"72e1a0365764ae1e5a641c5e52cc6734f04321d03e99b65273ac386056386d18","tags":["hosted","merge","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.173120Z","id":"6292b30fab7c704bd9d02a83781ac7fbf82719b9258fff54ad84124925768a99","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:808-930, record 44826f12.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":831},"end":{"line":953},"content_hash":"4fc246c7ef2dbffa199d9a8cf44a6b8c266dcff13243c43bab8ce3914f210925"},"summary":"Migration 30 (publishing to a public Clax) follows akesling/clax-artifacts' 29 (sessions.client_name); it renumbers if another branch lands a 30 first. It also rebuilds inbox_items to add the `push` kind, as migration 26 left the table.","supersedes":"e022ca731a8267befdbee499dfd70bf80fca250edd71536ae7789165d3ccd53b","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.231887Z","id":"0c3a61825005e7ac258fdb94012e39b4ffc04b909072ce0a26091659ba7fa53c","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:888-895, record 924ede60.\n\nSmall rows, but they outlive the artifact and the grant. Dropping keys of revoked grants or older than some months would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":911},"end":{"line":918},"content_hash":"3809d3eb40206bf1050d7706a17caa1d82c06599c44bd8c816fb14753e919899"},"summary":"publish_keys is never pruned: one row per version an agent token published with a key","supersedes":"b8105a392f24efa6bc643ed0bec3bbd2a0ab77196f5d161eb04c89c5000aba45","tags":["deferred","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.287691Z","id":"813e14984bbf89bc5675a3721acb2fdc1b1dd2f8b9632fb9fff81908d8f8b0a2","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:931-948, record 388db751.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":954},"end":{"line":971},"content_hash":"7d8c751bbf9693818ae00c620d322851f29dceeee90a9880b0582ce408b23081"},"summary":"Migration 31 (GitHub identities) follows akesling/clax-artifacts' 30 (publishing to a public Clax); it renumbers if another branch lands a 31 first","supersedes":"968d74e24c937a53279bd1935eb9518998cb23c40fe012e53b6d61e55b174d65","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.343594Z","id":"f9712a274820ae434beaf1b96367747a973eda9d891e52ebc3110c3be2bc84bb","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:1319-1348, record 2f7ad0c3.\n\nroutes/sessions.rs register calls end_bearer_sessions_beyond(gid, BEARER_SESSION_CAP - 1) and then register_session_restoring in separate transactions; concurrent initializes of one token can each count the same live set. The next registration trims it back. Accepted as a bound on build-up, not an exact limit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1329},"end":{"line":1358},"content_hash":"8ef33f44d4f1cafe046fb180228494b8e47afb2f14aca6b7df5ba45bf9f7a4bc"},"summary":"Two agent-token registrations at once can each leave room for themselves, so a token briefly holds more than BEARER_SESSION_CAP live sessions","supersedes":"2961ece31c461480f8a74711bd5cbf8072cf11c40694992bb70bed1e454e4d9f","tags":["hosted","review","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.399299Z","id":"ab5d16582dfe8aa0e8e66e1d79f9ab05a550b6b57a1755735fecbcb65b6e8dc9","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:1639-1655, record bcb6cc4e.\n\nrelease_owned_in (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs) selects threads WHERE target_session_id = ?1, and Store::roster groups threads by target_session_id; crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs indexes neither. Both are full scans of threads: off the request hot paths (ends, the reaper, GET /api/agents) and cheap at today's sizes, but linear in all threads ever made.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1735},"end":{"line":1751},"content_hash":"20c6bc83236711f3d0fd91be27eb8807d928e32beb5474638e9b1e8ace251388"},"suggested_fix":"Add CREATE INDEX threads_by_target ON threads(target_session_id) WHERE target_session_id IS NOT NULL in the next migration.","summary":"Every session end and every roster read scans threads for target_session_id, which has no index","supersedes":"347b05564c9c8cb862bd2ded4413588f966d8c47753ed42434a8833353a9b86d","tags":["perf","revisit:the next migration on this branch","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:10.504788Z","id":"8b3185d401644926b15a01bb4f90074953b4862526b1657ccb794b8ec9f9d264","body":{"detail":"MIGRATIONS[47] is ClaxBot's SQL; migrations::tests::the_app_migrations_follow_mains_in_this_order asserts CLAXBOT_MIGRATION == JOBS_MIGRATION + 1 == MIGRATIONS.len(), and a_fresh_database_reaches_48 the fresh user_version. Its Rust step (credits::seed_cost_lines) goes by its SQL (rust_step_of), and adoption counts its mark after the app's (MARKS_AFTER_APP), so a_home_of_this_numbering_takes_a_later_main_migration_and_the_apps_renumbering passes with a home at 48 opening as 49 under a simulated later numbering. A dev home this branch's earlier builds migrated (ClaxBot's tables at 42, no db_read_grants) is not upgraded: it would run the app's 43 to 47 on it and fail at 48 on 'table person_roles already exists', so it is reset. Closing this thread is the owner's call.","kind":"comment","references":"651f09e1c1ae3f1da17ec4f3484afc2fcb7daaf51d7082ae6ad6c0cf0780e66d","summary":"Renumbered: since merge 4f013eec this branch's ClaxBot migration is 48 (CLAXBOT_MIGRATION), after main's 42 to 47 (the Clax app's, kept as main has them)","tags":["claxbot","migration","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:10.505287Z","id":"529031cb7436ace5b609a7463a504ea15f5f7713299d4e69b8b1012f127e38d7","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1388},"end":{"line":1414},"content_hash":"677c7b2c177d96ba81250491319c6d3101d7f2254ed0ebbb43dfd85bbab54f16"},"summary":"Migration 48 (ClaxBot) follows main's 42 to 47 (the Clax app's) and stays after them: a later main migration taken below the app's moves it with them (MARKS_AFTER_APP)","supersedes":"348256e5c059c9ad1d3536048a690deca3f6d5a37faeee52667f65c15440611e","tags":["claxbot","migration","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:10.562174Z","id":"20cbd674cdaaca8525135eec92cd63b1102234c0af93d2227fa951d44612562f","body":{"detail":"Every call a script makes is journaled (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs RunHost::journal): reads keep their answers (a threads.read's comments, a db.list page), draft operations a null result. Nothing prunes the rows once their step commits, though only an open step's journal is ever read again (Tick::script, Tick::unreported_calls). A committed run's rows could be pruned at its run_end, or reads' answers dropped at commit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1541},"end":{"line":1552},"content_hash":"92152c95c44c8873a9a882474f1319fab4298453c7156b707c8ed68eea2257d6"},"summary":"Call journal rows (bot_calls) are kept for every step forever","supersedes":"97eb77d913e9b18e829ee9d70e112ae835f9cf0e9ab490370f63d353b17f76e2","tags":["storage","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:10.621808Z","id":"fcc953eb9454509e661d636f17430d62fd5294c67a2d243786b56dd7abafe006","body":{"detail":"Each DraftChange::Write stores its full content as a BLOB; the store does not bound a file's size, a draft's total, or how long an ended run's draft is kept (a stopped run's draft must stay viewable, spec 2026-10-21-claxbot-design section 6.3). The caller (clax-bot's files.write) must cap sizes, and a later change should prune drafts of runs that ended long ago or were published.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1553},"end":{"line":1559},"content_hash":"f325b86717df6d16cb53a01e25fcfa70401e2fc07ca66842609fd40e9968b1f2"},"summary":"Run drafts are kept whole in bot_draft_files with no size cap and never pruned","supersedes":"7956d1227cf1ac0ab6547ed016dc743e7dcf0419e4ab2084974090371f439177","tags":["claxbot","storage","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:10.678417Z","id":"2d8b116c3059b5768c19e315e191d7a85e4221f8d72882ebd9f4a678c844af7a","body":{"detail":"No table or name is shared, so the migrations do not collide. But an app's sample() calls are capped per artifact per local day in micro-USD (sample_spend, [sample] daily_cost_cap_usd in crates/clax-core/src/config.rs), while ClaxBot's model calls are charged per person per UTC week in milli-credits (usage_rows, crates/clax-store/src/credits.rs); neither sees the other's spend, so an instance key pays both without one cap. Likewise the app's jobs/job_steps (crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs, Store::commit_step) and ClaxBot's bot_runs/bot_steps (crates/clax-store/src/bot_runs.rs, Store::commit_bot_step, renamed from commit_step in the merge) each journal an agent's steps for resume after a kill. Whether they should share one spend ledger or one run model is the owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1388},"end":{"line":1414},"content_hash":"677c7b2c177d96ba81250491319c6d3101d7f2254ed0ebbb43dfd85bbab54f16"},"summary":"Two parallel ledgers of model spend and two of durable agent runs: the app's sample_grants/sample_spend and jobs (45, 47) beside ClaxBot's usage_rows/credit_lifts and bot_runs (48)","tags":["claxbot","merge","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:10.678587Z","id":"f6099b90578285dbdfda100bc773dd7dc50893d6f6afbd0822b6f307519e1ceb","body":{"detail":"MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38's doc says a new main migration goes below the app's with its mark added there, and adoption renumbers homes of the earlier numbering. Not taken: main's 42 to 47 are landed and homes the app installed are at 47 in that numbering; AGENTS.md has a branch take the next free number. MARKS_AFTER_APP keeps that recipe working with ClaxBot's 48 after the app's.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1708},"end":{"line":1713},"content_hash":"8f4c39729470cd4f14dc1d7a67f82f79891cae3bcd5701ce72a3d0a9f3d79728"},"summary":"Insert ClaxBot's migration below the app's, as main's 42 (MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38's recipe), the app's becoming 43 to 48","tags":["migration","revisit:main stops taking migrations below the app's, or the app's numbering is frozen","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T16:53:52.116580Z","id":"4df4bc8cc74433ae0f5c3991859a854364e5e4776843215c18f58cd0f1a44b69","body":{"kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1446},"end":{"line":1472},"content_hash":"3175615716a9ca4d4d920f33c84bfc3d6b91d32e9b887d1b8d34647fadd07b06"},"summary":"Migration 50 (ClaxBot) follows main's 42 to 49 (the Clax app's) and stays after them: a later main migration taken below the app's moves it with them (MARKS_AFTER_APP)","supersedes":"529031cb7436ace5b609a7463a504ea15f5f7713299d4e69b8b1012f127e38d7","tags":["claxbot","migration","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:05.973707Z","id":"ee83e6f4d3f534c66f743a86405973a50af29f06161743aa67ccca36f46d67e6","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/visibility.rs:72-79, record 1ce70140.\n\nMoved from crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:330-337, record b8541bce.\n\nUnattributed history is marked '(not connected)' (owner's decision on 7fdbaaf5). Comments the owner's browser made between migrations 12 and 15 carry a viewer row with minted_local NULL that claim_for_owner (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs) never claims, so they are marked on real installs too. Matching names is spoofable (spec §21.2); an explicit fold by the owner in the browser is not.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":73},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"31b72a09f53496f8d927466a9d2f661853a503a3fd7274e62dbae25d003fa4ac"},"summary":"An owner-only, browser-only 'this was me' in People that folds a legacy viewer row (or claims unattributed comments) into the owner, unmarking that history without trusting names","supersedes":"ec1b4b8cc08564396ec254194f7a05b9f7ec44518e4cedb2e7fe49dd642057b5","tags":["revisit:owners report their own old comments marked as not connected","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:06.935110Z","id":"914d5c5c03e303e3fbc8d67598741574ec4583745c4029d8a840e5e43a670c23","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs:13-14, record cbd48570.\n\nStore::fork_artifact_async copies version files only (ContentStore::fork). Pages reference assets by ID alone: the upload answers /_blob/<asset ID> (a hosted daemon's /_blob/<asset ID>?k=<key>, keyed by the asset ID only, hosted.rs asset_url), and routes/assets.rs blob looks the row up by ID (Store::get_asset). So the fork's page keeps loading the source's assets for every reader of the fork, a hosted one too (the key is in the page's bytes), until the source is deleted (delete_artifact_async removes its content, assets included) or its owner deletes that asset; the fork's own asset list (GET /api/artifacts/<fork>/assets) is empty. Copying under the same IDs is impossible: assets.id is the table's primary key (migration 1) and /_blob/<id> names no artifact. Copying under new IDs means rewriting the copied files' bytes, which changes the hashes and authors' bytes the fork keeps (content_sha256 equal to the source version's, crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs tests) and misses URLs a page builds in script. The hosted prototype has no assets.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"8f8a88dfee148d331f49e490b34e3ad9419ec674b3990eb7801ffb6511b3f63d"},"suggested_fix":"Decide: (a) key assets by (artifact_id, id) with /_blob/<id> resolved within the page's artifact (a migration and a route that knows its artifact), then copy rows and bytes under the same IDs into the fork; (b) keep a deleted artifact's asset bytes while a live fork names it as its source; or (c) accept, and say in docs/contract.md's fork section that assets stay the source's.","summary":"A fork copies no assets, so a forked page's /_blob/<asset ID> URLs stay the source's and break when the source or that asset is deleted","supersedes":"3f605810ac353760dd7f00a5dd173cad7dd7b7ebf066e5a9b7718bb25f2a5aa8","tags":["forks","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:07.735970Z","id":"3d60c364fa06700c260cd08625b1ec99880757182b6aae7858afb0704a73da45","body":{"detail":"When a push that was not a fast forward moves main off a step's unrecorded version v<n> onto a commit P on v<n-1>, P can take n only once the stray's tag is gone. Store::clear_stray_locked (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs) removes it at the next write of n (the step's resume, or anyone's write once the step is dead), but record_pushes_locked alone does not clear it, so a reconcile triggered by a push fails in tag_pushed with present until such a write. Needs a host that allows non-fast-forward pushes (the core's own server denies them by default: deny_non_fast_forwards).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":152},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"474ea2fb7dd190f73461401a95dc51adb8b50bc86e360ca022ed712d74200ba7"},"suggested_fix":"Call clear_stray_locked(id, current + 1, None) at the start of record_pushes_locked for a dead step's stray.","summary":"A reconcile with no write after it never records a push beside a stray step version","supersedes":"bbd0c773353cc18150e6bc302313a14eca19a39c811d15fc2662afcf5ceb7f04","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:08.385134Z","id":"08df4ee9fd04dca48ba56babb34808534b970082d2e01077ad1195e307d71bfd","body":{"detail":"record_render stores any well-formed digest for any draft, so a client holding the token and not the owner's agents (the route refuses those) can record a clean render of files it never rendered. The gate then holds only as far as the app reports truthfully. Comparing the digest with the draft's current version (clax_core::digest::manifest_digest of its files) would tie a render to content the core holds, but a draft is published version by version while the app renders, so the digest may name a version the draft has since moved past.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":379},"end":{"line":395},"content_hash":"f9bc71b76fcbab8e6c00b3dda25d7be4b6e40a733d2e06630875f8abde374335"},"suggested_fix":"Accept a render only when some version of the draft has that digest (versions.files_json), and answer 409 otherwise.","summary":"A recorded render is the app's word: the core does not check that the digest is of the draft's files","supersedes":"aae0642789c6d62e06b6ac3d5bf8348c93c6e585ed7856e79d6138fb857e6b31","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:09.526470Z","id":"5aff79277c96d3a40bd46b819669df65c4d69491e977966e6c80892d5cd8c1c4","body":{"detail":"Store::lock_publish_key (crates/clax-store/src/remotes.rs:608-614) holds an in-memory lock (ArtifactLocks::lock_key), so it serialises same-key publishes within one Store only. Across two processes on one database, both miss the key in replayed() (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs), and the second's version transaction fails in record_publish_key_in (remotes.rs:625-648) with publish_key_used, which the route returns as an error instead of the first's version. A failed create removes its own artifact row (create_artifact_async, crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs), so nothing is left behind. A hosted daemon is one process today, so no current path hits it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":683},"end":{"line":729},"content_hash":"63d3066b26a8e8478b2ba46113e3099f304e686d8d6e4246318fbd6cf4c55be1"},"suggested_fix":"If a hosted instance ever runs more than one process on one database, have the routes answer publish_key_used by re-running replayed().","summary":"The publish-key lock is per Store: of two processes publishing with the same key at once, the second fails with publish_key_used instead of replaying","supersedes":"029e7a62f2c2d8e8fafe53e062a4b6c6790ba66b1559f0afec210e561a4766e2","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:10.114081Z","id":"e51d8a6cfabc61541d8bebd82b09826d6588cdf4ea74e608c33d2a5a7a3518fa","body":{"detail":"Deleting a linked thread (Store::delete_thread_rows) drops its linked_outbox rows and keeps its linked_threads pairing ended with remote_thread_id still NULL when the 'thread' up-send had gone out but its answer had not come back. ack_outbox finds no outbox row (line 1019 returns Ok) and records nothing, so the pairing never learns the remote thread ID; the next read sees a remote thread no pairing names (linked_thread_by_remote) and mirrors it here as a new local thread. Fix direction: keep the remote thread ID on the ended pairing when the answer arrives (look the pairing up by the up-send's thread, not the outbox row), or record the up-sent thread's key so mirror can match it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1084},"end":{"line":1114},"content_hash":"857ce80f4e8c8e5a65d307aa7a629156b7351896061f47b0a9f4cde4af640f01"},"summary":"A local thread deleted while its 'thread' up-send is unacknowledged can come back as a new local thread","supersedes":"d0bfc77ca4599a2276f8acebf0dc5ebc042c4d1dee27b9f5946232cff05d1f42","tags":["linked-threads","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:39:10.923932Z","id":"0e11b8d2960ceda97cefae9161d6132ddd6688245635acf50160b6fe5d2e8545","body":{"detail":"Tag names are the owner's words (only the owner and the owner's agents make tags), so Vis::filter_artifact (crates/clax-http/src/views/thread.rs) leaves them alone, as the owner's own text. What a tag set says about an artifact is chosen by those who administer it (its creator among them): a person's agent that may read the artifact learns which tags its creator applied, though not any of that creator's own text. Accepted as the feature's point (shared tags, like GitHub labels).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":213},"end":{"line":220},"content_hash":"71c6a12de342dab3e752f71cf69d43a9117e5fc393cbd9b20eee792c3039f8c6"},"summary":"Tags reach every reader of an artifact, agents included, unfiltered by approvals","supersedes":"f6dd43ee604eccc67e27f31432a0a07a113109f1d64002bea11b9022c81b7ba9","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:47:44.716741Z","id":"a549f706b1a2d88b17408e99a2a72ccd0ceb5bb2055cce8c98def0ee78481b58","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs:724-727, record 5367fcc4.\n\nFailure: a home at migration 25 where a person's agent asked a question (a dev home run on this branch) keeps that question's item with recipient NULL after 26, so it sits in the owner's inbox and crates/clax-server/src/inbox.rs render reads its question unscoped (st.question), showing the person's question and answers to the owner, while the person never gets the item. Main's homes hold no person sessions, so they are unaffected. Accepted: migrations 24-26 are unmerged (spec M27), so only a dev home run on this branch can hold such items; questions themselves get their person from their session (questions.person is filled in by the migration).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":747},"end":{"line":750},"content_hash":"d6145a7e9021458c787c755d995bbac04faf22bddf368c6753393c86d9e097ab"},"summary":"Migration 26 leaves every existing inbox item the owner's, including question and finished items a connected person's agent made at schema 24-25","supersedes":"0ddfa157f963e14b879eca8b8c8cca5f4f3506ec2999a9c377840ab6fbc6367e","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/device.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:47:44.784759Z","id":"1c9a2bb3f0c7a8a762efc1b41acd79b94963811eea47dcb2564e269cc57afacb","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/device.rs:183-209, record 4e3bca1d.\n\napprove_device mints the bearer grant at approval; the token is only issued at the next poll, and the code expires after 600 s. Nobody holds the token, but the grant stays listed until revoked by hand.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":219},"end":{"line":245},"content_hash":"d19ff8efaed7ce6f8bd5b2940e8d477fb4564371f0e1d847e91c271fb9d9ac61"},"summary":"A device sign-in approved but never polled (the machine went away) leaves a live agent token on its person's People page","supersedes":"ff76d808fc22ebfaec9c930a42cdff9c5e95df6d33b52695cd704b679f952756","tags":["security","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:47:45.459830Z","id":"37eec885c35313e06fac25f282bd3b72478834bdac8cffdcab52782b06578741","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ca09c4f7","summary":"Renumbered after main's migrations 42-50: the branch's four are now 51 (LEGACY_PATHS), 52 (APP_DATA), 53 (SITE_SESSIONS) and 54 (ASSET_KEYS) in crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs, contiguous after main's 50; the store's migration tests (MARKS_AFTER_APP, ASSET_KEYS_MIGRATION) pass in `just check`.","supersedes":"d3492f5bba56de4ebc8bb1cff9d5d6bddb9b3e326f42fd10bc9026d536f87a04","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:47:45.530024Z","id":"e5cfae1e175d241eb9b4fa0eadd7da7f5beb0d0c7c4587b8b0145a3a8654d7dc","body":{"detail":"For an artifact that exists, publish_step_cut writes the step's documents in the artifact's own store (under the step's operation ID job:<id>:<key>) once the artifact is found at the step's base, and only then writes the version's content and commits the step. A kill between the two, a content write refused (version_present), or another writer taking the version in between leaves the documents written with no version and no step (crates/clax-content-git/tests/steps.rs a_killed_step_resumes_once, a_stray_no_step_marked_is_not_replaced, a_live_steps_stray_is_removed_by_another_write). A resume of the same step applies them no second time, but a step the job abandons (version_moved, plan again) leaves them; the next plan must pin to them (a_push_built_on_a_killed_steps_version_records_it_as_a_push). There is no transaction across the instance's and the artifact's stores.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1498},"end":{"line":1525},"content_hash":"d94bfcac426fe723a8a5e2a64d785f71c6247c1c7c1d3c4b6fa0fa48ab29ab6b"},"suggested_fix":"Write the documents after the step's transaction commits (as a new artifact's are) and let the job's runner retry the document write under the same operation ID until it lands, recording on the step that its documents are pending.","summary":"A publish step's document writes land before its version and stand when the version does not","tags":["site-origins","atomicity","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:10:11.399147Z","id":"87e7b100590f2deeba238dfaba90f853a4fbae7f187df657ea800ff0a5203a4e","body":{"detail":"For an artifact that exists, publish_step_cut writes the step's documents in the artifact's own store (under the step's operation ID job:<id>:<key>) once the artifact is found at the step's base, and only then writes the version's content and commits the step. A kill between the two, a content write refused (version_present), or another writer taking the version in between leaves the documents written with no version and no step (crates/clax-content-git/tests/steps.rs a_killed_step_resumes_once, a_stray_no_step_marked_is_not_replaced, a_live_steps_stray_is_removed_by_another_write). A resume of the same step applies them no second time, but a step the job abandons (version_moved, plan again) leaves them; the next plan must pin to them (a_push_built_on_a_killed_steps_version_records_it_as_a_push). There is no transaction across the instance's and the artifact's stores. A new artifact's writes already take the suggested order: recorded in the step's transaction in job_step_docs and written after it commits, by the step or by its replay (docs_left).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1502},"end":{"line":1529},"content_hash":"d94bfcac426fe723a8a5e2a64d785f71c6247c1c7c1d3c4b6fa0fa48ab29ab6b"},"suggested_fix":"Write the documents after the step's transaction commits, as a new artifact's are (job_step_docs, docs_left), and let the job's runner retry the step until they land; a pinned write that then finds its document moved can no longer refuse the step, so the step would need to record the refusal instead.","summary":"A publish step's document writes land before its version and stand when the version does not","supersedes":"e5cfae1e175d241eb9b4fa0eadd7da7f5beb0d0c7c4587b8b0145a3a8654d7dc","tags":["site-origins","atomicity","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T00:36:54.659620Z","id":"5afa1d1122a3598d8742025621469ab0986055121a80d7f2e029be97e2832393","body":{"detail":"commit_publish_step records a new artifact's writes in job_step_docs in the step's transaction (publish_step_tx), then writes them after it commits (jobs.rs:1565-1570). If that write is refused for good (a path or batch the artifact's store rejects: routes/jobs.rs parse_step checks only the op shape, and the new-artifact branch at jobs.rs:1522-1531 only refuses if_version and update), the version and step stand, the caller gets the error, and the row stays. docs_left then rewrites exactly those recorded writes on every replay, ignoring the retry's own docs, so each retry of that key fails again and the job's client can never read back the recorded step (artifact ID, version). Before 4619c66a a retry with docs: [] got the step back (docs_again returned early on empty docs). Fixes to weigh: check a new artifact's writes against its rules before the transaction, or on a non-transient refusal of recorded writes drop the job_step_docs row and answer the step with the refusal recorded. No test covers a refused after-write.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1938},"end":{"line":1974},"content_hash":"29b40c60ec15744f1365eafcba020b6bf1b6f01cacaf19323d5a271b334fa0e8"},"summary":"A new artifact's step whose recorded writes the store refuses can never be replayed: every retry of its key fails the same way","tags":["review","jobs","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T00:48:15.615123Z","id":"6b10ec6690941aba8074f7815277226026e75860913bf8b6eff3ad54d4544cf8","body":{"detail":"For an artifact that exists, publish_step_cut writes the step's documents in the artifact's own store (under the step's operation ID job:<id>:<key>) once the artifact is found at the step's base, and only then writes the version's content and commits the step. A kill between the two, a content write refused (version_present), or another writer taking the version in between leaves the documents written with no version and no step (crates/clax-content-git/tests/steps.rs a_killed_step_resumes_once, a_stray_no_step_marked_is_not_replaced, a_live_steps_stray_is_removed_by_another_write). A resume of the same step applies them no second time, but a step the job abandons (version_moved, plan again) leaves them; the next plan must pin to them (a_push_built_on_a_killed_steps_version_records_it_as_a_push). There is no transaction across the instance's and the artifact's stores. A new artifact's writes already take the suggested order: recorded in the step's transaction in job_step_docs and written after it commits, by the step or by its replay (docs_left).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1508},"end":{"line":1535},"content_hash":"d94bfcac426fe723a8a5e2a64d785f71c6247c1c7c1d3c4b6fa0fa48ab29ab6b"},"suggested_fix":"Write the documents after the step's transaction commits, as a new artifact's are (job_step_docs, docs_left), and let the job's runner retry the step until they land; a pinned write that then finds its document moved can no longer refuse the step, so the step would need to record the refusal instead.","summary":"A publish step's document writes land before its version and stand when the version does not","supersedes":"87e7b100590f2deeba238dfaba90f853a4fbae7f187df657ea800ff0a5203a4e","tags":["site-origins","atomicity","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T00:48:15.695185Z","id":"3752e6c0b1cb3b9f9f4fd64126dfa14d46f2c3a8fcc002671088f0e61fe71f8a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ddac3380","span":{"start":{"line":1938},"end":{"line":1974},"content_hash":"d09c0542ab619766872f97084153a6b1f51126f02e238bca46d902c09dce813b"},"summary":"Fixed: publish_step_cut checks a step's writes with app_data::check_batch (count, paths, duplicates, update and set bodies) before anything is recorded, so writes every store refuses never commit a step; a refusal for good (refused_for_good) after the commit, or in docs_left on a replay, drops the job_step_docs row: the committing call returns the error and replays answer the recorded step. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: 888 passed, 0 failed, 3 ignored, including jobs::tests::a_new_apps_refused_writes_refuse_its_step_before_it_commits (MAX_BATCH+1 writes; a set body deeper than MAX_DEPTH: no artifact, no step, no row) and jobs::tests::a_new_apps_writes_refused_after_its_step_are_given_up_and_the_step_answered (a refusing writer: the error, then the replayed step; refused recorded writes on replay: the replayed step twice, the row gone; an unreachable store keeps the row).","supersedes":"5afa1d1122a3598d8742025621469ab0986055121a80d7f2e029be97e2832393","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T19:34:25.879757Z","id":"3fd115f9ee64359ecdd13ff6b0cf0659e7408d7e2ce6f1dc6efce050e04ed075","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"82f069dddebad0d870cd438620c6287505acedaaf5facf7cb3be3a9c7c0d33d3","summary":"Since 4fb02e27 a hosted instance holds the owner's and the owner's agents' repository tokens to the owner's reach when minted and at every recheck (crates/clax-http/src/git_remotes.rs allows_one: MemberRights::owner(..).allows_at), and the hosts list the owner's own tokens for that recheck (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs live_held_tokens). So a write token this instance mints, the only kind credited to the owner on a host that names no pusher, reaches only artifacts the owner made or that are shared with the owner, and is revoked when such a share ends. What remains: a token minted outside Clax (the Cloudflare dashboard, the Artifacts API) still pushes as the owner, and Store::standing still allows the owner's pushes.","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T22:34:37.272637Z","id":"c1defae3d15e778f5934d4de20753a75c9c237c56fcbd9ce688d0abe53133e8a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:037f2afc","summary":"Store::reinstate_person (crates/clax-store/src/people.rs) clears blocked_at through github::unblock_in, behind the owner's POST /api/people/<pid>/reinstate and People's Reinstate. Evidence: bazel test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test --test_arg=reinstating_restores_access_and_unblocks_github prints 'test people::tests::reinstating_restores_access_and_unblocks_github ... ok' (the test revokes a GitHub person, sees github_blocked, reinstates, and signs the account in again).","supersedes":"b79ada9c7343bf9f5b33c9938212a509963ec4ac7c37f6ada1d39019076965c0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T22:34:37.323790Z","id":"302358960b5f1a08a43ce7e0a6ee9ecc3eedbdef4ade15301ba7edfa38bbd436","body":{"detail":"Store::revoke_person (crates/clax-store/src/people.rs) does not end the person's browser_sessions rows; Store::browser_session_of_hash (crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs) hides a revoked person's session by person_revoked_at alone. Store::reinstate_person clears person_revoked_at, so any session cookie of theirs that has not expired (30 days) works again at once, with no new sign-in. Their grants and agent tokens stay ended. For a person invited by link (no GitHub account) that old session is their only way back, since a hosted invite now makes a new person only; for a revocation made because a browser was lost, it reopens that browser. Options: end the person's browser sessions at revocation (they then can return only through GitHub), or end them at reinstating.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1749},"end":{"line":1770},"content_hash":"fc7a285b5e666b8a8e8dfc4301f5776759f5d1e9b8cb69cc2ab2257e5eb8112b"},"summary":"Reinstating a person brings back their unexpired browser sessions","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T22:34:37.323924Z","id":"57728dee968a62faecb43cf719dcba395d279d99cfa72662a99e4a3bcc3530f9","body":{"detail":"There is no column saying an invite made a new person (no migration), so invite_made_its_person treats an invite as a new person's when its viewer row was created in the same instant as the invite, the row has no other invite, and it has held no browser session, grant or GitHub identity. A viewer row made in the same clock instant as a later invite naming it, with none of that history, would pass; on a hosted daemon every viewer row is made by setup, an invite, a guest's sign-in (which makes a browser session) or a GitHub sign-in (which links an identity), so none does today. hosted::tests::an_invite_naming_an_existing_viewer_signs_no_browser_in covers a revoked person and a guest made in the same instant.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":412},"end":{"line":428},"content_hash":"4da3cf6c2f8eda6331de3640f25ef5cfe9ec954a6570e26faa2ee4f7002c2416"},"summary":"Whether an invite made its person is inferred from timestamps and the row's history","tags":["review","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.019390Z","id":"b7e74134650d319b1623f96ed06812d14b075445b77e8bd4e13899e2a425dc7c","body":{"detail":"record_render stores any well-formed digest for any draft, so a client holding the token and not the owner's agents (the route refuses those) can record a clean render of files it never rendered. The gate then holds only as far as the app reports truthfully. Comparing the digest with the draft's current version (clax_core::digest::manifest_digest of its files) would tie a render to content the core holds, but a draft is published version by version while the app renders, so the digest may name a version the draft has since moved past.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/drafts.rs:430:446 to crates/clax-store/src/drafts.rs:464:480: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":464},"end":{"line":480},"content_hash":"f9bc71b76fcbab8e6c00b3dda25d7be4b6e40a733d2e06630875f8abde374335"},"suggested_fix":"Accept a render only when some version of the draft has that digest (versions.files_json), and answer 409 otherwise.","summary":"A recorded render is the app's word: the core does not check that the digest is of the draft's files","supersedes":"aae0642789c6d62e06b6ac3d5bf8348c93c6e585ed7856e79d6138fb857e6b31","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.070059Z","id":"9a63abca43239aa407ca9b3a03b9ee54369394da0d94bc1e36ddc82557a8b77d","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs:858-862, record 3ac434ed.\n\nAn agent token is a bearer grant (grants.bearer = 1, its cxa_ token in grant_tokens, kept out of credential_index so it never passes the signed Clax-Grant path). The endpoint resolves Authorization: Bearer cxa_... with bearer_grant, then Store::grant_caller for its person and rights, and builds Caller::PersonAgent; no route accepts the token yet.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs:858:862 to crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs:900:904: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":900},"end":{"line":904},"content_hash":"6118ad026448bf7342835eef06f09082a183699f7c1c18391bc4c90fa653e306"},"summary":"Store::bearer_grant is how the remote MCP endpoint should authenticate an agent token","supersedes":"d180d1282705f126ad829cbf70930679cb88b286da7649d253acf7ccaa496a7a","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.121924Z","id":"67ccfb58b36116b959af33e93a88fdac60f6beb0e1ca0dd25a372d988edecfff","body":{"detail":"Spec §9 makes a stopped make job of every plans.json entry that no pending make claims. plans.json keeps the plan of every app built since, finished ones included (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/plan.dart PlanStore), so that would put a Keep going row in the queue for every finished build. The import makes one only while a feature is todo or doing.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs:472:474 to crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs:499:501: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":499},"end":{"line":501},"content_hash":"d764f559a2fae8f0174c4b236ea86cb57d1344812d64405f866cdd0fab37635c"},"summary":"A plan with no feature left to build makes no job","supersedes":"9fd36173bd98e32d83d1fbb7ecc994bfb5eddaafc77f8fa550ee8b3c536dac5c","tags":["revisit:the owner wants every kept plan in the queue, or a finished build's plan is needed in the core","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.171895Z","id":"4467ea2c83a46eeea3fd6cabe3dc97b2284d5e0a840d689a907eada01f19d5ae","body":{"detail":"The app's recovery starts the build of every plan not under a provisional key that is buildable (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart _recoverBuilds, and _buildable at worker.dart:705-706: not stopped, features to build, spentUsd under buildCapUsd). The import makes every plan with a todo or doing feature a stopped make job and does not read the plan's stopped field, so after the import a build the app would have resumed by itself waits for Keep going, and looks the same as one the person stopped. The choice is the owner's: queued for a buildable plan (the app's behaviour), or stopped for all (the person resumes each).\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs:479:492 to crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs:506:519: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":506},"end":{"line":519},"content_hash":"f3da61b6f158b7f8a9c29abffc14f53ef48365ed39bbe13d5980dd93e6b54a59"},"summary":"A plan under an app with features to build imports as a stopped make, though the app's own recovery builds it","supersedes":"0c194fcb63b4ecddf29ac0b160b0799f461154cb8f7b1fa928c087aeb9b35638","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.223828Z","id":"3f19efbc145959b0d2777952d3f2108116c13864667fc842612f49887b9cbc79","body":{"detail":"The app moves a make's plan to the app's ID once the make made it (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart newApp, plans.move) and clears pending-make.json after (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart, the finally of the make), so a pending make whose request has only an app's plan ended after making its app, and importing it would make that app a second time. The same inputs come from a second make of an earlier app's exact request that was cut off before its first plan_set (or a single-call make, which keeps no plan): that make is left out too, named in the summary's left_out. Not taken: keeping every such make queued (a made one makes a duplicate app), or telling them apart by time (pending-make.json keeps no time).\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs:494:514 to crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs:521:541: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":521},"end":{"line":541},"content_hash":"54dc184a022c804ee548f0f05b6fa264b3bb92bc9019b6ad911a5b5a23a69de0"},"summary":"A pending make is left out as made whenever an app's plan names its request and no provisional plan claims the make","supersedes":"9e3264daea4500a5cc3bd4d9e043c437501b227d76e2bfb45a92c455d475e46c","tags":["revisit:a make retried with an earlier app's request is found missing after the import","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.272691Z","id":"d4f2a7a56946e9f202b0857afe076c60c2787d052450822ea86e6de32f6c2de5","body":{"detail":"The app's recovery (_settleDocs in apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart) sent a record's document writes again with their pins when docs_done was false. On the queue a version's documents are written only inside its publish step, and an imported record's publish:<base> step is already committed, so the job the import writes (turn:1 and publish:<base>, then the reply) ends done and the record's db writes are never made. Test a_ledger_change_with_nothing_left_to_apply_is_done (base 2: documents never written, replied) imports it queued with a reply owing no thread.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs:634:667 to crates/clax-store/src/imports.rs:659:692: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":659},"end":{"line":692},"content_hash":"39b71fa2355b01786bd6b304f5e37fe5dcb04913404ea942cd4beea10826e35f"},"suggested_fix":"Either a step the queue commits for a landed version's pinned document writes (the store's batch with if_version pins in the step's transaction), or the import leaving such a record out and saying so in left_out.","summary":"A ledger change whose version landed with documents unwritten imports without them: the queue has no step that writes a landed version's documents","supersedes":"b64fd8cd88b53f2327d6204ba0e869ea0e88f2fe378bbcdc8fa11a734ac05c11","tags":["queue","import","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.324497Z","id":"ac4c5586fbdaeca948845b472f6205f4730f1ef3965028d54e372d73ea7440cb","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1363-1368, record 0118687f.\n\nconnection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:1589:1594 to crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:1611:1616: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1611},"end":{"line":1616},"content_hash":"c1c86e26871ba066020c75f1d9b1b954ee91add027a8fb30f98694a07930d59d"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","supersedes":"2eb022c9f93f2f45d225701a5bc3cf358bb49deeb5edd707d4263a3b45138f35","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.373731Z","id":"90142b51808dc6a1bd9bc5c1fba84a008eb04d434127fa84fcada4aba3f2396a","body":{"detail":"inbox_groups groups all of a query's matches (GROUP BY artifact over the driver's walk, with a temporary B-tree; crates/clax-store/src/plans.rs allows it for the ' groups' shapes) so each group's total and unread are exact across pages, then reads each listed group's newest rows by inbox_by_artifact. The unread section reads only unread items (inbox_unread); the read section, unfolded, reads the recipient's whole read history. The route runs it in the bulk lane (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs list). Accepted: an inbox of tens of thousands of items groups in milliseconds, and the read section loads only when unfolded.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:1675:1756 to crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:1697:1778: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1697},"end":{"line":1778},"content_hash":"c21e4c7179b4ee93301d6e354ee8a31dc042ecc2101279bbec0f7a94446d122b"},"summary":"Grouping the inbox by artifact reads every match to count each group","supersedes":"a885e2354eb808178f2943fbbe892b6cc510792607fee93dd8d95bc298f3cb69","tags":["inbox","perf","revisit:a group=artifact read over 50 ms in just perf, or inboxes past 100k items","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.423039Z","id":"88c9703834c3d55879e2c0d0a7a5ca7c83a86510b427388581fe5c95cdc241d0","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1552-1556, record 6014047e.\n\nnote_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:1860:1864 to crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:1898:1902: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1898},"end":{"line":1902},"content_hash":"df46c2781c4e06aa0fe53e6fadd564b9bcbcad9e060403b47de165ac7d60413a"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","supersedes":"5ab9a83e4245981d00d2bdbf73d7825a012475ae84d9647b68bf6a8f9161e029","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.472287Z","id":"a83632e54cba4d3390b5d3b2f1f6716dfd9bb56decc2a9b0432ae3e9de1d7338","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs:757-783, record 102e3b6a.\n\nMeasured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:768:794 to crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:1011:1037: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1011},"end":{"line":1037},"content_hash":"b3bfd31319c95da4542d5ac7bd7f9fa165b3082f4e9534f5f055a9a24bdcbbee"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"0e4f092370e31dcb4f89bb6cf9a6af26d09b32d88d9d0182e1eeab2a0b372ac6","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.522059Z","id":"b7bf9f84311954fb8d2e0129dbc0f766068dff49eeb1f7b4ef0239bcd32db5ac","body":{"detail":"narrowing() returns None when the person's rights are within the access the client asked for (people.rs:456-458); request_grant (people.rs:1115) and approve_grant (people.rs:1297-1301) then store narrow_json NULL, and grant_caller_in (people.rs:2541-2550) gives the grant the person's current rights. A client that asked for, say, read access while its person held only read keeps no record of that ask: when the owner later raises the person to the collaborator preset, the machine's agents gain write access it never asked for. The asked access survives only in the grant.request audit record (people.rs:627). Whether a grant should follow its person's rights upward is a product decision; the store currently cannot keep the ask either way.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:454:458 to crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:490:494: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":490},"end":{"line":494},"content_hash":"913a42f078e2d657c9aa36665eee58191ea253819621bde3a4a1cca32a66af23"},"suggested_fix":"Store the asked access whenever it is narrower than full rights (narrow_json = access unless access is Rights::full()), so effective rights stay person ∩ asked as the person's rights change; or record that following the person upward is intended in the grant section of the multi-person spec.","summary":"A grant whose client asked for at least its person's rights stores no narrowing, so it widens with every later raise of the person's rights beyond what it asked","supersedes":"8332718f9ffd0e03ff684a160447439939c4238a9bf4d0319c320eb3cf3ede88","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:45.571616Z","id":"e7ad8518868298ac543053ec80616922ecd93e9fa284b76e2769be8f45aac027","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs:1088-1102, record b5059e16.\n\nFor flow invite the grant's events carry grant_id and person but not invite_id, so the journal cannot join invite.create to the grant made from it except by person and time; invites.grant_id holds the link only while the row lives.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:1117:1131 to crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:1153:1167: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1153},"end":{"line":1167},"content_hash":"5797052e7ab6d41d1c7e1138621f9475ea1bbb4d84154b5bc865aea2b46b476f"},"suggested_fix":"Add invite_id to grant.request (flow invite) and to audit spec section 6.13 and multi-person spec section 20.2.","summary":"An invite-flow grant.request and grant.approve do not name the invite they redeemed","supersedes":"e9d6932d46817207d8a8fa6cfeb59d04be600176af7791c240b87cfb702dba27","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:46.337922Z","id":"871aa99e27bbaea8afee0ab8f0939c1501e7849950df311c53afd410a5b662a2","body":{"detail":"github_sign_in's setup branch (crates/clax-store/src/github.rs:207-218) calls hosted_setup_via (crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs:417), which commits the owner row, hosted_setup and the browser session in its own transaction, and only then runs link() in a second with_tx (github.rs:217). If the second transaction fails (a database error, or the process stopping between the two), the instance is set up with an owner row that no GitHub account is linked to: the owner's browser holds a session, but the account's next sign-in is matched only by owner_login, and a share waiting for the owner's login stays unbound until then. The non-setup owner branch (github.rs:220-238) links and signs in within one transaction.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/github.rs:207:218 to crates/clax-store/src/github.rs:201:212: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":201},"end":{"line":212},"content_hash":"b3b85a09d3fc0223666ecc51bd3b59bea2ad573f4319256cb41e584c1003cb75"},"suggested_fix":"Give hosted_setup_via a variant that runs inside a caller's transaction (or takes a closure run before commit), and call link() in that same transaction, with a test that makes link fail and expects no setup left.","summary":"The first GitHub owner sign-in sets up the instance and links the account in two transactions","supersedes":"d6fecf127a99bb8661ebe42347e317b85abae095792469c6b33e1e277f448347","tags":["review","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:46.388992Z","id":"3b92cf74758712f7b90268d5b86b6286714b64efa8319b3a442047bea10723d7","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs:331-346, record 87ab348f.\n\nshare_artifact resolves a login through github_identities.login, which is refreshed only at each sign-in (crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs link). If account A signed in as 'octo', later renamed on GitHub and never signed in here again, and someone else now holds 'octo' on GitHub, a share to '@octo' binds to A's person, not to whoever owns the login today. A login no one here has signed in with waits and binds at its first sign-in, which is safe: from then on the share follows the person, not the login (tested in shares.rs a_login_share_waits_for_its_first_sign_in_then_follows_the_person).\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs:331:346 to crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs:383:396: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":383},"end":{"line":396},"content_hash":"dfa12ca295cf2836c03c79e7de611bdcb7e955ca6d01af0878e30754914ff03d"},"suggested_fix":"Look the login up on GitHub's API (GET /users/<login>) when sharing, and bind by numeric ID.","summary":"A share by GitHub login binds at once to whichever account last signed in with that login here, which may be stale after a rename","supersedes":"3b63b900cef39fb78cbbbd827efcab83dfc14527172cd3b3bc2a6e3b8bbd7e66","tags":["security","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:46.440055Z","id":"32b759157766c727a8f926a48f644a8d80020ad5829c7a7fe0d660cedd642531","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/shares.rs:333-346, record 95291e43.\n\nshare_artifact's login lookup (github_identities joined to viewers) checks only that the row is not the owner's; it does not read github_identities.blocked_at or viewers.person_revoked_at. ShareTo::Person refuses a revoked person (unknown_person), so the two paths disagree. No access follows (a blocked account cannot sign in and a revoked person's grants end), but the sharer sees the share as granted to a named person rather than refused.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs:333:346 to crates/clax-store/src/shares.rs:385:396: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":385},"end":{"line":396},"content_hash":"ce5a66146948635a2d1e5e072cb900b086cda5a0dce7a06472beb34936472fe1"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse such a login as ShareTo::Person refuses a revoked person, or show the share as blocked.","summary":"A share by login binds to an account whose GitHub identity is blocked or whose person is revoked, and the dialog lists it as an ordinary person","supersedes":"3561332cb0a396d0c3108f501b9b050c474a1f7079f2ca9063ec3cd9c77ae3a2","tags":["sharing","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/github.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:46.643964Z","id":"513dd72802c568e2d8b4c6ecc7bfddf05a53f516952d42cb9bc0c88e313aef9c","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/github.rs:313-348, record d40983d3.\n\ncheck_quota counts the person's live artifacts (MemberCaps::max_artifacts, MEMBER_MAX_ARTIFACTS / [hosted] member_max_artifacts, default 200) and is called from create_artifact_async (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs) and fork_artifact_async (crates/clax-core/src/store/forks.rs). Nothing bounds the bytes a member writes: new versions of their own artifacts, asset uploads and pushed commits are uncounted, so one member can fill the content store within MAX_ASSET_BYTES per upload and the version size limits. A byte cap needs a running per-account counter charged in the version and asset transactions (record_version_locked, upload_asset).\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/github.rs:312:347 to crates/clax-store/src/github.rs:316:361: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file. The span now covers check_quota and check_quota_in.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":316},"end":{"line":361},"content_hash":"cec5f8a43ec3e22ddb04f382d8b8a745aa4a047b6cc3680e8cabc1a6f350a2f8"},"summary":"A GitHub member's account is capped by artifact count alone: no cap on stored bytes","supersedes":"7bb059c47702678d9680a7f63eaee6a9d513b387ba14aa9c0117b7ab8ca1920f","tags":["deferred","hosted","github","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:46.695366Z","id":"77dd829f5bc718ea3b6ecbbd8a6e5dc1baf1992112c9991df5ead64bbb13de05","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs:1477-1569, record fbaca2aa.\n\napprove_owner_on_connect is the single approval made without a browser (spec section 21 item 3, M15). It is bounded to the connect: once per grant, within OWNER_ANSWER_SECS (10 minutes) of the tokens' issue, never once the person has made or revoked any approval of the owner (409 owner_answered, so a revocation in People stands; 409 answer_closed after the window), replays refused by accept_t first. Only the continuation token says it, never the access token agents sign with (crates/clax-server/tests/api_grants.rs a_connected_machine_approves_the_owner_through_its_continuation), and clax connect refuses on an agent channel (crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs connect_refuses_on_an_agent_channel). What remains: a process of the person's that reads remote.json within those ten minutes, before clax connect answers, could answer yes for them; the person can revoke it in People, and that revocation is final. Tests: store::people::tests::connecting_records_the_persons_approval_of_the_owner_once, the_answer_about_the_owner_never_overrides_the_person.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:1506:1598 to crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:1554:1650: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file. The span now covers approve_owner_on_connect with its doc comment, the function the finding describes.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1554},"end":{"line":1650},"content_hash":"8b49154fc9098682cf00b3361bed19c40fca7124099c621c373014f446fba351"},"summary":"The person's approval of the owner is recorded without a browser once, at connect: an agent present then could answer for the person","supersedes":"9de6ef359975cc995a7761da3ad0c8c793bce195708af226f90df5562b0a17ec","tags":["security","spec:6.3","spec:21","M15","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T23:51:46.746027Z","id":"ec7af8dd519f22fa81cd14a0646f4afca8b5b60e16698ef639bc13bef69df1b2","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs:2273-2301, record 1d272fa3.\n\nAn invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:2273:2301 to crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:2460:2491: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file. The span now covers release_unconnected with its doc comment, where the finding's UPDATE statement is.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2460},"end":{"line":2491},"content_hash":"59de2faae5f6d78c06e63a87be227a7c1fed2124f222f77a39897b37f0981d95"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"05ca3c90a72b9254238c8d4ff6ac2fdff13d731d1a21261c0e67eac9642a67cd","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:08.807703Z","id":"8b351ffbe8b5d0e30859019e461afcff8d8c498b7dc40cc70ad15c37209081e0","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1363-1368, record 0118687f.\n\nconnection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1611},"end":{"line":1616},"content_hash":"c1c86e26871ba066020c75f1d9b1b954ee91add027a8fb30f98694a07930d59d"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","supersedes":"358b66eba9ba32dbea514d6edda85f7209b8c33f5db04464e67ad1ad23cd7f3a","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:08.874494Z","id":"98d8cc53f069ea3d34ecb0c2416f192135486258cb866bcba8ce570c313242b6","body":{"detail":"inbox_groups groups all of a query's matches (GROUP BY artifact over the driver's walk, with a temporary B-tree; crates/clax-store/src/plans.rs allows it for the ' groups' shapes) so each group's total and unread are exact across pages, then reads each listed group's newest rows by inbox_by_artifact. The unread section reads only unread items (inbox_unread); the read section, unfolded, reads the recipient's whole read history. The route runs it in the bulk lane (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs list). Accepted: an inbox of tens of thousands of items groups in milliseconds, and the read section loads only when unfolded.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1697},"end":{"line":1778},"content_hash":"c21e4c7179b4ee93301d6e354ee8a31dc042ecc2101279bbec0f7a94446d122b"},"summary":"Grouping the inbox by artifact reads every match to count each group","supersedes":"693eda0b3ba339509ef7d1fa80f2cb7815c6d4db655cc509a2a5a23160af66a3","tags":["inbox","perf","revisit:a group=artifact read over 50 ms in just perf, or inboxes past 100k items","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:08.941426Z","id":"779abbe0b217240f8daa8a1c8487c96f4dceccadab3b4f51a11b9711af720f79","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1552-1556, record 6014047e.\n\nnote_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1898},"end":{"line":1902},"content_hash":"df46c2781c4e06aa0fe53e6fadd564b9bcbcad9e060403b47de165ac7d60413a"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","supersedes":"d66522f45b75e146d3ce0504de997d5ad88a35df890f4f7fb20e654f9666b357","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:09.013620Z","id":"5d6ff123487b7b539b0ed5401d3d86928d9caada4402b7385bec96cd5cbda795","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/hosted.rs:858-862, record 3ac434ed.\n\nAn agent token is a bearer grant (grants.bearer = 1, its cxa_ token in grant_tokens, kept out of credential_index so it never passes the signed Clax-Grant path). The endpoint resolves Authorization: Bearer cxa_... with bearer_grant, then Store::grant_caller for its person and rights, and builds Caller::PersonAgent; no route accepts the token yet.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs:858:862 to crates/clax-store/src/hosted.rs:900:904: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":916},"end":{"line":920},"content_hash":"6118ad026448bf7342835eef06f09082a183699f7c1c18391bc4c90fa653e306"},"summary":"Store::bearer_grant is how the remote MCP endpoint should authenticate an agent token","supersedes":"9a63abca43239aa407ca9b3a03b9ee54369394da0d94bc1e36ddc82557a8b77d","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:09.079422Z","id":"3d0c3b2c07d6499cd6579d970338af34f4f82f5c709d8f4a426f82b055793049","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs:757-783, record 102e3b6a.\n\nMeasured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:768:794 to crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:1011:1037: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1031},"end":{"line":1057},"content_hash":"b3bfd31319c95da4542d5ac7bd7f9fa165b3082f4e9534f5f055a9a24bdcbbee"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"a83632e54cba4d3390b5d3b2f1f6716dfd9bb56decc2a9b0432ae3e9de1d7338","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T01:44:09.145721Z","id":"e1d30660cf1e472832e0bc9815645156a79c902e5c43f2c9687a01830f51e067","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs:2273-2301, record 1d272fa3.\n\nAn invite that expires unredeemed records nothing (audit spec section 6.13 lists only invite.create and invite.revoke). When release_unconnected then returns its person to a plain viewer it sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL in the sweep or a revoke, so rights set by invite.create's rights or person.rights change with no person.rights event: the journal's last word on that person's rights is wrong.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:2273:2301 to crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:2460:2491: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file. The span now covers release_unconnected with its doc comment, where the finding's UPDATE statement is.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2523},"end":{"line":2554},"content_hash":"59de2faae5f6d78c06e63a87be227a7c1fed2124f222f77a39897b37f0981d95"},"summary":"An invite's lapse is not recorded, and release_unconnected clears a person's flag and rights without an event","supersedes":"ec7af8dd519f22fa81cd14a0646f4afca8b5b60e16698ef639bc13bef69df1b2","tags":["review","rebase","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T02:22:45.699401Z","id":"50d83a1bada19fc6f925e11db76a962513716fc37d3ba9777b35d343f6641ff6","body":{"detail":"ServerHost::check_write (crates/clax-server/src/bot.rs) asks the owner's scope (MemberRights::allows_at) before a reply, resolve, document write or publish is planned; the guard each journaled write runs in its transaction returns Ok for the owner's own run (bot_rights None) and applies a person's rights without the reach rule. A share removed between the plan and the commit does not stop that one write.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":2061},"end":{"line":2065},"content_hash":"e50776ab99bf9fbc541a472a67b0afdf43d410be5e2cc501ea810301d9c2c3fc"},"suggested_fix":"Pass whether the daemon is hosted to check_bot_write_in and check the person's reach (Store::reach, and the share rights beyond it) in the same transaction.","summary":"check_bot_write_in, the in-transaction guard of a ClaxBot write, holds the owner's run to no scope: on a hosted Clax the reach is checked only when the write is planned","tags":["claxbot","hosted","reach","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit_query.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T04:27:58.973058Z","id":"2e9a0c0c1bdb6c3c3aa84f824863d51cb5881325ef21265bc77dbc7b83029b3e","body":{"detail":"scope_sql matches the actor's type and person through json_extract on every row, checks shares through correlated subqueries over artifact.update events (by audit_events_artifact), and text search is LIKE over kind, actor and body; only the kind groups (audit_events_kind, migration 42) and the artifact filter use an index directly. On a home with a large journal a member's audit page reads the whole table per page. Measure with just perf before relying on it for hosted instances with many members. Since c8ccd472 the share check is three correlated subqueries per candidate event: one over artifact.update share set/remove events on the event's artifact (audit_events_artifact) and two over person.revoke events for the reader (an audit_events_kind range, then json_extract on the body), which end a share period at a revocation; each is an index range scan per row the outer query examines.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":127},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"32a10c2157cd4f949ea944bf279afaf1b36e14ad2cf97a679c30dcd286169c89"},"suggested_fix":"Store the actor's person key in an indexed column (or a side table) when an event is recorded, keep share periods in a table, and scope on them.","summary":"A non-admin's audit query and every text search scan audit_events with json_extract","supersedes":"4a2d7e107419eda86dcc2d6876831acdaf2d38181826e814a71be39bd097a57f","tags":["claxbot","audit","perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit_query.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T04:28:00.156342Z","id":"f6997561a2bb444c2788146e6b47c9453d024e9855a616053f439cc86e2e9021","body":{"detail":"scope_sql admits, for a non-admin, events on artifacts they created and, as the implemented default, events on an artifact shared with them from the artifact.update that set the share to the one that removed it (or to the person's revocation, even if they connect again under the same public ID; a share as it is now also counts from its created_at unless revoked since, for shares made by GitHub login before the person had a public ID). audit_query::tests::a_share_shows_its_artifact_s_events_while_it_held pins it. Open questions for the owner: should a share's events stay visible after it is removed (it is not now), and should a viewer-only share see every event on the artifact (it does now), or only views and comments? audit_query::tests::revoking_a_person_ends_their_shares_in_the_trail_even_after_they_reconnect pins the revocation rule.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":127},"end":{"line":162},"content_hash":"32a10c2157cd4f949ea944bf279afaf1b36e14ad2cf97a679c30dcd286169c89"},"summary":"Audit scoping now includes artifacts shared with the reader, while the share held: the owner should confirm this default","supersedes":"86e0241bb348efcf9a48e80a41d46e6b6985f1574f22537f9a22245f958b67ab","tags":["claxbot","audit","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit_query.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T04:52:32.596883Z","id":"b39f21b11cdc77bee5cad289ac8ce379103dd5f244f56c8399d4bdec88b8acaa","body":{"detail":"scope_sql matches the actor's type and person through json_extract on every row, checks shares through correlated subqueries over artifact.update events (by audit_events_artifact), and text search is LIKE over kind, actor and body; only the kind groups (audit_events_kind, migration 42) and the artifact filter use an index directly. On a home with a large journal a member's audit page reads the whole table per page. Measure with just perf before relying on it for hosted instances with many members. Since c8ccd472 the share check is three correlated subqueries per candidate event: one over artifact.update share set/remove events on the event's artifact (audit_events_artifact) and two over person.revoke events for the reader (an audit_events_kind range, then json_extract on the body), which end a share period at a revocation; each is an index range scan per row the outer query examines.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":135},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"32a10c2157cd4f949ea944bf279afaf1b36e14ad2cf97a679c30dcd286169c89"},"suggested_fix":"Store the actor's person key in an indexed column (or a side table) when an event is recorded, keep share periods in a table, and scope on them.","summary":"A non-admin's audit query and every text search scan audit_events with json_extract","supersedes":"2e9a0c0c1bdb6c3c3aa84f824863d51cb5881325ef21265bc77dbc7b83029b3e","tags":["claxbot","audit","perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/audit_query.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T04:52:32.742360Z","id":"89b82ddcc7925a8f69c818fb7f61d0d1975471746445dd4557a32245ad57886b","body":{"detail":"scope_sql admits, for a non-admin, events on artifacts they created and, as the implemented default, events on an artifact shared with them from the artifact.update that set the share to the one that removed it (or to the person's revocation, even if they connect again under the same public ID; a share as it is now also counts from its created_at unless revoked since, for shares made by GitHub login before the person had a public ID). audit_query::tests::a_share_shows_its_artifact_s_events_while_it_held pins it. Open questions for the owner: should a share's events stay visible after it is removed (it is not now), and should a viewer-only share see every event on the artifact (it does now), or only views and comments? audit_query::tests::revoking_a_person_ends_their_shares_in_the_trail_even_after_they_reconnect pins the revocation rule.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":135},"end":{"line":170},"content_hash":"32a10c2157cd4f949ea944bf279afaf1b36e14ad2cf97a679c30dcd286169c89"},"summary":"Audit scoping now includes artifacts shared with the reader, while the share held: the owner should confirm this default","supersedes":"f6997561a2bb444c2788146e6b47c9453d024e9855a616053f439cc86e2e9021","tags":["claxbot","audit","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:11.100778Z","id":"70a684f7cbe337edd7a664bf4b040406f961bfb470ee082ee3c6c61f675eb763","body":{"detail":"record_render stores any well-formed digest for any draft, so a client holding the token and not the owner's agents (the route refuses those) can record a clean render of files it never rendered. The gate then holds only as far as the app reports truthfully. Comparing the digest with the draft's current version (clax_core::digest::manifest_digest of its files) would tie a render to content the core holds, but a draft is published version by version while the app renders, so the digest may name a version the draft has since moved past.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":394},"end":{"line":410},"content_hash":"f9bc71b76fcbab8e6c00b3dda25d7be4b6e40a733d2e06630875f8abde374335"},"suggested_fix":"Accept a render only when some version of the draft has that digest (versions.files_json), and answer 409 otherwise.","summary":"A recorded render is the app's word: the core does not check that the digest is of the draft's files","supersedes":"08df4ee9fd04dca48ba56babb34808534b970082d2e01077ad1195e307d71bfd","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T14:57:11.181534Z","id":"a2e1ccb1af724dfe69d95c7f3c37fac4ecb0fb2910f06f956aac00cea9adc4f9","body":{"detail":"record_render stores any well-formed digest for any draft, so a client holding the token and not the owner's agents (the route refuses those) can record a clean render of files it never rendered. The gate then holds only as far as the app reports truthfully. Comparing the digest with the draft's current version (clax_core::digest::manifest_digest of its files) would tie a render to content the core holds, but a draft is published version by version while the app renders, so the digest may name a version the draft has since moved past.\n\nRe-anchored unchanged from crates/clax-store/src/drafts.rs:430:446 to crates/clax-store/src/drafts.rs:464:480: originally recorded by mailto:alex@kesling.co (ai); the code it describes moved when this branch changed the file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":394},"end":{"line":410},"content_hash":"f9bc71b76fcbab8e6c00b3dda25d7be4b6e40a733d2e06630875f8abde374335"},"suggested_fix":"Accept a render only when some version of the draft has that digest (versions.files_json), and answer 409 otherwise.","summary":"A recorded render is the app's word: the core does not check that the digest is of the draft's files","supersedes":"b7e74134650d319b1623f96ed06812d14b075445b77e8bd4e13899e2a425dc7c","tags":["session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
