{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-24T16:31:25.844593Z","id":"6c1178dfe5b5065654df4ee7c9ce5c84994be5ef91fc5fdd6bb256039b4184a2","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of 98d8cc53 (crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs:1697:1778): the same record re-anchored on two lines of history (this branch's rebases and main), differing only in the span it cites.","supersedes":"90142b51808dc6a1bd9bc5c1fba84a008eb04d434127fa84fcada4aba3f2396a","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:5ba3638a-dc4b-4c8f-8349-140e70a28c92"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:01:33.059784Z","id":"1d76212ede47057809064813d1067637985796d0ba088320715fe5a4442527bf","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"d9389757cab927090053f7a4976099e8bb493673dd4601fcbd99024c86d276fb","summary":"The rerun's cost timed out CI: clax_store_lib_test took 135-296 s on CI after 652f225fc (83-194 s before) and hit CI's 300 s limit on four of eight pushes to main. cb7bd1f8b runs the rerun as its own target, //crates/clax-store:clax_store_one_connection_test (CLAX_TEST_STORE_ONE_CONNECTION=apart skips it in the lib test); locally the two then took 66.6 s and 63.1 s side by side. The rerun's cost itself is unchanged.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-26T20:29:31.578086Z","id":"09c5d1e19d9f3dd53fb38045e0f905fcf52470187c293dee7eed237f34535d69","body":{"detail":"Adopting a pushed commit builds its ValidatedPublish with capabilities: None, so a clax.json the push edits, adds or removes is stored as a file while artifacts.capabilities_json and versions.capabilities_json keep the previous declaration. The file and the declaration in force then disagree, and a later HTTP publish that re-sends the file applies the change with no push-time admin_only check having seen it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":429},"end":{"line":446},"content_hash":"e05bf310d1f0877791355c3f0a53adfb65344a794e0741a96dc390d6875a2da2"},"suggested_fix":"Parse a changed clax.json in the push with clax_core::manifest::parse, validate it, gate it like admin_change, and set capabilities from it (or refuse the push with invalid_manifest).","summary":"A git push that changes clax.json records the version without changing the declaration (capabilities: None)","tags":["clax-json","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/quickstart.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-26T23:48:35.999024Z","id":"041361757fa1bec481b6167f9128430a960a1d265b96390145798a01565c5c05","body":{"detail":"rule_in counts threads rows of any status, but Store::delete_thread (crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs:1977) removes the row. A person who comments and deletes the comment before a release lands (between two daemon starts, or two hosted sign-ins) gets the next release, though the stop rule is meant to hold from the person's first activity. Once an update has run while the thread existed, stopped_at is set and stays (quickstart::tests::one_thread_stops_updates_for_good).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":304},"end":{"line":338},"content_hash":"e65ec6a8f0e090581077be83b084306d13660212564343673e1f0f185bcc4b25"},"suggested_fix":"Set quickstarts.stopped_at in the thread-create transaction for an artifact that is a person's quickstart, or count the artifact's thread.create audit records in rule_in.","summary":"A thread made and deleted before the next update leaves no trace, so the quickstart is still treated as untouched","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/quickstart.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-26T23:48:36.065395Z","id":"f808e7b1b7edde928246718c8292dea13941199852fbdb2d1b187009aa475714","body":{"detail":"update_quickstart publishes the release's clax.json capabilities (clax_core::quickstart::Release::request). A capabilities change through Store::update_meta (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:325) is not a version, so rule_in still sees the quickstart as untouched and the next release puts the shipped declaration back. Title, pin and tags are kept (quickstart::tests::an_update_keeps_the_persons_title_and_pin); capabilities are not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":151},"end":{"line":219},"content_hash":"d70fb82f1dc072f9b7dbb5bf35ff577a699db7f729f69833ff96f2636327d1d4"},"summary":"An update replaces the capabilities a person set through a metadata patch without stopping updates","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/quickstart.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T00:28:49.481417Z","id":"b99492c2aefd1e586f55fce22f46d439d6f6311936156420506a6818172895de","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:d5b5cf93","references":"041361757fa1bec481b6167f9128430a960a1d265b96390145798a01565c5c05","summary":"Fixed in d5b5cf93: Store::create_thread_inner (crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs) sets quickstarts.stopped_at in the thread-create transaction for the thread's artifact. Test: quickstart::tests::a_thread_made_and_deleted_before_an_update_stops_updates_for_good (crates/clax-store/src/quickstart.rs) fails before the change at 'the thread's creation stopped updates' and passes after (bazel test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test). Proposed close for the owner.","tags":["status:proposed-close","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/quickstart.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T02:27:30.516634Z","id":"8784212026a465ec8b73ab822286f359981e07fc38ec4ca15a71ef26d3ad105d","body":{"detail":"seed_quickstart checks the person's held artifacts in one transaction (quickstart.rs:111-123) and creates the artifact and its quickstarts row in another (create_artifact_quota_async at :127). A person (or the owner) who publishes in the gap is seeded anyway. Narrow: a local core seeds at start before the router serves, and a hosted person is seeded in their own sign-in, before the first page load; moving the check into the create's closure would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":111},"end":{"line":134},"content_hash":"dc25833046674a244f49b1fa5f26ce77f83f3120c160c89543920fdf368c9cd4"},"summary":"The seed's held-artifact check and its create are not atomic","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T00:53:30.270051Z","id":"56245aa2611c35a8ad76a3fbd46c8d5fec40a3dbeea6045d2f30a1ec5e83db35","body":{"detail":"To renumber: CAPABILITY_APPROVALS_MIGRATION (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs) becomes the other branch's const + 1, or the other's becomes this one + 1; the order of the last two entries of MARKS_AFTER_APP (Mark::Table(\"capability_approvals\") and the other's mark) and of MIGRATIONS follows. Tests that name the number as a literal: migrations::tests::a_fresh_database_reaches_57 (fn name and assert_eq!(CAPABILITY_APPROVALS_MIGRATION, 57)), the MIGRATIONS[first + 15] index in the sequence test, and the comment and message in the later-numbering test (\"51 to 57 are one later now\"). Every other test names the const, crates/clax-embed/tests/old_homes.rs included; the last migration's const is what they should name.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1719},"end":{"line":1743},"content_hash":"cbd85ce4503bd5c5bac655d15a783c13f575e7796dee702364274ad4cb64ece2"},"summary":"Migration 57 (capability approvals) takes the next number after 56 (versions.capabilities_json); another branch writing a 57 means whichever lands second renumbers","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T03:35:25.209241Z","id":"673bc83f3c5501834f39f1117c7504164c2d5ba7eedaa9cc865d84d6e4d26402","body":{"detail":"Renumbered from 57 when this branch was rebased onto the quickstart's migration 57. To renumber again: CAPABILITY_APPROVALS_MIGRATION (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs) becomes the other branch's const + 1, or the other's becomes this one + 1; the order of the last entries of MARKS_AFTER_APP (Mark::Table(\"quickstarts\"), Mark::Table(\"capability_approvals\") and the other's mark, with the array length) and of MIGRATIONS follows. Tests that name the number as a literal: migrations::tests::a_fresh_database_reaches_58 (fn name and assert_eq!(CAPABILITY_APPROVALS_MIGRATION, 58)), migration_58_approves_every_declaration_in_force (its name and comment), the MIGRATIONS[first + 16] index in the sequence test, and the comment and message in the later-numbering test (\"51 to 58 after it are one later now\"). crates/clax-store/src/capability_approvals.rs's module doc and docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding-design.md section 7 name the number too. Every other test names the const, crates/clax-embed/tests/old_homes.rs included; the last migration's const is what they should name.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1735},"end":{"line":1760},"content_hash":"9c57d992a2c283457c2e96b8fafdf5da9724bc9948bd23fb3c5431fce212746d"},"summary":"Migration 58 (capability approvals) follows the quickstart's 57 (quickstarts); another branch writing a 58 means whichever lands second renumbers","supersedes":"56245aa2611c35a8ad76a3fbd46c8d5fec40a3dbeea6045d2f30a1ec5e83db35","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/quickstart.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T03:35:25.288317Z","id":"f068873c53ff1afe4633ef9c0d0960ad285bce7c118b55f43541e03ad1c7f949","body":{"detail":"approve_as_clax records each seeded or updated quickstart version's whole declaration as approved by `clax` (crates/clax-store/src/capability_approvals.rs record_in), so no Permissions bar asks about it. Accepted because Clax ships the release (web/quickstart/clax.json declares only db and user, neither gated) and the approval grants nothing: a net host or sample would still wait for the owner's answer on first use. If a release ever declares net, sample, account or another GATED name (crates/clax-core/src/capabilities.rs), its declaration is in force for every seeded person with no review of that change.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":297},"end":{"line":306},"content_hash":"3d5d6d7d63e35fff2528d0e372aed0fefdbdbe735485f7e6e21beca12e69e80b"},"summary":"A quickstart release that declares a gated name is in force without the owner approving its declaration","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/quickstart.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T03:36:59.455976Z","id":"04bec2fe73f042ab658cb87037aa381a2f824afbd940b4499c868a78780f54b0","body":{"detail":"seed_quickstart checks the person's held artifacts in one transaction (quickstart.rs:111-123) and creates the artifact and its quickstarts row in another (create_artifact_quota_async at :127). A person (or the owner) who publishes in the gap is seeded anyway. Narrow: a local core seeds at start before the router serves, and a hosted person is seeded in their own sign-in, before the first page load; moving the check into the create's closure would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":112},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"dc25833046674a244f49b1fa5f26ce77f83f3120c160c89543920fdf368c9cd4"},"summary":"The seed's held-artifact check and its create are not atomic","supersedes":"8784212026a465ec8b73ab822286f359981e07fc38ec4ca15a71ef26d3ad105d","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/quickstart.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T06:04:21.778969Z","id":"8b84214b87480ea6730cf32477b64cbc3933ef6ebac22cb9be94125e4662899a","body":{"detail":"approve_as_clax records each seeded or updated quickstart version's whole declaration as approved by `clax` (crates/clax-store/src/capability_approvals.rs record_in), so no Permissions bar asks about it. web/quickstart/clax.json declares db and user, and shell, which is in GATED (crates/clax-core/src/capabilities.rs): in a new gallery the quickstart points at Clax's own controls without the owner having approved `shell`. Accepted because Clax ships the release and the approval grants nothing: a net host or sample a release declared would still wait for the owner's answer on first use. A withdrawal or an approval by a person stops updates for good (crates/clax-store/src/capability_approvals.rs approve_capabilities and withdraw_capability call quickstart::stop_in), so a release never re-approves a name the owner withdrew. A release that adds another gated name is in force for every untouched quickstart with no review of that change.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":301},"end":{"line":311},"content_hash":"b60bf867abe94d0b058e058e5ee4dce46b1379e3c11b770c565218adf5e765ff"},"summary":"A seeded or updated quickstart's gated names, shell among them, are in force without the owner reviewing its declaration","supersedes":"f068873c53ff1afe4633ef9c0d0960ad285bce7c118b55f43541e03ad1c7f949","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/quickstart.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:52:22.667952Z","id":"b2bd058cdc1a4ea63e372e08e42e994e5455631570c68141baa2e668a39f1fd5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4647e4ba5","summary":"Fixed: Store::update_meta (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs) now calls quickstart::stop_in in its transaction when a patch changes the declaration, so the next release finds updates stopped and does not put the shipped declaration back. Test quickstart::tests::a_patch_that_changes_the_declaration_stops_updates passes in bazel test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test (PASSED in 268.0s, just test-affected main).","supersedes":"f808e7b1b7edde928246718c8292dea13941199852fbdb2d1b187009aa475714","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/queues.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:47.603574Z","id":"7a2bf2e12f9d973966ce580c9549763e1036de916d9597f75cc541e9553ceb46","body":{"detail":"Store::check_lease answers Ok when no session holds a live lease on the report and sid never held an unreleased one, so a triage agent may reply, resolve or set metadata without claiming first. Whether queue writes require a live lease is for the triage routes (crates/clax-server/src/routes/queue_agent.rs) to decide; this function alone does not enforce it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1185},"end":{"line":1195},"content_hash":"a4a9002d20e3e92a93f12476f8492f881c4e883052037e7be6b94498bb276330"},"summary":"check_lease admits a write from a session that never claimed the report","tags":["queues","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/queues.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:47.603746Z","id":"6c21984989b313668d766c6e087fe09280e89d34b89bcf7c0222584d62ceac30","body":{"detail":"file_report_async calls ensure_external_async with q.person, so artifacts.person is the queue maker's public ID (None for the owner). A triage member who is not the maker has no right on that artifact outside the queue's routes; hosted reach of /a/<id> for queue members is unresolved. The anchor's route is also dropped (anchor.route = None) and its file forced to index.html, since an external artifact has one placeholder file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":874},"end":{"line":930},"content_hash":"df2e1219cced59fd16a30d0142fbc27ed1a108d1deb0621b13d63e202113f4b8"},"summary":"An external report's artifact belongs to the queue's maker, so other members reach it only through the queue","tags":["queues","hosted","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/queues.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:19:15.333954Z","id":"e1c959869bbd333637cdc498a486e14d9465f6713c9c8f46e6ec0c680ad3e120","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-27-clax-sdk-design.md §7.4 says every write a claimant makes carries the lease's fence, and a write with an older fence is 409 lease_lost. check_lease_in instead compares the writing session with the thread's current lease (largest fence): a session that held a superseded or expired lease gets lease_lost, one that never claimed or released gets claim_required. The triage routes (crates/clax-server/src/routes/queue_agent.rs) and the queue tools send no fence. Equivalent while one session never holds two leases on one report at once, which queue_claims' (thread_id, session_id) key guarantees; a fence would matter only for a client that shares one session across workers.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":300},"end":{"line":316},"content_hash":"934c6439a83c2b7225350ab84739a4b19df472897e0b5c439aa258bf15ed6bd2"},"summary":"Writes under a lease are checked by the writing session, not by the fence the claim returned","tags":["queues","revisit:a client shares one session across several workers, or the SDK's agent helper sends fences","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/queues.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:19:15.334607Z","id":"c816d2721e350336000b75d15bacf0d18a57b2a2eb7e4d2ca26b3577ee12e60d","body":{"detail":"check_lease_in now answers CoreError::ClaimRequired (409 claim_required, crates/clax-http/src/error.rs) when no session holds a live lease and the session never claimed the report or released its claim; lease_lost and thread_taken are as before. Store::report_reply, Store::resolve_report, Store::set_thread_metadata_as and Store::set_report_artifact_metadata check it inside the write's transaction for an agent and not for a person (ReportWriter::Person): a triage member in a browser replies and resolves without a claim. The triage routes (crates/clax-server/src/routes/queue_agent.rs) use them; tests: queues::tests::an_agent_writes_only_under_its_own_lease_and_a_person_needs_none and api_queue_agent::an_agent_that_never_claimed_or_released_is_claim_required, api_queue_agent::a_person_replies_and_resolves_without_a_claim. This thread can be closed.","kind":"comment","references":"7a2bf2e12f9d973966ce580c9549763e1036de916d9597f75cc541e9553ceb46","summary":"Implemented in a6c1560d0: an agent's reply, resolve or metadata write on a report needs its session's live lease","tags":["queues","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/threads.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T02:05:01.054404Z","id":"5c28730d55293369d03f4691439752af16900725ac9c7a7fcc734303390f6894","body":{"detail":"list_threads_sql and threads_of_many_sql add `t.queue_id IS NULL`, and crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs thread_of answers 409 queue_report (commit 0c4e340d2). Other queries over `threads` (crates/clax-store/src/attention.rs open-thread counts, crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs reply items made by an agent's queue_reply, approvals scopes, crates/clax-server/src/routes/live.rs) were not audited for queue threads; a gallery count may include an external artifact's reports.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":463},"end":{"line":471},"content_hash":"1fb34d3818a068155b104a30a841e2422a4f3fbafeb5fe0615d18c4620d710ba"},"suggested_fix":"Audit each `FROM threads`/`JOIN threads` query and decide per reader whether a report belongs, adding `queue_id IS NULL` where it does not.","summary":"Only the thread listings and the one-thread routes leave reports out: attention counts, inbox items and other readers of threads still see a queue's reports","tags":["session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T02:05:01.054773Z","id":"5f9d4edc54faab504b6b0375897a9bdea728d7c575556b8b2c4bae8f8e5431a0","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/src/plans.rs plans the hot reads; the report listing's SQL is built inline in Store::reports (crates/clax-store/src/queues.rs) and is not among them, so nothing shows the planner uses the new index.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1775},"end":{"line":1776},"content_hash":"5b93962d0021d54b88fd6e9aa7cfcc00247cfeb26fe6e400fa141dd3bf93cddc"},"suggested_fix":"Expose the listing SQL as a const and add it to plans.rs with the index expected.","summary":"No query-plan check pins threads_by_queue_reporter to a reporter's report listing under reporters_see own","tags":["session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:17:45.840814Z","id":"cc2f4e6b4bc61a173ad5e4ee7a1c357adc0d47094526e2a77b1bc8d4f03bc36e","body":{"detail":"Those tables name a viewer row (viewer_id NOT NULL), and a claim (Store::claim_for_owner, Claim::Adopted) can make another row the owner's and fold the old one away, so a session opened for the CLI's owner row would name a row the claim deletes. Their lifetimes (SESSION_TTL_SECS 30 days, SIGNIN_TTL_SECS 10 minutes) and a spent code's answer (NotFound) differ from the local login's (400 days, 120 s, 410) too. login_codes and owner_browser_sessions name no row: a session is the owner's whatever row the owner is.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1846},"end":{"line":1863},"content_hash":"510833bc7a44bc1cf3be22ad9865663b99a17a1e21df28c174551a34664112bc"},"summary":"Keep a local daemon's owner browser sessions and login codes in hosted mode's browser_sessions and signin_links (migration 27)","tags":["design","local-trust","revisit:a local daemon signs people's browsers in, or hosted and local sign-in merge","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/confirmations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T03:34:46.863379Z","id":"f5583fe593fdbe4036da109ff6849ca7204755491b0a30e6d743e484b51130f2","body":{"detail":"agent_session_live selects any session with ended_at IS NULL, so a grant's session (sessions.grant_id set: an agent of another machine, which never holds the token) makes every listed token decision of the owner's wait for a browser confirmation too. Counting only sessions with grant_id IS NULL would match the threat (an agent running as the owner's OS user); the code follows the wording 'while any agent session is live' instead.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"c4984cb621f9ad68959b466209f1d253d0b510b60c3fc12ea6e41941c8308e6b"},"summary":"Any live session counts, a connected person's remote agent's included, though only an agent on this machine can read the daemon token","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
